hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4201","Another [report]. 342 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar - in Nishapur - informed us, that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz Abu Shuayb al-Adani narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every tie and lineage is cut off except my tie and lineage."
"4202","343 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Isa ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Adani narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every tie and lineage is cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and progeny."
"4203","Another [report]. 344 - And with the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day the sun eclipsed, and I did not hear recitation from him."
"4204","Another [report]. 345 - And with the same chain, Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Adani narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah who said: Ibn Abbas said: I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr, nor did he command us; and he conveyed."
"4205","Another [report]. 346 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Muslim al-Jundi narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah sent Muhammad to the red and the black, and said: O people, I am the Messenger of Allah to you all. It has a witness in the two Sahihs, from the narration of Yazid ibn Suhayb al-Faqir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah."
"4206","Another: 347 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Adib informed us, Abu 'Amr ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yahya narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from 'Ikrimah who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: None of His creation was secure except Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: {That Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins} to the end of the verse, and He said to the angels: {And whoever of them says: I am a god besides Him, him We shall requite with Hell}."
"4207","348 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yahya al-'Adani narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from 'Ikrimah who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: None of His creation is secure except Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: {That Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins}, because He said to the angels: {And whoever of them says: I am a god besides Him, him We shall requite with Hell}."
"4208","349 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, preferred Muhammad over the people of heaven and the people of earth. A man said to him: O Abu 'Abbas, what is his superiority over the people of heaven? He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says to the people of heaven: {And whoever of them says: I am a god besides Him, him We shall requite with Hell, thus We requite the wrongdoers}, and Allah, mighty and majestic, said to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins} to the end of the verse. It was said: O Abu 'Abbas, what is his superiority over the prophets? He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: {And We sent no messenger except in the tongue of his people}, and Allah, mighty and majestic, said to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {And We sent you not except to all mankind as a bringer of glad tidings and a warner}, so Allah sent him to men and jinn. Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah: we brought him as a witness."
"4209","Another: 350 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi there informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the Friday sermon when he recited a verse; a man beside 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: When was this verse revealed, for I have not heard it except now? 'Abdullah said: Glory be to Allah. The man fell silent, then he recited another verse, and the man said the same to 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, so 'Abdullah said: Glory be to Allah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, Ibn Mas'ud said to the man: You did not attend the Friday prayer with us. He said: Glory be to Allah! The man went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibn Umm 'Abd spoke the truth, Ibn Umm 'Abd spoke the truth. Thus Ibn Khuzaymah reported it in his Sahih."
"4210","Another: 351 - And with it Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, al-Hakam, meaning Ibn Aban, narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Zib'ara came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, you claim that Allah revealed to you this verse: {Indeed you and what you worship besides Allah are fuel for Hell, you will enter it}. Ibn al-Zib'ara said: The sun, the moon, the angels, 'Uzayr, and 'Isa son of Maryam have been worshipped; will all of these be in the Fire with our gods?! Then was revealed: {And when the son of Maryam is presented as an example, at once your people cry out, and they say: Are our gods better or is he? They did not present it to you except for argument; rather they are a contentious people}. Then was revealed: {Indeed those for whom the best reward has preceded from Us, they will be kept far from it}."
"4211","Khalid ibn Mihran al-Hadhdha from 'Ikrimah: 352 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, reading to him, the two shaykhs Abu al-Husayn Ibn al-Naqur and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati informed us, they said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-'Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us, 'Abdullah, he is al-Baghawi, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing is with your elders."
"4212","353 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given drink he said: Begin with the elders, or: with the eldest. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated 'Blessing is with your elders' from 'Abdullah ibn Salm, from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, from Khalid, and he said: Ibn al-Mubarak did not narrate it in Khurasan, he narrated it only at Darb al-Rum so the Syrians heard it from him."
"4213","Another: 354 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"4214","Another: 355 - Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to me, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Snakes are the transformed ones of the jinn, just as monkeys and pigs were transformed from Banu Isra'il. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa, from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar."
"4215","Another: 356 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr in Isfahan informed us, that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah Sammuyah informed us, Muslim, he is Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with him in a blanket and then menstruated and slipped away, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Have you menstruated? She said: Yes. He said to her: Wrap your waist, then return to your bed. Something like it has preceded in the narration of al-Hakam ibn Aban."
"4216","Another: 357 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad, he is al-Dawraqi, narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever imagines in his prayer that he has passed wind should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell. Something like it has preceded in the biography of Thawr ibn Zayd from 'Ikrimah."
"4217","Another: 358 - And with it 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Bishr narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj on foot. He said: Let her ride, for Allah, mighty and majestic, is free of need of her walking. In the two Sahihs from the narration of 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, he said: My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah, so she ordered me to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a verdict, and he said: Let her walk and let her ride."
"4218","Another: 359 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jallalah animal, the mujaththamah, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Khalid. Drinking from the mouth of the waterskin: al-Bukhari narrated it from Musaddad, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Khalid; our intent here is only the jallalah."
"4219","Another: 360 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ghiyath ibn Muhammad ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Nu'man narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Allah sent Muhammad to make him prevail over all religion, so our religion is above all creeds, and our men are above their women, and their men are not above our women. Al-Daraqutni said: Al-Nu'man ibn 'Abd al-Salam is alone in narrating it from al-Thawri."
"4220","Another: 361 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah in Isfahan informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mihran al-Muqri informed us, al-Sarraj, he is Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Qasabi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Safiyyah menstruated after the visit circumambulation, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to depart. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her."
"4221","Dawud ibn al-Husayn al-Qurashi, freedman of 'Amr ibn 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, from 'Ikrimah: 362 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Zaynab his daughter to her husband Abu al-'As ibn al-Rabi' upon the first marriage, and did not introduce anything new."
"4222","363 - And with it my father narrated to me, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter Zaynab to Abu al-'As ibn al-Rabi', her Islam having preceded his Islam by six years, upon the first marriage, and did not introduce a new testimony nor a new dower."
"4223","364 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter to Abu al-'As, two years later, upon her first marriage."
"4224","365 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Shu'ayb 'Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Zaynab to Abu al-'As upon the first marriage, and did not introduce anything new. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Ibn Ishaq, similarly, and said: There is no harm in its chain, and perhaps this came from Dawud ibn Husayn due to his memory. He said: And I heard 'Abd ibn Humayd say: I heard Yazid ibn Harun mention from Ibn Ishaq this hadith, and the hadith of al-Hajjaj from 'Amr from his father from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter to Abu al-'As with a new marriage. Yazid said: The hadith of Ibn 'Abbas has the better chain. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Khallad and Yahya ibn Hakim, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Ibn Ishaq."
"4225","Another: 366 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, he is Ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani, narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning this verse: {If they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them; if you turn away from them they cannot harm you at all, and if you judge, judge between them with justice; indeed Allah loves the just}. He said: When Banu al-Nadir killed a slain person from Banu Qurayzah they paid them half the blood-money, and when Banu Qurayzah killed a slain person from Banu al-Nadir they paid them the full blood-money, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the blood-money between them equal and full."
"4226","367 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: {If they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them; if you turn away from them they cannot harm you at all, and if you judge, judge between them with justice; indeed Allah loves the just}. He said: When Banu al-Nadir killed a slain person from Banu Qurayzah they paid them half the blood-money, and when Banu Qurayzah killed a slain person from Banu al-Nadir they paid them the full blood-money, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the blood-money between them equal."
"4227","368 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The verses in al-Ma'idah: {Judge between them with justice; indeed Allah loves the just} were revealed only concerning blood-money regarding Banu Qurayzah and Banu al-Nadir; the slain of Banu al-Nadir had nobility, so full blood-money was paid, while Qurayzah used to pay half the blood-money, so they sought judgment from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and Allah revealed that concerning them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held them to the truth in that and made the blood-money equal. Abu Dawud narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, similarly."
"4228","Another: 369 - Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghana'im al-Wa'iz, between Cairo and Egypt, informed us, that Abu Sabir 'Abd al-Sabur al-Harawi informed them, Mahmud ibn al-Qasim al-Azdi informed us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub informed us, Abu 'Isa Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tirmidhi informed us, Yahya ibn Musa narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Qurashi, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he was asked about tayammum, and he said: Allah, exalted, said in His Book when He mentioned ablution: {Wash your faces and your hands up to the elbows}, and He said concerning tayammum: {Wipe your faces and your hands}, and He said: {As for the thief, male and female, cut off their hands}. So the Sunnah regarding cutting is the two palms; tayammum is only the face and the two palms. Thus al-Tirmidhi narrated it in his book."
"4229","Another: 370 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr, he is Ibn Harb, narrated to us. 371 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, they both said: Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which religions are most beloved to Allah? He said: The easy upright religion."
"4230","372 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which religions are most beloved to Allah? He said: The easy upright religion."
"4231","Another: 373 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Hilali narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Rukanah ibn 'Abd Yazid, brother of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, divorced three times in one sitting, and grieved over her intensely, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How many times did you divorce her, O Rukanah? He said: Three times in one sitting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it is one."
"4232","374 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Rukanah ibn 'Abd Yazid, brother of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, divorced his wife three times in one sitting, and grieved over her intensely. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him: How did you divorce her? He said: I divorced her three times. He said: So he said: In one sitting? He said: Yes. He said: Then that is only one, so take her back if you wish. He said: So he took her back. Ibn 'Abbas used to hold that divorce is only at each period of purity."
"4233","Another: 375 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi, by authorization, informed us, that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umarah al-Ansari, known as al-Qaddah, I heard from him in Baghdad, narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Our arrival to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was five years after the Hijrah; we set out attaching ourselves to Quraysh in the year of the Confederates, I being with my brother al-Fadl, and with us our servant Abu Rafi', until we reached al-'Arj, then we turned off his riding road and took that road via al-Jathjathah until we emerged at Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, then we entered Madinah and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Trench, I being then eight years old and my brother thirteen years old. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn al-Husayn except his son Sulayman; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umarah is alone in it."
"4234","Dawud ibn Abi Hind al-Qushayri, their freedman, Abu Muhammad al-Basri, and the name of Abu Hind is Dinar, from 'Ikrimah: 376 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah 'A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abu al-'Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali ibn 'Asim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Muhammad Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi 'Umar al-'Adani informed us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrating, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to such-and-such place and does such-and-such, then he shall have such-and-such. He said: So the youths hastened to it while the elders remained firm under the banners; when Allah granted victory, the youths came seeking what Allah had assigned them, so the elders said: Do not take it to our exclusion, for we were a support for you. Then Allah, exalted, revealed: {So fear Allah and set right your relations}. Abu Dawud narrated it from Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, from Khalid, from Dawud, and from Ziyad ibn Ayyub, from Hushaym, from Dawud, the first being more complete, and from Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal, from Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Mawhab al-Hamdani, from Yahya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Dawud, in it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from al-Haytham ibn Ayyub al-Talqani, from al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la, from Mu'tamir. Ibn 'Adi said: Thus Dawud reported it in mursal form from 'Ikrimah."
"4235","Another: 377 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I myself heard from him, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Abu Jahl passed by and said: Did I not forbid you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked him, and Abu Jahl said to him: Why do you rebuke me, O Muhammad? By Allah, you know there is no man here with a greater assembly than me. He said: Then Jibril said: {Then let him call his assembly}. He said: So Ibn 'Abbas said: By Allah, had he called his assembly, the tormenting guards would have seized him."
"4236","378 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, while he was present, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us. 379 - Ibn Mardawayh said: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, all together, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at the Maqam, and Abu Jahl said: O Muhammad, did I not forbid you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke harshly to him, and he said: By Allah, you know that I am the noblest of the people of this valley in assembly. So Allah revealed: {Then let him call his assembly}. Ibn 'Abbas said: Had he called his assembly, the tormenting guards would have seized him at once."
"4237","380 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us, Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn al-'Abbas al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us, Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris informed us, Suwayd, he is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at the Maqam, and Abu Jahl passed by him and said: O Muhammad, did I not forbid you from this? And he threatened him, so he spoke harshly and rebuked him. He said: O Muhammad, with what do you threaten me? By Allah, I am the greatest of the valley people in assembly. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {Then let him call his assembly; We shall call the guards}. So Ibn 'Abbas said: Had he called his assembly, the tormenting guards would have seized him at once. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from 'Affan, from Wahb, from Dawud. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj, from Abu Khalid al-Ahmar."
"4238","Another: 381 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Quraysh said to the Jews: Give us something to ask this man about. They said: Ask him about the soul. So they asked him, and there was revealed: {And they ask you about the soul} up to: {little}. They said: Were we not given of knowledge except little, while we were given the Torah, and whoever is given the Torah has been given much good? Then was revealed: {Say: If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord} to the end of the verse."
"4239","382 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Quraysh said to the Jews: Give us something to ask this man about. They said: Ask him about the soul. So they asked him, and there was revealed: {And they ask you about the soul; say: The soul is of the affair of my Lord} to the end of the verse. They said: We were given abundant knowledge; we were given the Torah, and whoever is given the Torah has been given much good. He said: So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {Say: If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord, the sea would be exhausted}. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from this angle."
"4240","Another: 383 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us. 384 - Ibn Mardawayh said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Hamadhani narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, all together, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man of the Ansar apostatized and joined Makkah, then regretted and sent to his people: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me whether I have repentance? So Allah revealed: {How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their belief and bore witness that the Messenger is true}. So they wrote it to him, and he returned and accepted Islam."
"4241","385 - Abu 'Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid informed us, 'Ubaydullah informed us, my grandfather Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, 'Ali, he is Ibn 'Asim, narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a man of the Ansar apostatized from Islam and joined the polytheists, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their belief} to the end of the verse. So his people sent it to him, and he returned repentant, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted that from him and let him go. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Ali ibn 'Asim. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi', from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Dawud. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from 'Umar ibn Muhammad al-Buhayri, from Bishr ibn Mu'adh, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Dawud. 'Ali ibn 'Asim: we reported him for consideration."
"4242","Another: 386 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Maslamah ibn 'Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Qur'an came down in the month of Ramadan on the Night of Decree to this lowest heaven all at once, and Allah would newly reveal to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whatever He willed, and the polytheists would bring no example to dispute with except that Allah brought its answer, and that is His saying, blessed and exalted: {And they bring you no example except that We bring you the truth}."
"4243","387 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind said, we heard him narrating from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down the Qur'an all at once from the Preserved Tablet to the heaven of this world, then Jibril later brought it down upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); in it was what the polytheists said and its refutation."
"4244","388 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us, that Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim al-Razi informed them, reading to him in Damascus, he said: Abu al-Faraj, he is Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini, informed us, Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zakariyya al-Naysaburi informed us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i informed us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Qur'an came down in Ramadan on the Night of Decree, and it was in the lowest heaven, and whenever Allah, mighty and majestic, willed to introduce something new, it came down; between its beginning and its end were twenty years. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it. And he narrated it from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Dawud ibn Abi Hind."
"4245","Another: 389 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja ibn al-Fadl al-Hanbali informed us, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When Ka'b ibn al-Ashraf came to Makkah, Quraysh said to him: Are you the scholar of the people of Madinah and their chief? He said: Yes. They said: Do you not see this cut-off one severed from his people, who claims he is better than us, while we are the people of the pilgrimage rites, the keepers of the covering, and the providers of drink? He said: You are better than him. And there was revealed: {Have you not seen those who were given a portion of the Book; they believe in jibt and taghut and say to those who disbelieved: These are better guided} up to His saying: {a helper}."
"4246","390 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Jarbadhqani in Isfahan informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, while he was present, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, with his chain similarly, and in it: Do you not see this Sabian, and in it: Then was revealed: {Indeed your enemy is the one cut off}, and was revealed: {Have you not seen those who were given a portion of the Book} up to His saying: {Then you will find for him no helper}. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Abi 'Adi, similarly. And in it: {Indeed your enemy is the one cut off}. And with him: al-Sunaybir."
"4247","Another: 391 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Salih ibn Ahmad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: {And it is forbidden for a town which We destroyed}."
"4248","392 - And with it Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Yahya narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite: {And it is forbidden for a town which We destroyed}. He said: I said: What is hurm? He said: It is incumbent upon a town that they shall not return, as He said: {Did they not see how many generations We destroyed before them, that they do not return to them}, and as He said to Nuh: {None of your people will believe except those who have already believed}."
"4249","393 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn al-'Abbas al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us, Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shami al-Sarakhsi informed us, Suwayd, he is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, 'Ali, he is Ibn Mushir, narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to recite: And it is forbidden for a town which We destroyed that they shall not return. So I said to him: What is hurm? He said: It is incumbent upon a town which We destroyed that they shall not return, as Allah, exalted, said: {Did they not see how many generations We destroyed before them, that they do not return to them}, and as He said to Nuh: {None of your people will believe except those who have already believed, so do not grieve over what they used to do}."
"4250","Another: 394 - Abu Isma'il Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Mashadhah informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Khalaf al-Harbi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah al-Sulami informed us, Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la informed us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married the sister of al-Ash'ath ibn Qays and died before giving her a choice, so Allah, mighty and majestic, absolved her from him."
"4251","395 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Yahya ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn al-Fadl al-Makhbari informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nayruz al-Anmati informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Qutaylah, sister of al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, and died before giving her a choice, so Allah absolved her from him."
"4252","Another: 396 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn al-'Abbas al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us, Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris al-Sami al-Sarakhsi informed us, Suwayd, he is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, 'Ali, he is Ibn Mushir, narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The one of the sacrifice is Ishaq: {And We gave him glad tidings of Ishaq, a prophet among the righteous}. He said: He was given glad tidings of him when he was born, and given glad tidings of his prophethood after childhood."
"4253","Another: 397 - And with it from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When a woman gives birth after nine months, two complete years of nursing suffice him, because Allah said: {And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months}."
"4254","Another: 398 - And with it from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning Allah's saying: {They recite it as it ought to be recited}. He said: They follow it as it ought to be followed. Then he recited: {By the sun and its brightness, and the moon when it follows it}, meaning when it follows it. And he said: Causing harm in a bequest is among the major sins. Then he recited: {These are the limits of Allah, and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger} until he reached: {And for him is a humiliating punishment}."
"4255","399 - Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Hamzah ibn 'Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi in Cairo informed us, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: Causing harm in a bequest is among the major sins. Then he recited: {Without causing harm, a bequest from Allah; and Allah is Knowing, Forbearing}."
"4256","400 - Abu Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Firas informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Daybuli narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan, he is Ibn 'Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Deviation or injustice in a bequest is among the major sins. Al-Nasa'i narrated similarly: Causing harm in a bequest is among the major sins, from 'Ali ibn Hujr, from 'Ali ibn Mushir, similarly."
"4257","Al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit al-Basri from 'Ikrimah: 401 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to me, my father informed us, from Harun ibn Musa, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The food of two rivals showing off was forbidden. Abu Dawud narrated it, and with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the food of two rivals showing off, from Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa, from his father, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from al-Zubayr. And he said: Most of those who narrated it from Jarir do not mention Ibn 'Abbas in it, while Harun al-Nahwi mentioned Ibn 'Abbas in it, and Hammad ibn Zayd did not mention Ibn 'Abbas."
"4258","Another: 402 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah who said: {It is not for a prophet to embezzle}, he says: That his companions suspect him."
"4259","403 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja al-Abhani informed us, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: {It is not for a prophet to embezzle}. He said: It is not for his companions to think ill of him."
"4260","404 - And with it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: {It is not for a prophet to embezzle}: That his companions suspect him."
"4261","Another: 405 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hakam narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit and Ya'la ibn Hakim, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a sheep came running in front of him, so he raced it until he pressed his belly against the wall."
"4262","406 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi there informed us, that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them, 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us, Ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim and al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and a sheep passed in front of him, so he hastened toward the qiblah until he pressed his belly against the qiblah. 'Amr ibn Hakam: we reported him for consideration."
"4263","Zayd al-Hajjam Abu Usamah al-Kufi, freedman of Banu Thawr, from 'Ikrimah: 407 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zayd Abu Usamah narrated to us, 'Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men, masculine women, the tattooer and the one tattooed, the joiner of hair and the one for whom it is joined. Our intent here is only the end of the hadith, his saying: and the tattooer, to its end, for its beginning has been mentioned in al-Bukhari from the narration of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from 'Ikrimah. Zayd al-Hajjam: Yahya ibn Ma'in and Abu Hatim al-Razi deemed him trustworthy. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from 'A'ishah, and from the narration of her sister Asma, and it has been narrated in the Sahih by other paths."
"4264","Sa'id ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah al-Thaqafi al-Basri from 'Ikrimah: 408 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn 'Amr ibn Miskin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a group came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), bringing with them a woman, and said: O Muhammad, what was revealed to you concerning adultery? He said: Go and bring me two men of the scholars of Banu Isra'il. So they brought him two men: one a young eloquent man, the other an old man whose eyebrows had fallen over his eyes so that he lifted them with a band. He said: I adjure you by Allah to inform us of what Allah revealed to Musa concerning the adulterer. They said: You have adjured us by a mighty thing, and we inform you that Allah revealed to Musa concerning the adulterer stoning, and we were a youthful people, our women had beautiful faces, and that became widespread among us, and we did not uphold it, so we turned to flogging and public disgrace. He said: Take your woman away; when she delivers what is in her womb, then stone her. Sa'id ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Jubayr al-Thaqafi: Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Yahya ibn Ma'in, and Abu Zur'ah al-Razi deemed him trustworthy. Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari Abu Sufyan al-Basri: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: His position is truthfulness. Al-Daraqutni said: Sa'id al-Jahdari is alone in narrating it from Sa'id."
"4265","Salamah ibn Wahram al-Yamani from 'Ikrimah: 409 - Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Samad al-Sulami informed us, that 'Abd al-Awwal ibn 'Isa informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, 'Isa ibn 'Umar ibn al-'Abbas informed us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid informed us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Some Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat waiting for him, and he came out; when he drew near them he heard them conversing, and listened to their talk; one of them was saying: How amazing, Allah took from His creation a close friend, for Ibrahim is His close friend. Another said: What is more amazing than that Allah spoke to Musa directly. Another said: 'Isa is Allah's word and spirit. Another said: And Adam, Allah chose him. So he came out to them, greeted them, and said: I heard your talk and your amazement. Ibrahim is Allah's close friend, and so he is; Musa is His confidant, and so he is; 'Isa is His spirit and His word, and so he is; Adam, Allah chose him, and so he is. Behold, I am Allah's beloved, and no boast; I am the bearer of the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection, under it Adam and those below him, and no boast; I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast; I am the first to move the rings of Paradise, and no boast; Allah will open for me and admit me into it, and with me the poor of the believers, and no boast; I am the noblest of the first and the last before Allah, and no boast. Thus Imam 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi reported it in his book. Imam Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub al-Juzajani narrated it from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from 'Ali ibn Nasr ibn 'Ali, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid, and said: A gharib hadith."
"4266","Another: 410 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Hisham, he is Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rifa'i, narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out carrying al-Hasan on his shoulder, and a man said to him: O boy, what an excellent mount you have ridden. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what an excellent rider he is. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi, and said: A gharib hadith we know only from this angle. Zam'ah was weakened by some scholars due to his memory."
"4267","Another: 411 - And with it Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the muhallil and the one for whom it is done, the tattooer and the one tattooed, the briber and the bribed, the plucker of eyebrows and the one plucked, the joiner of hair and the one joined, the slanderer and the one who seeks it. Ibn Majah narrated from it the mention of the muhallil and the one for whom it is done, from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi."
"4268","Another: 412 - And with it from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bending the mouths of waterskins to drink. Then a man went to a waterskin after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it and bent it, and a snake came out of it."
"4269","413 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zam'ah, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bending the mouths of waterskins. He said: And a man, after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, came at night to a waterskin and bent it, and a snake came out upon him from it. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi."
"4270","Another: 414 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the valley of 'Usfan during Hajj he said: O Abu Bakr, which valley is this? He said: The valley of 'Usfan. He said: Hud and Salih passed through it upon red young camels, their halters of palm fiber, their waist-wrappers of woolen cloaks, their cloaks of striped Yemeni garments, reciting talbiyah, performing Hajj to the Ancient House."
"4271","415 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj, he passed by the valley of 'Usfan during Hajj and said: O Abu Bakr, which valley is this? He said: The valley of 'Usfan. He said: Hud and Salih passed through it upon red young camels, their halters of palm fiber, their waist-wrappers of woolen cloaks, their cloaks of striped garments, reciting talbiyah, performing Hajj to the Ancient House."
"4272","Another: 416 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi there informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us, Abu Tahir, he is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, my grandfather's son, informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us. 417 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah informed us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat. Nasr said in his hadith: He said: Ibn 'Abbas prayed upon a mat, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat. Abu Bakr, meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq, said: I have some doubt in my heart about Zam'ah ibn Salih."
"4273","418 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us. 419 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"4274","420 - And with it my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Abbas, and Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"4275","421 - Imam Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi and others informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"4276","422 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and 'A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Yahya ibn Abi 'Umar al-'Adani narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar and Salamah ibn Wahram, one of them said: from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"4277","Another: 423 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zam'ah, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Seek help with the pre-dawn meal for the fast of the day, and with the midday nap for the night prayer. Ibn Majah reported it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu 'Amir. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from Yahya ibn Ma'in, from Abu Dawud, from Zam'ah."
"4278","Another: 424 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Night of Decree: A mild night, serene, neither hot nor cold, its sun on its morning appears weak and red."
"4279","425 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Night of Decree is a serene night, neither hot nor cold; the sun on its day rises red and weak."
"4280","Another: 426 - And with it Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who practices sorcery or has it done for him, who takes omens or has them taken for him, who practices soothsaying or has it done for him."
"4281","Another: 427 - And with it from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best in character, gentle in manner, and the worst of you are the chatterers, the pompous in speech, the arrogant."
"4282","Another: 428 - And from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not come to women at night. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approached returning from a journey, alighted at a stop, and two men raced to their homes, and each found with his wife a man."
"4283","Another: 429 - And with it from Ibn 'Abbas: {Except that Allah comes to them in canopies of cloud}. He said: Canopies of cloud cut into layers."
"4284","Another: 430 - And with it Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, from Zam'ah ibn Salih, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling on one of his journeys, he heard a camel-driver chanting ahead of him, so he said to his Companions: Bring your mounts forward to be ahead of this driver. He said: So they urged their mounts until they caught up with them and greeted them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of which people are you? He said: Of Mudar. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the most of Mudar. They said: And who are you? He said: Then one of the people said: This is the Messenger of Allah. So they said: Welcome, you are dearer to us than our father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, you are indeed of Mudar. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We wanted to place our mounts ahead of this driver of yours. He said: They said: Yes, gladly. Shall we not tell you how chanting began? He said: Yes indeed. They said: So-and-so son of so-and-so, a man of the pre-Islamic age, used to rob people; one night he set out with a boy until they raided a people whose camels were resting in their courtyard, so they loosed their hobbles, then shouted at them. He said: Driving them well, he said to his boy: Chant for them to walk. The slave said: How shall I say? He said: Chant for them to walk. He said: By Allah, I do not know what to say. He said: So his master rose against him in anger with a stick and struck him; he shielded himself with his forearms, and the stick hit his forearms, so he began to say: O my hands, O my hands. So the camels hastened. He said: So his master said to him: Add more, may Allah make your eye weep. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until he lay back upon his mount."
"4285","Another: 431 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh in Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise last night and looked in it, and behold Ja'far flying with the angels, and Hamzah reclining upon a couch."
"4286","Another: 432 - Abu 'Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi 'Ali, known as Ibn al-Khurayf, in Baghdad informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed them, Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Sakina al-Anmati informed us, Abu al-Qasim 'Ubaydullah ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Saydalani informed us, Abu Bakr 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The people of the pre-Islamic age used to stand at 'Arafah until, when the sun was over the mountain tops like turbans upon men's heads, they moved on. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the departure from 'Arafah until the sun set, then prayed Fajr at Muzdalifah when dawn broke, then moved on when everything became bright at the last time before the sun rose."
"4287","433 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The people of the pre-Islamic age used to stand at 'Arafat until, when the sun was over the mountain tops like turbans upon men's heads, they poured forth; then they stood at Muzdalifah until, when the sun was about to be over the mountain tops, they moved on. When Islam came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the departure from 'Arafat until the sun disappeared, and hastened the departure from Jam', departing from it when everything became bright at the last time, and prayed his day at dawn darkness."
"4288","434 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Zam'ah, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Jam', and when everything became bright before the sun rose, he poured forth. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the hadith of 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the polytheists would not pour forth until the sun rose over Thabir, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opposed them before sunrise."
"4289","Another: 435 - Abu al-Fadl 'Abd al-Wahid ibn 'Abd al-Salam ibn Sultan al-Bay' in Baghdad informed us, that al-Mubarak ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Shahrazuri informed them, Isma'il ibn Mas'adah ibn Isma'il al-Jurjani informed us, Hamzah ibn Yusuf al-Sahmi informed us, Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi informed us, Ibn Mukram, he is Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram, narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, and in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu Shurayh."
"4290","Another: 436 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot assume my form. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"4291","Another: 437 - And with it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is none of the children of Adam except that in his head are two chains, one in the seventh heaven and the other in the seventh earth; when the servant humbles himself, Allah raises him by the chain in heaven, and when he wishes to exalt himself, Allah lowers him."
"4292","Another: 438 - And with it Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn 'Adi informed us, al-Husayn ibn 'Abdullah al-Qattan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zam'ah, from Salamah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays two rak'ahs without self-distraction. Then he said: Which would you take, the slave or the horse? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. Zam'ah ibn Salih al-Makki: Some scholars criticized him, though Muslim narrated from him in his Sahih. Ibn 'Adi said, mentioning some of Zam'ah's hadith: He sometimes errs in some of what he narrates, and I hope there is no harm in his hadith. Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rifa'i: Muslim also narrated from him, though some criticized him."
"4293","Sulayman ibn Fayruz al-Shaybani Abu Ishaq from 'Ikrimah: 439 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed me, that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man touch another man skin to skin, nor a woman another woman."
"4294","440 - Abu Ja'far, also, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man touching another man skin to skin, and a woman another woman. Al-Bukhari narrated a hadith from Musaddad, from Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-Shaybani, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah. Muslim narrated from the narration of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father: Let no man lie with another man under one garment, nor a woman with another woman under one garment. Its end. Praise belongs to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace."
"4295","Simak ibn Harb from 'Ikrimah: 1 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, reading to her, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas. He said: One of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed in a basin; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to perform ablution from it or to wash, and she said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I was in major impurity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water does not become impure."
"4296","2 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a woman of the Prophet's wives (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from major impurity, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and performed ablution from her leftover. She said: I bathed from it. He said: Nothing makes water impure."
"4297","3 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi there informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Salih ibn Bakr al-Sulami al-Naysaburi, informed us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us. They said: Abu Ahmad, he is al-Zubayri, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us. 4 - Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah said: 'Utbah ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us. 5 - Abu Bakr said: Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed from major impurity, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution or washed from her leftover. This is the hadith of Waki'. Ahmad ibn Mani' said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution from her leftover. Abu Musa and 'Utbah ibn 'Abdullah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to perform ablution from her leftover, and she spoke to him, so he said: Nothing makes water impure."
"4298","6 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing makes water impure. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Waki', and from 'Ali ibn Ishaq, from Ibn al-Mubarak, all from Sufyan, in it: Nothing makes water impure. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Ibn al-Mubarak. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr Ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas, and from 'Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki', similarly. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we reported it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, and from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, and from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas. Our intent from this hadith is only his saying: Nothing makes water impure. As for the mention of washing, Muslim narrated from the hadith of 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: My knowledge and what occurs to my mind is that Abu al-Sha'tha, he is Jabir ibn Zayd, informed me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with the leftover of Maymunah."
"4299","Another: 7 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad in Herat informed us, that Zahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Ghazi al-Harras informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather, meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-'Ijli narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I sighted the crescent tonight. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? He said: Yes. He said: Stand, O so-and-so, and call among the people: Let them fast tomorrow."
"4300","8 - Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah said: Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah with this chain similarly, he said: And he ordered Bilal, who called among the people."
"4301","9 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr, he is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I sighted the crescent tonight. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? He said: Yes. He said: Stand, O Bilal, and call among the people: Let them fast tomorrow."
"4302","10 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hazim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: People disputed about the crescent in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a bedouin came and testified that he saw it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am Allah's Messenger? He said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called out that fasting is tomorrow. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, from al-Husayn al-Ju'fi, and from Musa, from Hammad, from Simak, similarly, without mentioning Ibn 'Abbas. Abu Dawud said: A group narrated it from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, in mursal form. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Isma'il, from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr, from Simak, similarly, and from Abu Kurayb, from Husayn al-Ju'fi, from Za'idah, with it. And he said: Al-Thawri and others narrated it from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in mursal form. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz Ibn Abi Rizmah, from al-Sinani, from Sufyan, from Simak, with a connected chain, and from Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Husayn, with it, and from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Abu Dawud, and from Muhammad ibn Hatim, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, all from Sufyan, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, in mursal form. And he said: This is more correct than the hadith of al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani, because Simak ibn Harb was sometimes prompted, so it was said to him: from Ibn 'Abbas. Ibn al-Mubarak is firmer in Sufyan than al-Fadl, and when Simak is alone with a basis he is not a proof, because he was prompted and accepted prompting. Ibn Majah narrated it from 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah al-Awdi and Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi, from Abu Usamah, from Za'idah, with it. I say: The narration of Za'idah and Hazim ibn Ibrahim al-Bajali strengthens the narration of al-Fadl al-Sinani; I have seen more than one hadith of Sahih hadith which Ibn al-Mubarak narrates stopping it. As for Simak ibn Harb, reports about him differed; Yahya ibn Ma'in deemed him trustworthy. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Truthful, trustworthy, and Muslim narrated much from him in his Sahih."
"4303","Another: 11 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us, that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it; if a cloud or haze stands between you and it, complete Sha'ban as thirty, and do not meet Ramadan by fasting a day of Sha'ban."
"4304","12 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Hatim Ibn Abi Saghirrah, from Simak ibn Harb who said: I woke fasting on the doubtful day of Ramadan, and came to 'Ikrimah while he was eating bread, greens, and grapes. He said: Come and eat. I said: I am fasting. He said: I swear by Allah you shall break it. I said: Glory be to Allah. He said: I swear by Allah you shall break it. When I saw him swearing without exception, I came forward and ate though full, having taken suhur just before that. Then he said: Bring now what you have. He said: Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if cloud stands before it, complete the number as thirty, and do not meet the month by anticipating it."
"4305","13 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad in Herat informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu al-Qasim Ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Ghazi al-Harras informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather, meaning Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, informed us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Bazzar narrated to us with a strange report, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak who said: I entered upon 'Ikrimah on the doubtful day of Ramadan while he was eating. He said: Come and eat. I said: I am fasting. He said: By Allah you shall come. I said: Then narrate to me. He said: Ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the month by anticipating it; fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if cloud or haze stands between you and its sight, complete the number as thirty."
"4306","14 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if haze stands before it, complete the number, and the month is twenty-nine."
"4307","15 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated to us, al-Walid Ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not precede the month. Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if haze is between you and it, complete the number."
"4308","16 - And with it Sulayman informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if haze stands before it, complete thirty. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Isma'il, from Hatim Ibn Abi Saghirrah with his chain: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if cloud stands between you and it, complete the number as thirty, and do not meet the month by anticipating it. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, from al-Husayn ibn 'Ali, from Za'idah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas, similarly, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah also, and from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Hatim Ibn Abi Saghirrah, similarly, and from Qutaybah, from Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Abu Yunus, from Simak, similarly. It is narrated in Muslim from the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended it for its sighting; if it is obscured for you, complete the number. In what we mentioned is an addition to this. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas."
"4309","Another: 17 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a man came as a Muslim in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then his wife came as a Muslim after him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, she had accepted Islam with me. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned her to him."
"4310","18 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a woman accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then her husband came after her and said: O Messenger of Allah, she had accepted Islam with me, so he returned her to him. Abu Dawud reported it from 'Uthman Ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yusuf ibn 'Isa, both from Waki', and al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"4311","Another: 19 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was turned toward the Ka'bah, they said: How about our brothers who died before that while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {And Allah would never waste your faith}."
"4312","20 - Abu Muhammad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was turned toward the Ka'bah, they said: O Messenger of Allah, what about our brothers who died before that, who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {And Allah would never waste your faith}. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam, Khalaf ibn al-Walid, and Shadhan, from Isra'il. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari and 'Uthman, from Waki', from Sufyan, from Simak. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad and Abu 'Ammar, from Waki', from Isra'il, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"4313","Another: 21 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: There were Qurayzah and al-Nadir; al-Nadir were nobler than Qurayzah. He said: When a man of Qurayzah killed a man of al-Nadir he was killed for him, but when a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah he paid a hundred wasqs of dates. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah, and they said: Hand him over to us to kill him. They said: Between us and you is the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they came to him, and there was revealed: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice}: a life for a life. Then was revealed: {Do they seek the judgment of ignorance?} Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-'Ala. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar, both from 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"4314","Another: 22 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Zubayri and Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, they said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A woman accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and married; her first husband came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had accepted Islam and she knew of my Islam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her from her latter husband and returned her to her first husband."
"4315","23 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: The paternal aunt of 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith accepted Islam and emigrated, then married, while her husband had accepted Islam before her; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned her to her husband."
"4316","24 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Isra'il, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A woman accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then her first husband came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I accepted Islam with her, and she knew of my Islam with her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her from her latter husband and returned her to her first husband."
"4317","25 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr, he is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: A woman accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); her husband came after her and said: O Messenger of Allah, she had accepted Islam with me, so he returned her to him. Abu Dawud narrated it from Nasr ibn 'Ali, from Abu Ahmad, from Isra'il. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi, from Hafs ibn Jumay', from Simak, similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili. Sulayman ibn Mu'adh, it is said he is Sulayman ibn Qarm: we reported him for consideration, and Muslim narrated from him for consideration."
"4318","Another: 26 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib al-Tamimi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Umar informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: {And indeed the devils inspire their allies}. He said: They say: What is slaughtered for other than Allah, do not eat it; what Allah slaughtered, eat it. So Allah revealed: {And do not eat of that over which Allah's name has not been mentioned}. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Isra'il. Ibn Majah narrated it from 'Umar ibn 'Abdullah al-Awdi, from Waki', from Isra'il, similarly."
"4319","Another: 27 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi there informed us, that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them, Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us, Judge Abu Sa'id al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke eloquent speech. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some eloquence is magic, and indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"4320","28 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. 29 - Al-Tabarani said: Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, they said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began speaking eloquent speech. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some eloquence is magic, and indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"4321","30 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke eloquent speech. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some eloquence is magic, and indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"4322","31 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, Simak narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom, and indeed some eloquence is magic. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hasan ibn Musa, 'Abd al-Rahman, and 'Affan, from Abu 'Awanah, and from al-Fadl, from Sharik, from Simak, and from Abu Sa'id, from Za'idah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and said: A hasan hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr Ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu Usamah, from Za'idah, from Simak. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah did not say: Indeed some eloquence is magic. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it in full from Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sayrafi, servant of Talut, from Ibn Abi al-Shawarib Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik, from Abu 'Awanah. In al-Bukhari from the hadith of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom. It has been narrated with an addition to this."
"4323","32 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: I said to Abu Usamah: Did Za'idah narrate to you, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom, and indeed some eloquence is magic. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would quote poetry? He said: Yes."
"4324","33 - Abu Ja'far, also, informed us, that Abu al-Khayr 'Abd al-Karim ibn 'Ali ibn Furajah informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, Abu 'Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would quote poetry."
"4325","34 - Abu 'Arubah said: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, al-Walid Ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah who said: I asked 'A'ishah: Did you ever hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) quote poetry? She said: Sometimes when he entered his house he would say. So 'Ikrimah narrated it from Ibn 'Abbas and 'A'ishah."
"4326","Another: 35 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A caravan came to Madinah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought ounces from it and distributed them among the widows of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, and said: I do not buy anything for which I do not have its price."
"4327","36 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a caravan that arrived, meaning he profited, ounces of gold in it, and gave them in charity to the widows of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, and said: I do not buy anything for which I do not have its price. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from al-Zubayri and Aswad ibn 'Amir, from Sharik. Abu Dawud narrated it from 'Uthman Ibn Abi Shaybah and Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Sharik, and from 'Uthman, from Sharik."
"4328","Another: 37 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali al-Sufi in Baghdad informed us, that Abu al-Waqt 'Abd al-Awwal ibn 'Isa informed them, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, 'Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to me, al-Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A mouse came dragging the wick. He said: The slave girl went to drive it away. Then it brought it and burned, before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the mat he was sitting upon, burning from it the size of a dirham. So he said: When you sleep, extinguish your lamps, for Satan guides the likes of this to this, and it burns you."
"4329","38 - Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tammar narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Talhah narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A mouse came dragging the wick, brought it and cast it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the mat he was sitting upon, burning from it the size of a dirham's place. So he said: When you sleep, extinguish your lamps, for Satan guides the likes of this to this, and it burns you. Thus Abu Dawud reported it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Ahmad ibn Adam al-Jurjani Ghundar, from 'Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah."
"4330","Another: 39 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz al-Harawi there informed us, that Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl informed them, Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us, Judge al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a small mat."
"4331","40 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a small mat. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman, 'Abd al-Samad, Husayn ibn 'Ali, and Abu Sa'id, from Za'idah, from Simak, and from 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu 'Awanah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb, from Mansur Ibn Abi Muzahim, from Abu al-Ahwas. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4332","Another: 41 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the prohibition of wine came down, they said: O Messenger of Allah, what about our brothers who died while drinking it? Then was revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believed and did righteous deeds for what they tasted} to the end of the verse."
"4333","42 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When wine was forbidden, they said: O Messenger of Allah, our companions who died while drinking it! So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believed and did righteous deeds for what they tasted}. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Khalaf ibn al-Walid, from Isra'il. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from 'Abd ibn Humayd, from 'Abd al-'Aziz Ibn Abi Rizmah, from Isra'il, and said: A hasan hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"4334","Another: 43 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad Ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi in Damascus informed us, that Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad al-Sulami informed them, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad Ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Uthman Ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Imam informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Abdus Ibn Abi Zaydun al-Qaysarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he finished Badr: Go after the caravan, there is nothing before it. Al-'Abbas, a captive in bonds, said: It is not proper. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why? He said: Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"4335","44 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he finished Badr: Go after the caravan, there is nothing before it. Al-'Abbas, a captive in bonds, said: It is not proper. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why? He said: Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"4336","45 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished Badr: Go after the caravan, there is nothing before it. He said: So al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib called to him: It is not proper for you. He said: And why? He said: Because Allah, mighty and majestic, promised you only one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from 'Abd al-Razzaq and Yahya ibn Adam, both from Isra'il. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from 'Abd ibn Humayd, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Isra'il, and said: A hasan hadith."
"4337","Another: 46 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih al-'Ijli narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning this verse: {O you who believed, indeed among your wives and children are enemies to you, so beware of them}. He said: These are men who accepted Islam from the people of Makkah and wanted to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and understood the religion, they wanted to punish them. So Allah revealed: {O you who believed, indeed among your wives and children are enemies to you, so beware of them; but if you pardon, overlook, and forgive, then indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful}."
"4338","47 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Qurashi in Damascus informed us, that 'Ali ibn al-Muslim al-Sulami informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid Ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn 'Uthman informed us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Imam informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubdus al-Qaysarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, and a man asked him about this verse: {O you who believed, indeed among your wives and children are enemies to you, so beware of them; but if you pardon, overlook, and forgive, then indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful}. He said: He said: These are men who accepted Islam from the people of Makkah and wanted to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but their wives and children refused to let them go. Then they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw that people had understood the religion, they intended to punish them. So Allah revealed: {O you who believed, indeed among your wives and children are enemies to you, so beware of them; but if you pardon, overlook, and forgive, then indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful}. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, and said: A hasan sahih hadith."
"4339","Another: 48 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trim his mustache, and Ibrahim the Close Friend used to trim his mustache."
"4340","49 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr, he is Ibn Harb, narrated to us, Yahya Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to cut his mustache, and Ibrahim, peace be upon him, used to cut his mustache."
"4341","50 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah Sammuyah informed us, Muhammad, he is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Trimming the mustache is of the Sunnah."
"4342","51 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya Ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trim his mustache, and your father Ibrahim, peace be upon him, before him used to trim his mustache. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn al-Walid al-Kindi, from Yahya ibn Adam, from Isra'il, similarly, and said: A hasan gharib hadith."
"4343","Another: 52 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani there informed us, that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb. 53 - Abu Ja'far, also, in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Sawdah feared that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divorce her, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to 'A'ishah. So he did, and Allah revealed: {There is no blame upon them to settle between them a settlement, and settlement is best}. So whatever they settle upon is permissible. The wording is al-Muqaddami's. The narration of Yunus: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divorce her, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, do not divorce me, keep me, and give my day to 'A'ishah. So he did, and this verse came down: {And if a woman fears from her husband discord or neglect} to the end of the verse. He said: So whatever they settle upon is permissible. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abu Dawud, and said: A hasan gharib hadith. I say: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh, it is said he is Ibn Qarm, and there is criticism of him, though Muslim narrated from him."
"4344","Another: 54 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet traders, do not leave milk in udders, and let none of you sell for another."
"4345","55 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah bint 'Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the market, do not leave milk in udders, and let none of you sell for another. Imam Ahmad and his son 'Abdullah narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad Ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad, from Abu al-Ahwas, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Our intent from this hadith is: and do not leave milk in udders, for in the two Sahihs from the narration of Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting riders and a townsman selling for a bedouin. I said to Ibn 'Abbas: What is his saying: a townsman selling for a bedouin? He said: He should not be his broker."
"4346","Another: 56 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah who said: There were two co-wives; there was clamor between them, and one threw a stone at the other, causing her to miscarry a dead boy, and the woman died. Judgment was given against the killer for blood-money. Her uncle said: She miscarried, O Messenger of Allah, a boy whose hair had grown. The killer's father said: He lies; by Allah, he neither cried, nor reasoned, nor drank, nor ate; such is void. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rhymed speech of pre-Islamic ignorance and its soothsaying?! I see for the boy a slave as compensation. Ibn 'Abbas said: The name of one was Mulaykah and the other Umm 'Afif. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim, from 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi, from Asbat, similarly, and I do not see Ibn 'Abbas in it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Bakr al-A'yan, from 'Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah, similarly. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"4347","Another: 57 - Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Qurashi in Damascus informed us, that 'Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad informed us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Uthman Ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Imam informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubdus Ibn Abi Zaydun al-Qaysarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged a fifth for buried treasure."
"4348","58 - Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, and Abu Nu'aym, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged a fifth for buried treasure. 59 - My father said: Aswad, meaning Ibn 'Amir, narrated it to us, Isra'il narrated to us. He said: And he judged, and Abu Nu'aym said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged a fifth for buried treasure."
"4349","60 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged a fifth for buried treasure. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, from Isra'il. Ibn Majah narrated it from Nasr ibn 'Ali, from Abu Ahmad, from Isra'il. It has a witness in the two Sahihs with the narration of Sa'id and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"4350","Another: 61 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, 'Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you differ about a road, make it seven cubits, and whoever builds a building, let him support it upon his neighbor's wall."
"4351","62 - And with the same chain, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you disagree about the road, make it seven cubits, and whoever is asked by his neighbor to support upon his wall, let him do so."
"4352","63 - And with the same chain, my father narrated to me, Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you disagree about the road, leave seven cubits then build, and whoever is asked by his neighbor to support upon his wall, let him support him. Ibn Majah narrated it - and he did not mention what is at its end about one who builds a building - from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli and Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj, from Qabisah, from Sufyan."
"4353","Another 64 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr - he is al-Muqaddami - narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No infection, no omen, no Hamah, no Safar. A man said: We take the mangy sheep and cast it among the sheep and they become mangy. He said: Then who infected the first?!"
"4354","65 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. 66 - Al-Tabarani said: And Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Ibn al-Tabba narrated to us - both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No infection, no omen, no Hamah, no Safar. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we take the mangy sheep and cast it among the sheep and they become mangy. He said: Then who infected the first?! Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Said, from Zaidah, from Simak, and from Affan from Abu Awanah. And Ibn Majah narrated: (No omen, no Hamah, no Safar) from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it - in full - from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah, from Abu Awanah. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah."
"4355","Another 67 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That Quraysh came to a female soothsayer and said to her: Tell us who among us most resembles the owner of this station. She said: If you drag a cloak over this plain then walk upon it, I will inform you. So they dragged it, then the people walked upon it, and she saw the footprint of Muhammad, and said: This one most resembles him among you. Then they remained after that twenty years, or close to twenty years, or as Allah willed, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from Israil, similarly."
"4356","Another 68 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land and wants to sell it, let him offer it to his neighbor. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ahmad ibn Sinan and al-Ala ibn Salim, from Yazid ibn Harun. It has a corroboration in Muslim from the narration of Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"4357","Another 69 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present, Abu Nuaym informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come out from the east a people who recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats, they pass through the religion - or he said: through Islam - as the arrow passes through the target."
"4358","70 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People from my ummah will recite the Quran, passing through Islam as the arrow passes through the target."
"4359","71 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it myself from him - Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People from my ummah will recite the Quran, passing through Islam as the arrow passes through the target. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Suwayd ibn Said, from Abu al-Ahwas. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Sahl ibn Hunayf. And in Muslim from the narration of Ali, peace be upon him, and Abu Dharr and Abu Said."
"4360","Another 72 - My maternal uncle, the Imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Abu Zurah Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them - at Baghdad - Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Muqawwimi informed us, Abu Talhah al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah ibn Bahr al-Qattan informed us, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us, Ali ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Ansar had homes far from the mosque and they wanted to move closer, so it was revealed: {And We record what they have put forth and their traces}. He said: So they stayed. Ibn Majah brought it thus in his Sunan."
"4361","73 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz - at Isfahan - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Yunus informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman adh-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The homes of the Ansar were far from the mosque, and they wanted to move to be near the mosque, so Allah revealed {And We record what they have put forth and their traces}. They said: Yes, we shall stay in our place, so they stayed. It has a corroboration in Sahih al-Bukhari from the hadith of Humayd from Anas: Banu Salamah wanted to move. And in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Abu Nadrah from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: The open lands became vacant and Banu Salamah wanted to move near the mosque, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Banu Salamah, your dwellings, for your traces are recorded, so they stayed and said: It would not please us that we had moved."
"4362","Another 74 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every joint of man is a prayer. A man from the people said: This is hard, and who can bear this! He said: Enjoining good and forbidding evil is a prayer, and carrying the weak is a prayer, and every step one of you takes toward prayer is a prayer."
"4363","75 - And with the same chain Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every joint of the son of Adam each day is a charity, then he mentioned a similar hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili from Abu Mamar."
"4364","Another 76 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us - that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it myself from him - Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go out on a journey, he said: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the burden of travel and from gloom upon return, O Allah, contract the earth for us and ease travel for us, and when he wanted to return, he said: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord, and when he entered among his family, he said: A return to our Lord, a return that leaves no sin against us."
"4365","77 - And with the same chain my father narrated to me, Ishaq - he is Ibn Isa - narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go out on a journey, he said: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the burden of travel and gloom upon return, O Allah, contract the earth for us and ease travel for us."
"4366","78 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. 79 - Al-Tabarani said: And Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go out on a journey he said: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the burden of travel and gloom upon return, O Allah, contract the earth for us and ease travel for us, and when he returned he said: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord, and when he entered among his family he said: A return, a return to our Lord in repentance, leaving no sin against us. It has a corroboration in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Ali al-Azdi, from Ibn Umar, similar to it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, from Khalaf ibn Hisham, from Abu al-Ahwas, similarly."
"4367","Another 80 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Ghaffar - he is Ibn Abd Allah - narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Misar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I shall surely fight Quraysh three times, then he fell silent, then said: If Allah wills."
"4368","81 - And with the same chain Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Shabib narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely fight Quraysh, by Allah I shall surely fight Quraysh, by Allah I shall surely fight Quraysh, three times, then he said: If Allah wills."
"4369","82 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah I shall surely fight Quraysh, by Allah I shall surely fight Quraysh, and he said at the third: If Allah wills. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Idris, from Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah."
"4370","Another 83 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us - that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man should touch another man in one garment, nor a woman another woman. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq from Israil. 84 - He said: And Aswad did not raise it. And he narrated it to us from Hasan, from Simak, from Ikrimah, mursal. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, from al-Naqid, from al-Zubayri, from Israil. It has a corroboration in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Said from his father: (Nor should a man lie with a man in one garment, nor a woman lie with a woman in one garment). And similar to it already preceded in the narration of Sulayman ibn Fayruz al-Shaybani."
"4371","Another 85 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Jafar ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever existed in Jahiliyyah, Islam only increased it in strength or newness."
"4372","86 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - it was said to Sharik: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes - he said: There is no alliance in Islam, and every alliance that existed in Jahiliyyah, Islam only increased it in newness and strength."
"4373","87 - And Abu Ahmad and Abu Tahir informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - and he raised it - he said: Whatever alliance existed in Jahiliyyah, Islam only increased it in newness and strength. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hajjaj from Sharik. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"4374","Another 88 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Dajjal is one-eyed, white-complexioned, bright, as if his head is a viper, the most resembling of people to Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan; as for the destruction of the destroyed, your Lord is not one-eyed. Shubah said: So I narrated it to Qatadah, and he narrated to me something similar."
"4375","89 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Ikrimah narrating, from Ibn Abbas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: Bright, white-complexioned, one-eyed, the most resembling of people to Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan - or he said: Qatr - as for the destruction of the destroyed, your Lord - Mighty and Exalted - is not one-eyed. Imam Ahmad and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it thus. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Wahb ibn Jarir from Shubah, and in it there is no: (bright). And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Sulayman ibn al-Husayn al-Attar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh, from his father, from Shubah. And Abu al-Walid narrated it from Zaidah, with an addition."
"4376","90 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is curly-haired, white, moon-bright, as if his head is a tree branch, his left eye effaced, and the other as if a floating grape, the most resembling of people to him is Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan; as for the destruction of the destroyed, he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed."
"4377","Another 91 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, then the qiblah was turned afterwards."
"4378","92 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah informed us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he and his Companions, toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, then the qiblah was changed afterwards. Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated it from Zaidah. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd ar-Rahman, from Zaidah. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Ishaq Amr ibn Abd Allah as-Sabii, from al-Bara ibn Azib: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Madinah, prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months."
"4379","Another 93 - Abu Jafar Muhammad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. 94 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was sleeping and I was visited, and it was said to me: Tonight is Laylat al-Qadr, so I stood while drowsy, and my foot caught on one of the ropes of the tent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing in prayer. Ibn Abbas said: So I looked at the night, and it was the night of the twenty-third. And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi."
"4380","95 - And Abu Ahmad and Abu Tahir informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Simak informed us, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: I was visited while sleeping in Ramadan, and it was said to me: Tonight is Laylat al-Qadr. He said: So I stood while drowsy, and I caught hold of one of the ropes of the tent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was praying. He said: So I looked at that night, and it was the night of the twenty-third."
"4381","Another 96 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sharik and Salam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, Hajj every year? He said: No, rather one Hajj, and had I said every year it would have been every year."
"4382","97 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Upon every Muslim is one Hajj, and had I said every year it would have been. And Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Dawud, and Yahya ibn Adam, from Sharik."
"4383","Another 98 - Abu Ahmad and Abu Tahir informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us. 99 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he commanded Ali, so he prepared ghusl for him, then gave him a garment and said: Screen me and turn your back to me. The wording of Ahmad is: with it Jafar. And in the narration of al-Tabarani: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Ali, and the rest is similar."
"4384","Another 100 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Mahmud narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Hatim ibn Abi Saghirah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons a prayer meets Allah while He is angry with him. Sahl ibn Mahmud and Salih are both trustworthy."
"4385","Another 101 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jawwas al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the saying of Allah: {And stand before Allah devoutly obedient}. He said: They used to speak in prayer; the servant of a man would come to him while he was in prayer and speak to him about his need, so they were forbidden from speech. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4386","Another 102 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas - freedman of Banu Hashim - narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: {While you are heedless}, he said: Amused, turning away from them."
"4387","Another 103 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Man Thabit ibn Nuaym al-Hawji narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us. 104 - Sulayman said: And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, both said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, both said: The prophets were from Banu Israil except ten: Nuh, Hud, Lut, Salih, Shuayb, Ibrahim, Ismail, Ishaq, Isa, and Muhammad - may Allah bless them - and there is no prophet with two names except Isa and Yaqub, peace be upon them both."
"4388","Another 105 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Aishah bought Barirah from the Ansar to free her, and they stipulated her wala for themselves, so she stipulated that for them; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came she informed him, and he said: Wala belongs only to the one who frees. Then he ascended the pulpit and said: What is with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah; whatever condition is not in the Book of Allah is rejected to the Book of Allah. And Barirah had a husband, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her choice: if she wished to remain with her husband as she was, and if she wished she would separate from him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house and saw a sheep's leg, and said to Aishah: Will you not cook this meat for us. She said: It was given in charity to Barirah and she gifted it to us. He said: Cook it, for it is charity for her and a gift for us. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Tamim. It is narrated in al-Bukhari from the narration of Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The husband of Barirah was a black slave, called Mughith, a slave of Banu so-and-so; it is as if I am looking at him circling behind her with his tears flowing upon his beard, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abbas, do you not marvel at the love of Mughith for Barirah, and the hatred of Barirah for Mughith. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If only you would go back to him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, do you command me? He said: I am only interceding. She said: Then I have no need of him. And what we mentioned is not this, and what we mentioned has a corroboration in the Sahih from the hadith of Aishah."
"4389","Another 106 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib al-Tamimi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - {Our Lord, we have believed, so write us among the witnesses}. He said: With Muhammad and his ummah, that they testify for him that he conveyed, and they testified for the messengers that they conveyed."
"4390","107 - And with the same chain Abu Bakr ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Bazzaz narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying: {We have believed, so write us among the witnesses}, meaning: Muhammad - peace be upon him - and his ummah, and they are the witnesses testifying for their Prophet that he conveyed, and for the messengers that they conveyed."
"4391","Another 108 - And with the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Kamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Israil al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying: {And a witness from her household testified}, he said: A bearded one."
"4392","109 - And with the same chain Ibn Mardawayh said: Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Qilabah ar-Raqashi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, similar to it."
"4393","Another 110 - And with the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: {An elevated land with settlement and water}. He said: I was informed that they are the rivers of Damascus."
"4394","Another 111 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep of Sawdah bint Zamah died, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so died - meaning the sheep - so he said: Why did you not take its skin. She said: Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Allah Almighty only said: {Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden to an eater who eats it except that it be carrion or spilled-out blood or the flesh of swine}, and you do not eat it; that you tan it and benefit from it. So she sent to it and skinned its hide. Then she tanned it and made from it a waterskin until it wore out with her."
"4395","112 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep of Sawdah bint Zamah died, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so died - meaning the sheep - so he said: Did you not take its skin. They said: Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: He only said: {Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden to an eater who eats it except that it be carrion or spilled-out blood or the flesh of swine}, you do not eat it, you only slaughter it and benefit from it. So she sent to it, and skinned its hide, and tanned it, and made from it a waterskin, until it wore out with her."
"4396","113 - And with the same chain Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep died, then he mentioned similar to it, and at its end: So they made its skin, and I saw it after a year. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sawdah, she said: A sheep of ours died, so we tanned its skin, then we kept making nabidh in it until it became worn. And al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the narration of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did you not make use of its hide. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only eating it was forbidden. And what we mentioned has an addition over this. And this hadith has been narrated in the Sahih from Ibn Abbas from Maymunah, and from Ibn Abbas without mentioning Maymunah. So what we mentioned thus, Ibn Abbas narrated it from Sawdah, and in this narration of ours he did not mention Sawdah. And this hadith has parallels in the Sahih."
"4397","Another 114 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad - at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying: {A day the measure of which is fifty thousand years}. He said: The Day of Resurrection, {And indeed a day with your Lord is as a thousand years of what you count}. He said: Of the six days in which Allah created the heavens and the earth, and regarding His saying: {He arranges the matter from the heaven to the earth, then it ascends to Him in a day the measure of which is a thousand years}, he said: Of the six days in which Allah created the heavens and the earth."
"4398","Another 115 - And with the same chain from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying {And the sky with return}. He said: Rain after rain. {And the earth with splitting}. He said: Its splitting for vegetation."
"4399","Sayyar ibn Abd ar-Rahman as-Sadafi, the Egyptian, from Ikrimah 116 - Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, that Muflih ad-Dumi informed them, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid ad-Dimashqi and Abd Allah ibn Abd ar-Rahman as-Samarqandi narrated to us, both said: Marwan narrated to us. Abd Allah said: Abu Yazid al-Khawlani narrated to us - and he was a truthful shaykh, and Abu Wahb used to narrate from him - Sayyar ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Mahmud said as-Sadafi: from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) obligated Zakat al-Fitr as purification for fasting from idle talk and obscenity, and as food for the poor; whoever gives it before prayer, it is an accepted zakat, and whoever gives it after prayer, it is a charity among charities."
"4400","Shabib ibn Bishr al-Bajali from Ikrimah 117 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid an-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim at-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the privy, then came out and there was a covered basin. He said: Who made this? Abd Allah said: I. He said: O Allah, teach him the interpretation of the Quran."
"4401","Another 118 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Bishr informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - {And your turning among those who prostrate}. He said: From prophet to prophet until you were brought forth a prophet."
"4402","119 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz - known as Qafak - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ghiyath ibn Muhammad ibn Ghiyath and Ibrahim ibn Aban ibn Rustah narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: {And your turning among those who prostrate}, from prophet to prophet until you were brought forth a prophet."
"4403","120 - And my maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed them - at Baghdad - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, the judge Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Batha informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ash-Shafii informed us, Ibrahim - he is Ibn Abd Allah - narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas - {And your turning among those who prostrate}: From prophet to prophet until you emerged a prophet."
"4404","Another 121 - Abu al-Yumn Zayd ibn al-Hasan ibn Zayd al-Kindi - in the outskirts of Damascus - and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf - at Baghdad - informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khayyat informed them, Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn an-Naqqur informed us, Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us - by dictation - my father, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Isa, narrated to me, Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah an-Numayri narrated to us, Abu Asim an-Nabil ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying, Mighty and Exalted: {Our Lord, You made us die twice and You gave us life twice}. He said: He gave them life when they were nothing. Then He made them die, then He gave them life."
"4405","Another 122 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman adh-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Qattan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: This verse: {Indeed those who believed and those who were Jews and the Sabians and the Christians and the Magians and those who associated partners}. He said: Those who were Jews: the Jews. And the Christians: they are the Christians, and the Sabians: they have no book, and as for the Magians, they are the people of idols, and as for the polytheists, they are the Christians of the Arabs: Banu Taghlib and Banu Jusham ibn Zuhayr; whoever among them is in that state, their slaughtered animals and their women are not lawful for a Muslim; because they say at slaughter: In the name of the Messiah, and their women are not lawful for a Muslim except one among them who is a virgin whose virginity has guarded her. And the blood-money of the Jew and the Christian is half the blood-money of the Muslim: five thousand, and the blood-money of the Muslim is ten thousand, and the blood-money of the Magian was one hundred, and no Muslim is killed for a disbeliever."
"4406","Another 123 - And with the same chain Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn ad-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying: {To those who write the Book with their hands then say: This is from Allah, to purchase with it a small price}. He said: The rabbis of the Jews found the description of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) written in the Torah: dark-eyed, of medium stature, curly-haired, handsome-faced; when they found him in the Torah they erased him out of envy and transgression. Then a group from Quraysh of the people of Makkah came to them and said: Do you find in the Torah a prophet from us? They said: Yes, we find him tall, blue-eyed, lank-haired. So Quraysh denied, and said: This is not from us."
"4407","Another 124 - The Shaykh, the Imam Abu Bakr Abd ar-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili informed us - with my recitation to him at Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad as-Saigh informed you, recited to him. 125 - And Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Sukaynah al-Anmati informed us - with my recitation to him at Baghdad - and Abu ar-Raja Abd al-Hadi ibn Ali ibn Qasim, and Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ar-Rudhravarie, and Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Shirwayh ibn Shahrdar ibn Shirwayh ad-Daylami - at Hamadhan - that Abu al-Mahasin Nasr ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Barmaki informed them, both said: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn an-Naqqur al-Bazzaz informed us, Abu al-Qasim Isa narrated to us, my father Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah, the minister, narrated to us, Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah an-Numayri narrated to us, Abu Asim an-Nabil ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying, Mighty and Exalted: {Why do you say what you do not do}, he said: A man would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: I did such and such, and I did such and such, so Allah Almighty revealed: {Why do you say what you do not do}."
"4408","Another 126 - And with the same chain Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa narrated to us - by dictation - my father, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah, narrated to us, Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah an-Numayri narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding the saying of Allah the Exalted: {He decreed a term}. He said: Death, {And a specified term with Him}. He said: Until he meets his Lord."
"4409","Another 127 - And with the same chain my father, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah, the minister - may Allah raise his rank - narrated to us, Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Abu Asim an-Nabil ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Shabib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah have mercy on him - : {And they enjoined mercy}. He said: Mercy to people."
"4410","Another 128 - And with the same chain Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah an-Numayri narrated to us, Abu Asim ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - {And stand before Allah devoutly obedient}. He said: They used to speak in prayer, so they were commanded to be silent. Similar to it already preceded in the hadith of Simak."
"4411","Another 129 - Abu Muhammad Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ali ibn al-Muslim al-Lakhmi - at Damascus - informed us, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fath as-Sulami, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn an-Nadr al-Harawi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hammad at-Tahrani narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: From here and from here, meaning: {That day people will proceed in separate groups}."
"4412","Another 130 - And with the same chain from Ibn Abbas - {For they are with heads raised}, as the beast is raised with the bridle."
"4413","Another 131 - And with the same chain from Ibn Abbas - {And the heaven We built with strength}. He said: With power."
"4414","Another 132 - And with the same chain from Ibn Abbas - {And dense gardens}. He said: Trees that bear no fruit, shaded under."
"4415","Another 133 - And with the same chain from Ibn Abbas - {And whoever turns blindly from the remembrance of the Merciful}. He said: He becomes blind."
"4416","Another 134 - My maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed them, Abu al-Fadl Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, the judge al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Batha informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ash-Shafii informed us, Abu Muslim narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying, Mighty and Exalted: Emerging from between the backbone and the ribs, he said: The ribs are the place of the necklace."
"4417","Another 135 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim mentioned, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us. He said: My father narrated to me, my father narrated to me, he said: Shabib ibn Bishr informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - For whoever has a heart or gives ear while he is heedful. He said: The hypocrites would sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then go out and say: What did he say just now; they have no hearts with them."
"4418","Another 136 - And with the same chain Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - So We strengthened those who believed against their enemy, he said: So We gave power to those who believed."
"4419","Another 137 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Jarbadhqani - at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Mudar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Asim ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rivers are four: Sayhan and Jayhan and the Nile and the Euphrates; as for Sayhan, it is the river of Balkh, and as for Jayhan, it is the Tigris, and as for the Nile, it is the river of Egypt, and as for the Euphrates, it is the Euphrates of Kufah; so all that the son of Adam drinks is from these four; the rivers emerge from beneath the Rock."
"4420","Another 138 - And with the same chain Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Shabib narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - While you are lawful in this city. He said: You, O Muhammad, it is lawful for you to fight in it, and as for other than you, no."
"4421","Another 139 - And with the same chain Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - Indeed your hater is the cut off. He said: Abu Jahl."
"4422","140 - And with the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn ad-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying: When the earth is shaken with its shaking. He said: It moves from beneath, And the earth discharges its burdens. He said: The dead, And man says: What is with it: The disbeliever. That day it will relate its news. He said: Its Lord said to it: Speak, so it spoke. Because your Lord inspired it. He said: He inspired it. That day people will proceed in separate groups. He said: From each, here and here, So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it: Its weight in good he will see. Ahmad ibn Amr said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan saying: I heard Abu Asim saying: Forty red atoms weigh a black atom, and eighty black atoms are a barley grain."
"4423","Safwan ibn Amr, from Ikrimah 141 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Barzah al-Aslami was a soothsayer judging between the Jews in what they brought to him for judgment, then some Muslims brought their dispute to him, so Allah revealed: Have you not seen those who claim they believed in what was revealed to you and what was revealed before you, they want to take judgment to the Taghut - up to His saying - We intended nothing but good."
"4424","Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Kufi Abu Hariz, judge of Sijistan, from Ikrimah 142 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali as-Sufi and Abu al-Hasan Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari and Abu Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yaish - at Baghdad - and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi - at Cairo, informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn ash-Shaybani informed them, Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, he said: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzakki informed us, Abu Ishaq as-Sarraj informed us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt and over her maternal aunt."
"4425","143 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Musa - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan - narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Abu Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman marry over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Rawh from Said from Abu Hariz, and he did not mention Qatadah like the narration of Abd al-Ala. And at-Tirmidhi narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Ala, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mukram ibn Khalid al-Burti, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman, from al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah from Abu Hariz. And in it, and he said: If you women do that, you will sever your kinships."
"4426","144 - With it Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married over the paternal aunt and over the maternal aunt, and said: If you do that, you will sever your kinships. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the narration of ash-Shabi from Abu Hurayrah."
"4427","Abd Allah ibn Kaysan al-Marwazi Abu Mujahid from Ikrimah 145 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Zuhayr ibn Tahir ash-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, the Imam, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ibn Abi Rizmah, narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Kaysan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named the two prostrations of forgetfulness al-Murghimatayn."
"4428","146 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ibn Abi Rizmah, narrated to me, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named the two prostrations of forgetfulness al-Murghimatayn. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ibn Abi Rizmah. And Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we brought it. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah. I said: And Abd Allah ibn Kaysan, al-Bukhari said about him: Munkar al-hadith, and Abu Hatim ar-Razi said: Daif al-hadith, and an-Nasai said: Not strong; except that when we saw Ibn Khuzaymah and al-Busti brought his hadith, we brought it."
"4429","Another 147 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Mufaddal as-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us, that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi and Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them. 148 - And the Imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli and Abu al-Fath Masud ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Jundani and Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh - at Isfahan - and Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad al-Thaqafi - at Damascus - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them. 149 - And it was said to Abu al-Faraj: Abu Addan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Mutahhar, Ibn Abi Nizar, informed you - recited to him while you were present - they said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Harawi narrated to us - at Baghdad - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa as-Sinani narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Kaysan, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, went out at midday, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, heard of that and went out, and there was Abu Bakr. He said: O Abu Bakr, what brought you out at this hour? He said: By Allah, what brought me out is what I find in my belly of intense hunger. He said: And I, by Allah, nothing but it brought me out. While they were thus, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them and said: What brought you two out at this hour? They said: By Allah, what brought us out is what we find in our bellies of intense hunger. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing but it brought me out. So they stood and went until they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari; and Abu Ayyub had mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) food or milk, but that day he was late and did not come at its time, so his family fed him and he went to his palms working in them. When they came to the door of Abu Ayyub, his wife came out and said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those with him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Where is Abu Ayyub? She said: He will come to you, O Prophet of Allah, presently. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, and Abu Ayyub saw him while he was working in palms of his, so he came hastening until he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Welcome to the Prophet of Allah and those with him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is not the time you used to come to me. So he returned him, then came to a cluster of dates and cut it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I did not want this. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I loved that you eat of its ripe dates and unripe dates and dry dates and tadhunub, and I shall surely slaughter for you along with this. He said: If you slaughter, do not slaughter one with milk. So he took a young goat of his or a kid and slaughtered it, and said to his wife: Bake, and I shall cook, for you know baking better. So he took half the kid and cooked it, and roasted half of it. When the food was ready it was placed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took some of the kid and placed it upon a loaf, then said: O Abu Ayyub, convey this to Fatimah - peace be upon her - for she has not had the like of this for days. When they ate and were satiated, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bread and meat and unripe dates and dry dates and ripe dates, and his eyes shed tears. Then he said: This is of the bliss you will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection. That weighed heavily upon his Companions, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you get the like of this and strike with your hands, say: In the name of Allah and the blessing of Allah, and when you are satiated say: Praise be to Allah Who fed us and quenched us and favored and excelled, for this suffices for this. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - no one would do him a favor but he loved to repay him - so he said to Abu Ayyub: Come to us tomorrow. But he did not hear. So Umar said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to come to him. When he came to him he gave him a slave girl and said: O Abu Ayyub, treat her well, for we saw nothing but good as long as she was with us. When Abu Ayyub brought her he said: I find nothing better for the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than to free her, so he freed her. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Kaysan except al-Fadl ibn Musa. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Said as-Sadi, from Ali ibn Khashram, similarly."
"4430","Another 150 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu az-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Aktham, the judge, narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray toward a grave, nor pray over a grave."
"4431","Another 151 - And with this chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu ad-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, you had said to me on the day of Uhud when martyrdom was delayed from me and those martyred were martyred: Martyrdom is behind you. He said: How patient when this is dyed from this, and he gestured to his beard and his head. Ali said: As for what you explained, it is not of the places of patience, but it is of the places of glad tidings and honor."
"4432","Another 152 - And with the same chain Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from the expedition of Tabuk and performed umrah, and when he descended from the pass of Usfan he commanded his Companions to lean to the mountain path until I return to you, then he went and stopped at the grave of his mother and supplicated his Lord at length, then he wept and his weeping intensified and these wept for his weeping, and they said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not weep in this place except that something has occurred in his ummah they cannot bear. When these wept, he stood and returned to them and said: What makes you weep? They said: O Prophet of Allah, we wept for your weeping; we said: Perhaps something has occurred in your ummah we cannot bear. He said: No, though some of it has been, but I stopped at the grave of my mother and asked Allah to permit me to intercede for her on the Day of Resurrection, but Allah refused to permit me, so I pitied her, and she is my mother, so I wept. Then Jibril - peace be upon him - came to me and said: And the seeking of forgiveness of Ibrahim for his father was only about a promise he had promised him, then when it became clear to him that he is an enemy to Allah he disassociated from him. So disassociate you from your mother as Ibrahim disassociated from his father. So I pitied her, and she is my mother, and I asked my Lord to lift four things from my ummah, so He lifted two from them and refused to lift two from them. I asked my Lord to lift from them stoning from the sky, and drowning from the earth, and that He not divide them into sects, and that He not make some taste the violence of others. So He lifted from them stoning from the sky and drowning from the earth, and Allah refused to lift two from them: killing and turmoil. And he turned to the grave of his mother only because she is buried beneath such and such, and Usfan belonged to them."
"4433","Another 153 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman at-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu ad-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the expedition of Hunayn there was revealed to him: When the help of Allah comes and the conquest, to the end of the surah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali ibn Abi Talib, O Fatimah bint Muhammad: The help of Allah has come and the conquest, and I saw people entering the religion of Allah in crowds, so glory be to my Lord and with His praise, and I seek His forgiveness, indeed He is Most Relenting. And O Ali, there will be after me among the believers jihad. He said: For what do we fight the believers who say: We believe? He said: For innovating in the religion when they act by opinion, and there is no opinion in the religion; religion is only from the Lord, His command and His prohibition. Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, what if a matter presents to us about which no Quran descended and no sunnah from you passed. He said: You make it consultation among the worshippers from the believers, and do not decide it by opinion. Had I been appointing anyone, none would have been more deserving of it than you; for your precedence in Islam, and your kinship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and your marriage, and with you is the mistress of the believing women, and before that what was of the suffering of Abu Talib for me, and the Quran descended while I am keen to guard for him in his children."
"4434","Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn al-Asbahani al-Kufi, from Ikrimah 154 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr with them as three and forgot one, then left. Then a man from his Companions called Dhu ash-Shimalayn entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened? He said: What is that? He said: You prayed three. So he took his hand and went out to people who were with him and said: Is Dhu al-Yadayn truthful? They said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He claims I prayed three. They said: He spoke the truth. So we thought you were commanded in that with a command. So he prayed with them one rakah, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness. Ismail ibn Aban: I deem him al-Warraq al-Azdi, not al-Ghanawi, for al-Ghanawi was criticized, and he is older than this, and Allah knows best."
"4435","Another 155 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present, Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Masruq al-Kindi narrated to us, from Sufyan ath-Thawri, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a date cluster and died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought his inheritance and gave it to his fellow countrymen; perhaps: He gave his inheritance to a man of his kin."
"4436","Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Ghasil, from Ikrimah 156 - Abu Jafar Muhammad as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Mabahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa ibn Uthman al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Sayfi ibn Ribi narrating, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Allah will not punish you nor your children. Al-Bukhari narrated for Abd ar-Rahman from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - a hadith other than this. And Ismail ibn Musa ibn Uthman I deem other than the one about whom Abu Hatim ar-Razi said: He is unknown; for he said: Ismail ibn Musa al-Ansari, he narrated from Iyad ibn Iyad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays in congregation, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated from him."
"4437","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad from Ikrimah 157 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, al-Hudhayl ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Rawwad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The death of the stranger is martyrdom."
"4438","158 - And the Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad as-Salafi informed us - by ijazah - and Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah, known as Ibn Rawahah, informed us from him, that Abu al-Ghanaim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun an-Narsi al-Hafiz informed them - at Kufah - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us - by dictation - Ali ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, al-Hudhayl ibn al-Hakam al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The death of the stranger is martyrdom."
"4439","159 - And Abu Jafar as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, al-Hudhayl ibn al-Hakam ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The death of the stranger is martyrdom. Ibn Majah narrated it from Jamil ibn al-Hasan al-Jahdami, from Abu al-Mundhir al-Hudhayl."
"4440","Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari from Ikrimah 160 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd ar-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ukhuwwah and Umm Habibah Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir - at Isfahan - informed us, that Said ibn Abi ar-Raja as-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn an-Numan informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into the vessel and breathing into it."
"4441","161 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Israil, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into food and drink."
"4442","162 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breathing into the vessel or blowing into it. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd Allah an-Nufayli, from Ibn Uyaynah. And at-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Adani, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Abd ar-Rahim ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Muharibi, from Sharik, from Abd al-Karim, with its meaning. And from Abu Bakr ibn Khallad al-Bahili, from Sufyan, with his chain: He forbade blowing into the vessel."
"4443","Another 163 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr - he is Ibn Harb - narrated to us. 164 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, both said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah - meaning Ibn Amr - narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man went out from Khaybar, then two men followed him and another following them saying: Go back, go back, until he sent them back, then he caught up with the first and said: These two are two devils, and I kept with them until I sent them back; when you come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), convey salam to him and inform him that we are here gathering our charities, and had they been fit for him we would have sent them to him. He said: When the man came to Madinah he informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade being alone. Their wording is one, except that in the narration of Zuhayr ibn Harb (convey to him) and with him (had they been fit we would have sent them to him), he did not say: fit for him. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Khattabi, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, with his chain, similarly."
"4444","Another 165 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf - at Baghdad - informed us, that Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sad al-Baghdadi informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Muzaffar Mahmud ibn Jafar al-Kawsaj and Abu al-Qasim Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Mandah informed us, both said: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Mansur al-Antaki narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That a man from the polytheists called to duel on the day of Badr, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out to him, O Zubayr. So az-Zubayr went out to him and dueled him and killed him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his spoils."
"4445","Another 166 - Abu Jafar Muhammad as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin man died and he had no agnates, and he had a freedman whom he had freed, so that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Did he not anger for his anger and approve for his approval? They said: Yes. So he gave him the property of his freedman in inheritance. Abu Hamzah, his name is Muhammad ibn Maymun as-Sukkari al-Marwazi; al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated for him."
"4446","Another 167 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had the Jews wished for death they would have died, and they would have seen their seats in the Fire."
"4447","168 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Had those who invoke curses against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gone out, they would have returned finding neither property nor child. And this is the beginning of the hadith before it. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Jahl said: If I see Muhammad praying at the Kabah I shall surely tread upon his neck. It reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Had he done it, the angels would have seized him. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: Had the Jews wished for death they would have died, and had those who invoke curses against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gone out, they would have returned finding neither family nor property. We brought it because in al-Bukhari it is mawquf, and what we mentioned is marfu."
"4448","Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr from Ikrimah 169 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhai informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun az-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad at-Tamimi informed us, Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take good omens, and the good name pleased him. Thus Ibn Hibban brought it in his book. And Imam Ahmad narrated it from Aswad ibn Amir, from Huraym, from Layth, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take good omens and not take bad omens, and the good name pleased him. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No infection and no omen, and optimism pleases me. Al-Bukhari added: And optimism pleases me, the righteous good word."
"4449","Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir from Ikrimah 170 - And with the same chain Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us, Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: He is not from us who does not honor the elder, and have mercy on the young, and enjoin good, and forbid evil. Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Jarir from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Malik. And Imam Ahmad narrated it from Uthman ibn Muhammad, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr. And Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Nuaym, from Sharik, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir. And at-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Sharik, from Layth, from Ikrimah, and he did not mention Abd al-Malik, and said: A gharib hadith. I said: And I think Jarir did not hear it from Abd al-Malik, by evidence of the narration of Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi: from Jarir, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from him, and Allah knows best."
"4450","Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj from Ikrimah and others 171 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr as-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail as-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadha informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ar-Razi - known as Mihyar and he was truthful - narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - that while he was sitting, Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah ennoble his face - came and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, this Quran slips from my chest, and I cannot retain it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abu al-Hasan, shall I not teach you words Allah will benefit you with, and one you teach will benefit, and what you learn will be firm in your chest? He said: Yes, teach me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When it is the night of Friday, if you can stand in the last third of the night, for it is a witnessed hour, and supplication in it is answered, and it is the saying of my brother Yaqub to his sons: I shall seek forgiveness for you from my Lord, until the night of Friday comes; if you cannot, then in its middle; if you cannot, then in its beginning. So pray four rakahs: recite in the first rakah the Opening of the Book and Surah Ya-Sin, and in the second rakah the Opening of the Book and Ha-Mim, the Smoke, and in the third rakah the Opening of the Book and Alif-Lam-Mim, the Revelation, and in the fourth rakah the Opening of the Book and Tabarak, the Mufassal. When you finish the tashahhud, praise Allah - Mighty and Exalted - and praise Allah well, and send blessings upon me, and do well, then say at the end of that: O Allah, have mercy on me by abandoning sins ever as long as You keep me alive, and have mercy on me not to burden myself with what does not concern me, and grant me good consideration in what pleases You from me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of Majesty and Honor and Might that cannot be sought, I ask You by Allah, and O Merciful, by Your Majesty and the Light of Your Face, to bind my heart to memorize Your Book as You taught me, and grant me to recite it in the manner that pleases You from me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of Majesty and Honor and Might that cannot be sought, I ask You by Allah, O Merciful, by Your Majesty and the Light of Your Face, to illuminate my sight with Your Book, and to loosen my tongue with it, and to relieve my heart with it, and to expand my chest with it, and to employ my body with it; for none aids upon truth but You, and none grants it but You, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah. O Abu al-Hasan, do that three Fridays or six or seven, you will be answered, by permission of Allah - Blessed and Exalted. In our audition copy it was: from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Ikrimah; and it is an error."
"4451","172 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib - at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman adh-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Said al-Bushanji narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd ar-Rahman ad-Dimashqi, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas: that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - came to him and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, this Quran slips from my chest, and I cannot retain it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abu al-Hasan, shall I not teach you words Allah will benefit you with, and one you teach will benefit, and what you learn will be firm in your chest! He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, teach me. He said: When it is the night of Friday, if you can stand in the last third of the night, for it is a witnessed hour, and supplication in it is answered, and it is the saying of my brother Yaqub to his sons: I shall seek forgiveness for you from my Lord. At-Tirmidhi brought it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan at-Tirmidhi, from Sulayman ibn Abd ar-Rahman ad-Dimashqi, with his chain from Ata and Ikrimah, and it is longer than this, and said: A gharib hadith we know only from the hadith of al-Walid. I said: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Ishaq at-Tustari, from Hisham ibn Ammar, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi, from Abu Salih and Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, similarly, and in it is an addition over this of the coming of Ali - peace be upon him - and his memorizing, as at-Tirmidhi mentioned or similar. And our shaykh Abu al-Faraj Ibn al-Jawzi mentioned that this hadith is not authentic due to the sole transmission of al-Walid ibn Muslim by it, and said: The scholars of transmission said: He used to narrate from al-Awzai hadiths which are with al-Awzai from weak shaykhs, from shaykhs al-Awzai had met, like Nafi and az-Zuhri, so he drops the names of the weak and makes them from al-Awzai from them. I said: And this saying, our shaykh did not mention who said it. And al-Bukhari and Muslim agreed upon bringing his hadith in their Two Sahihs, and Marwan ibn Muhammad at-Tatari and Abd al-Ala ibn Mushir praised him, and they are of his city, and I did not see in the book of Ibn Abi Hatim any mention of disparagement of him, and he said: I asked my father about him, and he said: Salih al-hadith. And at-Tabarani narrated it from other than his hadith."
"4452","Another 173 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, informed me, claiming that Ibn Abbas informed him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep on the day of sacrifice among his Companions, and said: Slaughter them for your umrah, for they suffice you. And Sad ibn Abi Waqqas got a billy goat."
"4453","Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal from Ikrimah 174 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Abu az-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd ar-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man placing his foot upon the side of a sheep while sharpening his blade, and it was looking at him with its sight. So he said: Why not before this; do you want to kill it twice!"
"4454","Uthman ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf al-Ansari, from Ikrimah 175 - Abu Jafar as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Prayer from anyone upon anyone is not proper except upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4455","Uthman ash-Shahham al-Basri Abu Salamah, from Ikrimah 176 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ath-Thaqafi - at Damascus - informed us, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while both were present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ahmad ibn Isam narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Uthman ash-Shahham narrated to us, Ikrimah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when I eat of this meat I become aroused, and I have forbidden meat upon myself. So it was revealed: O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah has made lawful for you."
"4456","Another 177 - Abu Jafar as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Israil, from Uthman ash-Shahham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a blind man had an umm walad who would revile the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and speak ill of him much; so he would forbid her but she would not stop, and rebuke her but she would not be rebuked. Then one night she mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and attacked him, so he could not bear it and stood to the dagger and placed it in her belly, then leaned upon it until he killed her. Then her two children awoke between her legs stained with blood. So that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood and gathered the people, then said: I adjure by Allah a man who has a right upon me and did what he did, to stand. So the blind man came forward wailing and said: I, by Allah, O Prophet of Allah, am her owner; she is my umm walad, and I have from her two sons like two pearls, and she was indeed gentle and kind to me, but she would mention you and revile you, so I would forbid her but she would not stop, and rebuke her but she would not be rebuked. Last night she mentioned you and attacked you, so I could not bear it and stood to the dagger and placed it in her belly, then leaned upon it until I killed her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I bear witness that her blood is void."
"4457","178 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ath-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Dharr as-Salihani informed them - recited to him - Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ismail ibn Salim narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ash-Shahham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That an umm walad of a man would revile the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would forbid her but she would not stop, and rebuke her but she would not be rebuked. Then one day she reviled him, so he took a dagger and placed it in her belly, then leaned upon it until he pierced through. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness that her blood is void. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali. And an-Nasai narrated it from Uthman ibn Abd Allah, from Abbad ibn Musa."
"4458","Isam ibn Qudamah al-Bajali, and it is said: al-Jadali, Abu Muhammad, from Ikrimah 179 - Abu Ismail Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Mashadhah and others informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir ash-Shahhami informed them, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Maghribi informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us, from Isam ibn Qudamah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while he was with his wives: Would that I knew which of you the dogs of al-Hawb will bark at; killed to her right and to her left are groups of people, and she will barely escape."
"4459","Ata ibn as-Saib from Ikrimah 180 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi - at Damascus - informed us, that Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad as-Sulami informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali, the Imam, informed us, Said ibn Abdus ibn Abi Zaydun al-Qaysarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us. 181 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi - at Baghdad - informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to one of his daughters while she was struggling with her soul; so he fell upon her and did not raise his head until she passed away. He said: Then he raised his head and said: Praise be to Allah, the believer is in good; his soul is drawn from between his sides while he praises Allah. The wording of Aswad ibn Amir; and in the narration of al-Firyabi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached one of his daughters while she was struggling with her soul, so he bent over her and remained bent over her until her soul departed. Then he stood from her saying: Praise be to Allah, the believer is in good in every state; his soul exits from between his sides while he praises Allah."
"4460","182 - And with the same chain, Abd Allah said: My father narrated to me, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a daughter of his dying, and embraced her, and placed her between his breasts, and she died while between his breasts. Then Umm Ayman cried out. So he said: Do you weep in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! She said: Do I not see you weeping, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I do not weep; it is only mercy. The believer is in all good in every state; his soul exits from between his sides while he praises Allah, Mighty and Exalted."
"4461","183 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ath-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A small daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was attended. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her and drew her to himself, and placed her before him. Then Umm Ayman wept, and she is the mother of Usamah. So he said: Do you weep, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is with you. She said: Why should I not weep while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeps. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not weep; it is only mercy. The believer is in all good in every state; his soul is drawn from between his sides while he praises Allah. At-Tirmidhi narrated it in ash-Shamail from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri. And an-Nasai narrated it from Hannad ibn as-Sari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ata ibn as-Saib, similarly. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Kamil, from Abu Awanah, from Ata ibn as-Saib."
"4462","Another 184 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi - at Cairo - informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn informed them, Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan al-Bazzaz informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ash-Shafii informed us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that he was asked about the slaughtered animals of the Arab polytheists, so he recited: And whoever among you takes them as allies, then he is of them."
"4463","Ilba ibn Ahmar al-Yashkuri from Ikrimah 185 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq at-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Ilba ibn Ahmar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the sacrifice came, so seven shared in the cow, and ten in the camel."
"4464","186 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from Ilba ibn Ahmar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We were on a journey and the sacrifice came, so we slaughtered the cow for seven and the camel for ten. At-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth and more than one, and said: A hasan gharib hadith. And an-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Fadl, similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Ghazwan, and Hadiyyah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi, from al-Fadl, with its meaning. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Awn, from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth."
"4465","Another 187 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ath-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Ilba ibn Ahmar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines in the earth and said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women of Paradise: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh."
"4466","188 - And Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ilba, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines in the earth. He said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women of Paradise: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh."
"4467","189 - And Abu Jafar as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu an-Numan narrated to us. 190 - At-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, they said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat al-Kindi narrated to us, from Ilba ibn Ahmar al-Yashkuri, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines in the earth, then said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women of Paradise: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd as-Samad and Yunus ibn Muhammad from Dawud. And an-Nasai narrated it from al-Abbas ibn Muhammad from Yunus ibn Muhammad, and from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub from Abu an-Numan, and from Amr ibn Mansur from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Muhammad ibn Aban from Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat."
"4468","Ali ibn Badhimah al-Jazari from Ikrimah 191 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi ar-Raja - at Isfahan - informed us, that Masud ibn al-Hasan ath-Thaqafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman adh-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated to us. 192 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Anbari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, both said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated. He said: It was abrogated by: O you who believe, when you rise to prayer, wash your faces. An-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Dawud, from Sufyan."
"4469","Another 193 - Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Isa ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah did not reveal: O you who believe, except Ali is its chief and its noble; and Allah reproached the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in more than one place, and He did not mention Ali except with good."
"4470","194 - It was recited to Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi - while we listened at Damascus - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Mawazini as-Sulami informed you - while you listened at Damascus - it was said to him: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd as-Salam ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ubayd ibn Sadan, the witness - at Damascus, recited to him, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf ibn Yaqub ar-Rabi informed us, Abu al-Abbas Hajib ibn Arkin informed us, [lacuna] Ibn Abd Allah al-Barakat, Isa ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah did not mention: O you who believe, except Ali is its master and its noble and its chief; and Allah reproached the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in verses of the Quran, and He did not mention Ali except with good."
"4471","Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah from Ikrimah 195 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal as-Sufi and Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi, the two Isfahanis - in their book - informed us, that Abu Muhammad Abd ar-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan ad-Duni informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar ad-Dinawari informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq as-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd ar-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb an-Nasai informed us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth informed us, al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife does not withhold the hand of one who touches. He said: Send her away if you wish. He said: I fear my soul will follow her. He said: Enjoy her. An-Nasai narrated it thus. And Abu Dawud narrated it, he said: Husayn ibn Hurayth wrote to me. It was said: He meant that she is generous, squandering his wealth."
"4472","Another 196 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ath-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us. 197 - And Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Tawus - at Damascus - informed us, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn as-Sulami informed them, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, he said: It was recited to the judge Abu Bakr Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayyanji - while I was present listening - it was said to him: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed you - recited to him - Abd Allah ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Allaf Abu Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Khattab ibn Ubayd Allah, Ibn Abi Bakrah, informed us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah have mercy on him - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would have commanded killing every jet-black one; so kill the specified ones among dogs, for they are the accursed of the jinn."
"4473","Another 198 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz al-Harawi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Fudayli informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Malihi informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq as-Sarraj narrated to us - by dictation - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Mani, truthful trustworthy, narrated to us, Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The sun rises every year in three hundred and sixty openings, rising each day in an opening, not returning to that opening until the same day of the next year; and it rises only unwillingly. So it says: O Lord, do not make me rise upon Your servants, for I see them disobeying You, doing Your disobediences, I see them. He said: Have you not heard the saying of Umayyah ibn Abi as-Salt: Until it is dragged and flogged. So I said: O my master, is the sun flogged?! He said: You bit upon the obscenity of your father! He was only compelled by the meter to flogging."
"4474","Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki from Ikrimah 199 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ath-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous dream is a part - I think he said - of forty-six parts of prophethood. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Ubadah ibn as-Samit, and from the narration of Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah."
"4475","Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar from Ikrimah 200 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Umar ibn Ata informed me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: There is no celibacy in Islam."
"4476","201 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no celibacy in Islam. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Rawh from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata and others, from Ikrimah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no celibacy in Hajj. And he mentioned after it the hadith of Muhammad ibn Bakr. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman, from Abu Khalid, from Ibn Jurayj."
"4477","Another 202 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq at-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Habban al-Kufi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Provision: the supplies and the mount. Ibn Majah narrated it from Suwayd ibn Said, from Hisham ibn Sulayman al-Qurashi."
"4478","Amr ibn Dinar al-Athram from Ikrimah 203 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib - at Dar al-Qazz in Baghdad - informed us, that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them. 204 - And Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Harraz - at al-Karkh in Baghdad, informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, both said: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan ibn Malik al-Qatii narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi and Bishr ibn Musa al-Asadi narrated to us, both said: Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs: the umrah of the prevention, and the second when they agreed upon the umrah of the next year, and the third from al-Jiranah, and the fourth which was with his Hajj."
"4479","205 - And Abu Jafar as-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us. 206 - At-Tabarani said: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi and Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, they said: Dawud ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs: the umrah of al-Hudaybiyah, and the umrah of the fulfillment the next year, and his third umrah from al-Jiranah, and his fourth umrah which was with his Hajj."
"4480","207 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Dawud - meaning al-Attar - narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs: the umrah of al-Hudaybiyah, and the umrah of the fulfillment, and the third from al-Jiranah, and the fourth which was with his Hajj. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yunus from Dawud. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd Allah an-Nufayli and Qutaybah from Dawud. And at-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, from Dawud, and said: A gharib hadith. And from Said ibn Abd ar-Rahman from Ibn Uyaynah from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - mursal. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafii, from Dawud. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Jandi, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafii, from Dawud, except that he made it from Amr and Ikrimah. It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik."
"4481","Another 208 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi ar-Raja al-Hafiz - at Isfahan - informed us, that Masud ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Qasim ath-Thaqafi informed them, Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman adh-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub and Muhammad ibn Mansur ibn Ata narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf and companions of his came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, we were in honor while we were polytheists, then when we believed we became humbled. He said: I was commanded with pardon, so do not fight the people. When Allah moved him to Madinah He commanded him with fighting, but they held back. So Allah Almighty revealed: Have you not seen those to whom it was said: Restrain your hands and establish prayer and give zakat, then when fighting was written upon them, behold a group of them fear people. An-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq, from his father, with its meaning, and its end with him is: and establish prayer."
"4482","Another 209 - The Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Akhdar - at Baghdad - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn az-Zaghuni and Said ibn Ahmad ibn al-Banna informed him - recited to them - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali az-Zaynabi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, Yahya - he is Ibn Said - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: When the polytheists turned back from Uhud and reached ar-Rawha they said: You neither killed Muhammad nor took the maidens as followers; evil is what you did."
"4483","210 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr and Fatimah bint Saad al-Khayr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas. And Sufyan said another time: Ikrimah informed me, he said: When Abu Sufyan turned back from Uhud and they reached ar-Rawha, they said: You neither killed Muhammad nor took the maidens as followers; evil is what you did. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called the people and they responded until they reached Hamra al-Asad or the well of Abi Inabah. So Allah - Mighty and Exalted - revealed: Those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after injury befell them. And Abu Sufyan had said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your appointment is the season of Badr where you killed our companions. As for the coward, he returned, and as for the brave, he took the equipment of fighting and trade. So they came to it and found no one there, and they traded. So Allah Almighty revealed: So they returned with favor from Allah and bounty, no evil touching them. An-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz, similarly. The wording of Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz; and in the narration of Yahya ibn Said and his companions: your appointment; and with him: the equipment of fighting; and with him: so they traded."
"4484","Another 211 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Sulayman al-Jammal narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Huyayy ibn Akhtab and Kab ibn al-Ashraf came to Makkah to Quraysh and allied with them to fight the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they said to them: You are the people of ancient knowledge and the people of the Book, so inform us about us and about Muhammad. They said: What are you? And what is Muhammad? They said: We slaughter the noble camels, and give milk over water, and free the captives, and give drink to the pilgrims, and join kinships. They said: What is Muhammad? They said: A rootless one who severed our kinships, and the thieves of the pilgrims, Banu Ghifar, followed him. They said: Rather you are better than him and more guided in way. So Allah Almighty revealed: Have you not seen those given a portion of the Book believing in Jibt and Taghut, to the end of the verse."
"4485","Another 212 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad at-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali made Fatimah lawful with an iron armor."
"4486","Another 213 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came from a journey, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you stay with so-and-so woman and enter upon her. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that."
"4487","Another 214 - And with the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: A man asked Ibn Abbas: What suffices for ghusl? He said: A sa, and a mudd for wudu. A man said: It does not suffice me. He said: May you have no mother, it suffices one better than you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It has a corroboration in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jabr, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bathe with the sa and perform wudu with the mudd. And in Muslim from the hadith of Safinah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a sa of water would suffice him to wash from janabah, and a mudd would suffice him for wudu. And he has nothing in the Sahih but it."
"4488","215 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani - there - informed us, that Said ibn Abi ar-Raja informed them - recited to him, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There were people of Makkah who had become Muslim, and they would conceal their Islam; then the polytheists brought them out with them on the day of Badr. He said: Some of them were struck. So the Muslims said: These companions of ours were Muslims and were coerced, so seek forgiveness for them. So this verse was revealed about them: Indeed those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves, to its end. So he wrote with this verse to those remaining of the Muslims in Makkah, that they have no excuse. So they went out, and the polytheists caught up with them and they gave them apostasy. And this verse was revealed about them: And of people is he who says: We believe in Allah, then when he is harmed in Allah he makes the trial of people like the punishment of Allah. And he wrote to them, so they grieved and despaired of all good. Then it was revealed about them: Then indeed your Lord, for those who emigrated after they were tried, to its end. So they wrote to them with that: Allah has made for you a way out, so go out. Then the polytheists caught up with them and fought them until whoever was saved was saved, and whoever was killed was killed. And there was a man of Banu Bakr, called Damrah, and he was ill, so he said to his family: Take me out of Makkah, for I feel the heat. They said: Where shall we take you? So he gestured with his hand toward the road of Madinah. So they took him out, and he died two miles from Makkah. So this verse was revealed: And whoever goes out of his house emigrating to Allah and His Messenger, then death overtakes him."
"4489","216 - And the Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi ar-Raja al-Hanbali - at Isfahan - informed us, that Masud ibn al-Hasan ath-Thaqafi informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman adh-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: And there was a man in Makkah of Banu Bakr, called Damrah, and he was ill. So he said to his family: Take me out of Makkah, for I feel the heat. His family said: Where shall we take you? So he gestured with his hand: Madinah. So they took him out, and he died two miles from Makkah. So this verse was revealed about him: And whoever goes out of his house emigrating to Allah and His Messenger. As for His saying: Indeed those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves, al-Bukhari brought it similarly."
"4490","Another 217 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ath-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Khallal informed them, Abu al-Fadl Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ahmad ar-Razi informed us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us - at Makkah - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ad-Daybuli narrated to us, Abu Ubayd Allah Said ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - regarding His saying: And cups that were crystal, crystal of silver. He said: Had you taken of the silver of the people of this world and fashioned it until it becomes like the wing of a fly, you would not see water through it; but the crystal of Paradise is in the whiteness of silver with the clarity of crystal."
"4491","218 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir ash-Shahhami informed them, Abu Nasr Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Musa informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad as-Saliti informed us, Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Hamdawayh ibn Sahl narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Had I taken silver of the silver of this world and worked it until you make it like the wing of a fly, you would not see through it; but the crystal of Paradise is like the whiteness of silver with the clarity of crystal."
"4492","Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Hamdani as-Sabii from Ikrimah 219 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd ar-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You have turned grey, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes, Hud and its sisters turned me grey. At-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Muawiyah ibn Hisham, from Shayban, and said: A hasan gharib hadith we know from the hadith of Ibn Abbas only from this face. Ali ibn Salih narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, similarly. And something of this was narrated from Abu Ishaq from Abu Maysarah, mursal. Ad-Daraqutni mentioned it and mentioned this chain and others, and mentioned much disagreement in it."
"4493","Amr ibn Abi Amr, and the name of Abu Amr is Maysarah, freedman of al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Ikrimah 220 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi - there - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them, Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Ismail ad-Dabbi informed us, the judge Abu Said al-Khalil ibn Ahmad as-Sijzi informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ath-Thaqafi as-Sarraj informed us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."
"4494","221 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find lying with a beast, kill him and kill the beast with him. It was said to Ibn Abbas: What is with the beast?! He said: I heard nothing from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that; but I deem that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that its meat be eaten or benefited from, while that deed was done with it."
"4495","222 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid ath-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find lying with a beast, kill him and kill the beast."
"4496","223 - And with the preceding chain, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done - and both are one hadith. Imam Ahmad narrated it, its beginning from Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i, from Abd al-Aziz. And the mention of the beast was narrated from Abd al-Wahhab, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, with its meaning. And from Abu Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Amr; and in neither of them is the statement of Ibn Abbas. And Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Nufayli, from al-Darawardi Abd al-Aziz. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr al-Sawwaq, from Abd al-Aziz, and said: We know it only from the hadith of Amr and Ikrimah. And Sufyan narrated from Asim, from Abu Razin, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Whoever approaches a beast, there is nothing upon him; Ibn Bashshar narrated that to us, from Ibn Mahdi, from al-Thawri, and this is more authentic. And al-Nasai narrated: whoever approaches a beast, from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah and Abu Bakr ibn Khallad, from Abd al-Aziz - and he did not mention the beast."
"4497","Another, 224 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah - he is al-Qa'nabi - narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 225 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr ibn Muhammad - at Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that a man clung to his debtor for ten dinars, and said to him: By Allah, I have no repayment with which to pay you today. He said: By Allah, I shall not leave you until you pay me or bring a guarantor who guarantees for you. He said: By Allah, I have no repayment, and I find no one to guarantee for me. He said: So he dragged him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this man clung to me and I asked him for one month's respite, but he refused unless I pay him or bring him a guarantor; so I said: By Allah, I find no guarantor, and I have no repayment today. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall we grant him respite for only one month? He said: No. He said: Then I shall guarantee it for you - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guaranteed it. Then the man went and brought him the amount he had promised him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From where did you get this gold? He said: From a mine. He said: Then go, for we have no need of it, and there is no good in it - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid it off for him. The wording is that of Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz. And in the narration of Isma'il ibn Abdillah: ...he said: By Allah, I have nothing with which to pay you today - and with him: or you bring me a guarantor who guarantees for you; he said: By Allah - and with him: I said: By Allah, I find no guarantor - and with him: Then I shall guarantee it for you - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guaranteed it - and with him: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: From where did you get this? He said: From a mine. He said: Go, for we have no need of it; there is no good in it - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid it off for him. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Qa'nabi. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad."
"4498","Another, 226 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: I used to hear the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house while I was in the chamber."
"4499","227 - And Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, who said: The recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night was at a volume that one in the chamber could hear while he was in the house."
"4500","228 - And Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at a volume that one in the chamber could hear. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it in al-Shama'il from al-Darimi, from Yahya ibn Hassan, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad. I say: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad was criticized by some of them, while Malik ibn Anas deemed him trustworthy."
"4501","Another, 229 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them, Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us, al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sarraj informed us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah: that a group of the people of Iraq said to Ibn Abbas: What do you think about this verse, in which we were commanded what we were commanded, yet no one acts upon it - the statement of Allah, mighty and majestic: O you who believe, let those whom your right hands possess and those who have not reached puberty among you ask your permission three times, before the dawn prayer - to the end of the verse. So Ibn Abbas said: Indeed Allah - mighty and majestic - is gentle, forbearing, compassionate, merciful to the believers, and loves concealment. And people had no curtains or veils for their houses, so sometimes the servant or the child or the man would enter upon his family, so Allah - mighty and majestic - commanded them to seek permission at those private times. Then Allah brought them covering and good, yet I do not see anyone acting upon that."
"4502","230 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them, Ahmad al-Dhakwani informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Haytham al-Muqri' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Maslamah and Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah: that a group of the people of Iraq asked Ibn Abbas, saying: O Ibn Abbas, what do you think about this verse which Allah commanded us with what He commanded, yet no one acts upon it - the statement of Allah: O you who believe, let those whom your right hands possess ask your permission - to His statement: some of you from others. And Ibn Abbas said: Indeed Allah is gentle, merciful to the believers, and loves concealment. And people had no coverings or coarse cloths for their houses - in the narration of al-Zubayri; as for al-Qa'nabi, he said: nor veils - so sometimes the servant would enter the house, or his orphan, and the man upon his family, so Allah commanded them to seek permission at those private times. Then Allah brought them coverings and good, yet I do not see anyone acting upon that. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Qa'nabi, from Abd al-Aziz, similarly."
"4503","Another, 231 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - [transmission break; the text of the report is not given here]."
"4504","232 - And Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - [transmission break; the text of the report is not given here]."
"4505","233 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - [transmission break; the text of the report is not given here]."
"4506","234 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us that Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Fudayli informed them, Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us, al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sarraj informed us, Qutaybah - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib ibn Abdillah ibn Hantab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed whoever takes allegiance to other than his patrons, and Allah has cursed whoever changes the landmarks of the land, and Allah has cursed whoever leads a blind man astray from the path, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut. The wording is that of the hadith of Qutaybah. And in the narration of Sulayman ibn Bilal: 'Allah has cursed' throughout without the conjunction waw; and with him: Allah has cursed whoever leads a blind man astray from the road, Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and Allah has cursed whoever falls upon a beast, Allah has cursed whoever disobeys his parents, Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut - he said it three times. And the narration of Zuhayr ibn Muhammad: He said: Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and Allah has cursed whoever changes the landmarks of the land, and Allah has cursed whoever reviles his parents, and Allah has cursed whoever takes allegiance to other than his patrons, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut - he said it three times, meaning 'the deed of the people of Lut.' And the narration of Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Ibn Abi al-Zinad and al-Darawardi: He said: Allah has cursed whoever changes his patrons, Allah has cursed whoever changes the landmarks of the land, Allah has cursed whoever leads a blind man astray from the road, and Allah has cursed whoever curses his parents, and Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and Allah has cursed whoever falls upon a beast, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut."
"4507","235 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdillah - known as Sammawayh - informed us, Abdillah - he is al-Qa'nabi - narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz - meaning al-Darawardi - narrated to us, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed whoever takes allegiance to other than his patrons, and Allah has cursed whoever curses his parents, and Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah the Exalted, and Allah has cursed whoever changes the landmarks of the land, and Allah has cursed whoever leads a blind man astray from the path, and Allah has cursed whoever falls upon a beast, and Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad; and from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Ibn Ishaq; and from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq; and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Zuhayr - all of them from Amr - and in the narration of Zuhayr, 'whoever falls upon a beast' was not mentioned. And al-Nasai narrated it from Qutaybah, similarly. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"4508","Another, 236 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Jarbadhaqani informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them - recited to him while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdan al-Saffar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shadha al-Jawhari narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about this verse: Do not expel them from their houses, nor let them leave, except that they commit a clear indecency. He said: The clear indecency is that the woman behaves insolently toward the husband's family and harms them."
"4509","Qatadah ibn Di'amah al-Sadusi from Ikrimah, 237 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-mujaththamah and al-jallalah, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"4510","238 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the milk of the jallalah, and al-mujaththamah, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"4511","239 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed her, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-mujaththamah and al-jallalah and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Qatadah; and from Abd al-Samad, from Hisham - and in it: the milk of the jallalah; and from Abd al-Samad, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, likewise. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa, from Hammad, from Qatadah. And he also narrated the prohibition of the milk of the jallalah - from Muhammad ibn Muthanna, from Abu Amir, from Hisham, from Qatadah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father; and from Ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Sa'id - and said: a hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasai narrated it from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Hisham - and said: the milk of the jallalah instead of riding it. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Khallad al-Bahili, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi, from Sa'id, from Qatadah - and with him: the milk of the jallalah. As for drinking from the mouth of the waterskin, al-Bukhari narrated it from the narration of Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Ikrimah."
"4512","Another, 240 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Dharr al-Salihani informed them, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 241 - Ibn Abi Asim said: And Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad - meaning Ghundar - narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 242 - He said: And Bundar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The molars are equal. Abu Dawud narrated: The fingers are equal and the teeth are equal - from Abbas al-Anbari, from Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith; and from Abdillah al-Darimi, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl - both from Shu'bah. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abbas al-Anbari with his chain: The teeth are equal, the front tooth and the molar are equal. And Yazid al-Nahwi narrated it from Ikrimah; it will come, Allah willing, in his biography."
"4513","Another, 243 - Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Muflih ibn Ahmad al-Dumi informed them, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani informed us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, that Ikrimah narrated to him, that Ibn Abbas said: It was affirmed for the pregnant woman and the nursing mother. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it in his chapter: And upon those who can fast it, a ransom. And al-Bukhari narrated from the hadith of Ata', from Ibn Abbas: And upon those who are burdened by it, a ransom of feeding a poor person - Ibn Abbas said: It is not abrogated; it is for the very old man and the very old woman who cannot fast, so they feed a poor person for each day."
"4514","Another, 244 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"4515","245 - And Abu al-Fath Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi informed us - in his letter - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us, Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim - he is Ibn Tahman - narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two rams each. Thus al-Nasai narrated it."
"4516","246 - Another: Abu Ahmad Abdillah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Uqbah ibn Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that his sister had vowed to walk to the House. He said: Command your sister to ride and to offer a sacrificial camel."
"4517","247 - And with the preceding chain, my father narrated to me, Bahz narrated to us, Hammam informed us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Uqbah ibn Amir asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: His sister vowed to walk to the House, and he complained to him of her weakness. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel."
"4518","248 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to perform Hajj on foot, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, and he said: Indeed Allah - mighty and majestic - is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel."
"4519","249 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us. 250 - Al-Tabarani said: And Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, both saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Uqbah ibn Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: His sister vowed to walk to the House. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel."
"4520","251 - Al-Tabarani said: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to walk, and he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan and Abd al-Samad, from Hammam. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, and from Ibn al-Muthanna, from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, from Hammam. And he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated similarly, and Khalid from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah, so she commanded me to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling, and he said: Let her walk and let her ride."
"4521","Another, 252 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, present, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Are you surprised that intimate friendship should be for Ibrahim, and speech for Musa, and the Vision for Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Mu'adh."
"4522","Another, 253 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Qatadah narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 254 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - and the statement of Abu Dharr: Then He revealed to His servant what He revealed - both said: His servant is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The wording is one. Al-Nasai narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Abbas alone, from Yazid ibn Sinan al-Basri, resident of Egypt, from Mu'adh."
"4523","Another, 255 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu al-Fath Isma'il ibn al-Fadl al-Sarraj informed them - while he was present - Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Thabit ibn Qays concerning the case of Jamilah bint Salul: Take your garden from her, and do not take more. What is meant by it: and do not take more."
"4524","Another, 256 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw my Lord, blessed and exalted. And I heard this hadith from my father; he dictated it to me in another place."
"4525","257 - And with the preceding chain, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw my Lord, blessed and exalted."
"4526","258 - And Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I saw my Lord - then he mentioned his speech."
"4527","259 - And with the preceding chain, Ahmad ibn Abi Asim informed us, Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I saw my Lord, mighty and majestic."
"4528","260 - And my maternal uncle, the learned Imam Abu Muhammad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Hibatullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Hilal al-Daqqaq informed them - at Baghdad - Abdillah ibn Ali, known as Ibn Zakariyya al-Daqqaq, informed us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bishran informed us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz informed us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I have indeed seen my Lord. Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, saying: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah saying: I heard Abu Zur'ah al-Razi saying: The hadith of Qatadah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas concerning the Vision is authentic; Shadhan and Abd al-Samad ibn Kaysan and Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd narrated it, and none denies it except a Mu'tazili."
"4529","Another, 261 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi informed us - by license - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasai informed us, Amr ibn Ali informed us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The fingers are ten by ten. It is halted; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is not mentioned in it. It is mentioned in al-Bukhari from the narration of Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one and this one are equal - meaning the little finger and the thumb."
"4530","Another, 262 - Abu Abdillah Isma'il ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Wakkas al-Qattan informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Kinani narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 263 - And Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, the judge Abu Ya'la Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Farra' informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, both saying: Mu'adh ibn Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - that a man came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I am a very old man for whom standing is hard, so command me a night in which Allah - mighty and majestic - may grant me success in Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Keep to the seventh."
"4531","264 - And Abu Ali Diya' ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali ibn al-Khurayf informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Aziz ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati al-Harbi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abu Abdillah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal ibn Asad al-Shaybani and Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, both saying: Mu'adh ibn Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I am a very old man for whom standing is hard, so command me a night in which Allah may grant me success in Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Keep to the seventh. And this is the wording of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, may Allah be pleased with him. Thus Imam Ahmad narrated it in al-Musnad, with the addition: a very old, sick man for whom standing is hard, so command me a night."
"4532","Another, 265 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The husband of Barirah was a black slave called Mughith. Ibn Abbas said: I used to see him in the streets of Madinah wringing his eyes; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning her four rulings: her masters had stipulated the wala' for themselves, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the wala' belongs to the one who frees; and he gave her the choice, so she chose herself; and he commanded her to observe the waiting period; and charity was given to her, so she gifted some of it to A'ishah, so A'ishah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her, and a gift for us."
"4533","266 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wala' belongs to the one who frees; and meat was given in charity to Barirah, so she gifted some of it to A'ishah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her and a gift for us. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam."
"4534","267 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the husband of Barirah was a black slave named Mughith. He said: I used to see him following her in the streets of Madinah, wringing his eyes over her. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave four rulings concerning her: that her masters had stipulated the wala', so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled the wala' for the one who frees; and he gave her the choice, so she chose herself, and he commanded her to observe the waiting period. He said: And charity was given to her, so she gifted some of it to A'ishah, and she mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: It is charity for her, and a gift to us. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Bahz. And Abu Dawud narrated from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Affan with his chain, that the husband of Barirah was a black slave named Mughith, so he gave her the choice - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and commanded her to observe the waiting period. We mentioned earlier that in the Sahih there is mention of Barirah and her husband, and in this there is the added mention of the rulings."
"4535","Another, 268 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us. [Transmission break.] 269 - And Abu Tahir al-Khadir ibn Hibatullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Tawus informed us - at Damascus - that Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, saying: It was recited to the judge Abu Bakr Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayanji - while I was present hearing - it was said to him: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed you - recited to him - Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you change grey hair with is henna and katam."
"4536","Another, 270 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I saw the Dajjal, white and of fair complexion, huge, elephantine - that is, enormous in body - as though the hair of his head were the branches of a tree, one-eyed, as though his eye were the morning star; I liken him to Abd al-Uzza, a man of Khuza'ah."
"4537","Another, 271 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa' al-Aquli informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Khayrun informed them, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah informed us, saying: It was recited to the chief Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn al-Wazir Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah - while I was listening - saying: It was recited to Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, saying: Hammam was asked about the statement of Allah, mighty and majestic: Mankind was one nation - so Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: They were all upon Islam."
"4538","272 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His statement, mighty and majestic: Mankind was one nation - he said: All upon Islam."
"4539","273 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - concerning His statement: Mankind was one nation - he said: Upon Islam."
"4540","274 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Da'laj narrated to us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 275 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, both saying: Shayban narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: All of them upon Islam - concerning His statement: Mankind was one nation, then Allah sent the prophets as bearers of glad tidings and warners."
"4541","Another, 276 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Da'laj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - And We know those of you who went before, and We know those who come later - he said: Those who went before: Adam and those who passed; and those who come later: those in the loins of men."
"4542","Another, 277 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'dan narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harun Shayta narrated to us, Sawrah ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Shayban al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - We know what We have enjoined upon them concerning their wives. He said: He enjoined upon them that there be no marriage except with a guardian and witnesses and a dowry. And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim said: He said: Indeed Allah enjoined upon them."
"4543","Qaza'ah, freedman of Abd al-Qays, from Ikrimah, 278 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad informed me, that Qaza'ah, freedman of Abd al-Qays, informed him, that he heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: Ibn Abbas said: I prayed beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with A'ishah behind us praying with us, while I was beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying with him."
"4544","279 - And Abu Ali Abdillah [...] ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad - meaning Ibn Sa'd - informed us, that Qaza'ah, freedman of Abd al-Qays, informed him, that he heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I prayed beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with A'ishah behind us praying with us, while I was beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying with him. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Hajjaj, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, similarly."
"4545","Mubarak Abu Amr - it is said he is al-Khayyat al-Basri - from Ikrimah, 280 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Mubarak Abu Amr narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet, who said: Whoever dies with the smell of fadikh wine in his belly, Allah will disgrace him before all witnesses on the Day of Resurrection. Mubarak Abu Amr: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him and mentioned no criticism of him, and said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi and Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated from him."
"4546","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Aswad or another from Ikrimah, 281 - Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Makki al-Asbahani informed us - there - that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad - he is Ibn Ibrahim - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Humayd narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, and every alliance in the Jahiliyyah has only been strengthened by Islam; and it would not please me to have red camels if I broke the alliance that was in Dar al-Nadwah."
"4547","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rukanah from Ikrimah, 282 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rukanah informed me, Ikrimah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix a hadd for wine. Ibn Abbas said: And a man drank an intoxicant and was found swaying in a mountain pass, so he was taken to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he came opposite the house of al-Abbas, he slipped away and entered to al-Abbas and clung to him. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he laughed and said: Has he done it! And he did not ask about him."
"4548","283 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah informed me, saying: Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give a ruling of a hadd for wine. Ibn Abbas said: So a man drank and became drunk, and was found swaying in the mountain pass, so he was taken to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he came opposite the house of al-Abbas, he slipped away and entered to al-Abbas and clung to him. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he laughed and said: Has he done it! Then he did not command anything concerning him."
"4549","284 - And Abu Tahir and Abu Ahmad informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give a ruling of a hadd for wine. Ibn Abbas said: A man drank and became drunk, and was found swaying in a mountain pass, so he was taken to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he came abreast of the house of al-Abbas, he slipped away and entered to Abbas and clung to him from behind. That was mentioned to the Prophet, so he laughed and said: He has indeed done it! Then he did not command them anything concerning him. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abu Asim, similarly."
"4550","Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, from Ikrimah, 285 - Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Hafiz informed us - at Isfahan - that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, that he narrated to him, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Abu Bakr said to Finhas - who was among the scholars and rabbis of the Jews: Fear Allah and accept Islam, for by Allah, you know that Muhammad is a messenger from Allah; he has come to you with the truth from Him, which you find written with you in the Torah and the Gospel. Finhas said: By Allah, O Abu Bakr, we did not ask Allah out of poverty, while He is poor toward us; and we do not humble ourselves to Him as He humbles Himself to us; and indeed we are rich; and had He been independent of us, He would not have borrowed our wealth as your companion claims - he forbids us usury yet gives it to us; and had He been independent of us, He would not have given us usury. So Abu Bakr became angry and struck the face of Finhas. Then Finhas informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: What carried you to what you did to Finhas? So he informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what he had said. Then he stood and Finhas denied, saying: I did not say that to you. So Allah revealed: Allah has heard the statement of those who said: Indeed Allah is poor and we are rich - to His statement - the punishment of the Blaze. It was revealed concerning Abu Bakr and what he did thereof out of his anger."
"4551","Another, 286 - And with the preceding chain, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, that he narrated to him, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Those who rejoice in what they attain of the world - like what they adorned for people of misguidance - and love to be praised for what they did not do - that people say of them: a scholar, while they are not people of knowledge; they did not carry them upon guidance nor upon good; and they love that people say: they did - while they did not do."
"4552","Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami from Ikrimah, 287 - Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Babasri informed us - at Bab al-Basrah of Baghdad - that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, saying: Ikrimah narrated to me that he saw Ibn Abbas wearing the waist-wrapper, placing the front edge of his wrapper over the back of his feet and raising it from behind. I said: Why do you wear the wrapper in this manner? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing it thus. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ali ibn Shu'ayb, from Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad, from Muhammad, similarly."
"4553","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - and it is said: Ibn Maysarah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qadi Abu Amr al-Qurashi, father of Asbat - from Ikrimah, 288 - The Imam Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Hamad ibn Hamid al-Artahi informed us - at Egypt - that Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Umar al-Farra' al-Mawsili authorized for them, Abu Zakariyya Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Bukhari informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Mughni ibn Sa'id ibn Ali al-Azdi al-Maliki informed us, Abu Ja'far Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ayyub Abu al-Bishr narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - concerning the statement of Allah, mighty and majestic: Indeed the companions of Paradise this Day are busy, rejoicing - he said: The deflowering of virgins."
"4554","289 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them, Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Misri narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - concerning His statement: Indeed the companions of Paradise this Day are busy, rejoicing - he said: The deflowering of virgins."
"4555","Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri from Ikrimah, 290 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Busri narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Hani' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, saying: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Nus'ah was a clan of Banu Malik ibn Kinanah, of Banu Fuqaym; the last of them was a man called al-Qalammas, and he was the one who postponed al-Muharram, and he was a king. He would declare al-Muharram lawful one year and forbid it the next year; when he forbade it, there were three consecutive months: Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and al-Muharram - which is the number Allah forbade in the covenant of Ibrahim, peace be upon him. And when he declared it lawful, Safar entered in place of al-Muharram to match the number, saying: I have completed the four as they were, for I did not declare a month lawful except that I forbade another month in its place. So the Arabs who owed allegiance to al-Qalammas for his kingship remained upon that, until Allah sent Muhammad, peace be upon him, and he completed al-Muharram as three consecutive months, and Rajab, the month of Mudar which is between Jumada and Sha'ban. Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Indeed the number of months with Allah is twelve months in the Book of Allah on the day He created the heavens and the earth, of them four are sacred; that is the upright religion, so do not wrong yourselves therein - do not make the unlawful lawful, nor the lawful unlawful, as the people of shirk used to do. Then He explained to them, saying: Postponement is only an increase in disbelief by which those who disbelieve are led astray. They declare it lawful one year and forbid it one year, to match the number of what Allah forbade, so they declare lawful what Allah forbade; the evil of their deeds was adorned for them, and Allah does not guide the disbelieving people."
"4556","Mujahid ibn Jabr al-Makki from Ikrimah, 291 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran narrated to us, Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid - that he heard Ikrimah, who heard Ibn Abbas saying: When there was revealed: And whoever seeks other than Islam as religion - to the end of the verse - the Jews said: Then we are Muslims. So Allah said to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Dispute with them, saying: Refute them. He said: So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And pilgrimage to the House is due to Allah from people, whoever can find a way to it; and whoever disbelieves - of the people of the creeds - then Allah is independent of the worlds. Allah said to His Prophet: Say to them that Allah has enjoined upon the Muslims pilgrimage to the House, but they refused and said: Pilgrimage is not upon us."
"4557","Matar ibn Tahman al-Khurasani Abu Raja' al-Warraq from Ikrimah, 292 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Harith Abu Qudamah narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq - or a man - from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prostrate in any of the Mufassal after he moved to Madinah."
"4558","293 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 294 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Balkhi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi' al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Qudamah al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prostrate in any of the Mufassal since he moved to Madinah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi'. Abu Qudamah was criticized by more than one of the Imams, though Muslim narrated from him in his Sahih. And Azhar ibn al-Qasim was deemed trustworthy by Ahmad ibn Hanbal; and Abu Hatim al-Razi said: His hadith is written but not used as proof. Perhaps Ibn Abbas did not see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in Madinah - and Allah knows best - for it is narrated in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in When the sky splits open, while Abu Hurayrah only accepted Islam after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah."
"4559","Musa ibn Muslim al-Saghir Abu Isa al-Tahhan from Ikrimah, 295 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Muslim al-Tahhan al-Saghir narrated to us, saying: I heard Ikrimah raising the hadith - as I recall, to Ibn Abbas - saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves snakes out of fear of seeking them out is not of us; we have not made peace with them since we warred against them."
"4560","296 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muslim, saying: I heard Ikrimah raising the hadith, as I recall, to Ibn Abbas, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves snakes out of fear of seeking them out is not of us. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ibn Numayr, similarly."
"4561","Maysarah ibn Uthman - and Ibn Abi Hatim said: Ibn Ammar; and it is said: Ibn Tammam al-Ashja'i al-Kufi - from Ikrimah, 297 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Isa ibn Muslim al-Hamdani narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Uthman al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Khadijah, Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: O Muhammad, convey my greeting of peace to Khadijah, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearls, in which there is no noise nor toil. Isa ibn Muslim Abu Dawud al-Tuhawi: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not strong; and Abu Zur'ah said: Lenient - yet it has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa."
"4562","Al-Nadr ibn Arabi al-Amiri from Ikrimah, 298 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The number of the people of Badr was the number of the companions of Talut; they were three hundred and thirteen men. It has a witness in al-Bukhari from the hadith of al-Bara' ibn Azib."
"4563","Nuh ibn Rabi'ah, freedman of the Ansar, Abu Makin al-Basri, from Ikrimah, 299 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - as I recall - that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him while he was present - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Dahhak al-Shaybani informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Safwan ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Abu Makin, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar and said to him: Do you desire anything? He said: Yes, bread. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people: Whoever has any bread with him, let him bring it. So a man came with a morsel and fed it to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sick one of you desires something, feed it to him. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali, and in it: wheat bread."
"4564","Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qardusi from Ikrimah, 300 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his coat of mail was pawned with a Jewish man for twenty sa' of barley which he had taken as food for his family."
"4565","301 - And Abu Abdillah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi and others informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Mu'allim informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us. [Transmission break.] 302 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to me, my father - both saying: Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken while his coat of mail was pawned for thirty sa' of barley which he had taken as provision for his dependents. The wording is that of Ibn Mani'. And in the narration of Imam Ahmad: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken while his coat of mail was pawned with a Jewish man for thirty sa' of barley which he had taken as provision for his dependents."
"4566","303 - And Shahdah bint Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Abari informed us - in her letter to us - and my maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us from her - it was said to her: Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baqillani informed you, saying: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us, Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ziyad al-Qattan al-Mattuthi informed us, Abu Ishaq Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi and Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his coat of mail was pawned with a Jew for twenty sa' of food which he had taken for his family. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Hisham, and in it: for thirty sa'. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, saying: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasai narrated it from Yusuf ibn Hammad, from Sufyan ibn Habib, from Hisham with his chain, with the wording: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his coat of mail was pawned with a Jew for thirty sa' of barley for his family. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of al-Aswad from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought food from a Jew on credit and pawned to him a coat of mail of iron - except that some of them said: thirty, and some said: twenty."
"4567","Another, 304 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Dhari' narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 305 - Al-Tabarani said: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Zakariyya al-Sarimi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, loves that His concessions be taken just as He loves that His strict obligations be taken. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa, from al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Dhari'."
"4568","Another, 306 - And with the preceding chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Zakariyya al-Sarimi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the overwhelming of debt, and the overwhelming of the enemy, and from the ruin of the unmarried woman, and from the trial of the Dajjal. Abbad ibn Zakariyya: I saw no mention of him in the book of Ibn Abi Hatim. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa, from al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Zari', from Abu Mihsan Husayn ibn Numayr, from Hisham."
"4569","Another, 307 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us, al-Ansari narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - concerning His statement: He does not utter a word except that with him is an observer ready - he said: O boy, saddle the horse, give water to drink - nothing is written except good and evil."
"4570","Hilal ibn Khabbab al-Abdi from Ikrimah, 308 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Thabit - meaning Ibn Yazid - narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend consecutive nights hungry with his stomach empty, while his family found no supper. He said: And most of their bread was barley bread."
"4571","309 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend consecutive nights hungry with his stomach empty while his family found no supper. He said: And most of their bread was barley bread. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa, from Thabit. And al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah both narrated it from Abdillah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi, from Thabit ibn Yazid. And al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih hadith. Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd al-Ahwal was deemed trustworthy by Ibn Ma'in."
"4572","Another, 310 - And with the preceding chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya - companion of al-Basri - narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 311 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn al-Kumayt narrated to us, saying: And Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, both saying: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, both saying: Thabit ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month in all the prayers: Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha."
"4573","312 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz al-Harawi informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, saying: My grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us - may Allah have mercy on him - Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd al-Ahwal narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a consecutive month. [Transmission break.]"
"4574","313 - And Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a consecutive month in Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr, at the end of every prayer when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him - from the last rak'ah - supplicating against them: against a clan of Banu Sulaym, against Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Usayyah - while those behind him said amen. He had sent to them calling them to Islam, but they killed them. Affan said in his hadith: He said: And Ikrimah said: This was the beginning of qunut. The wording is one, except that in the narration of Muhammad ibn Yahya: supplicating against a clan - and with him: He said: He sent to them calling them to Islam, but they killed them; Ikrimah said: This is the beginning of qunut. Thus Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih. And Abu Dawud narrated it - up to his statement: while those behind him said amen - from Abdillah ibn Mu'awiyah, from Thabit."
"4575","Another, 314 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Hilal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas. [Transmission break; the text of the report is not given here.]"
"4576","315 - And Abu Ahmad Abdillah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad and Hasan - he is Ibn Musa - narrated to us, both saying: Thabit narrated to us. Hasan said: Abu Zayd. Abd al-Samad said: Hilal narrated to us; Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis, then he came in his night and informed them of his journey, and of the sign of Bayt al-Maqdis and their caravan. So some people said - Hasan said: Do we believe Muhammad in what he says! So they apostatized as disbelievers, and Allah struck their necks along with Abu Jahl. And Abu Jahl said: Muhammad frightens us with the tree of Zaqqum; bring dates and butter, and gorge yourselves. And he saw the Dajjal in his form with the vision of the eye, not the vision of sleep; and Isa, Musa, and Ibrahim, the blessings of Allah upon them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Dajjal, and he said: White and fair-complexioned. Hasan said: I saw him, elephantine, white and fair-complexioned; one of his eyes standing as though it were a brilliant star, as though the hair of his head were the branches of a tree. And I saw Isa, a young man, white, curly-haired, sharp-sighted, compact in build. And I saw Musa, peace be upon him, dark-skinned, brown, with abundant hair - Hasan said: hair - strongly built. And I looked at Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and I did not look at any limb of his limbs except that I looked at it from myself as though he were your companion (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Greet Malik, peace be upon him - so I greeted him. The wording is that of the narration of Imam Ahmad. And in the narration of Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr, he said: Some people said: We believe Muhammad - so they apostatized as disbelievers. And with him: without the fa' in 'gorge yourselves'; and with him: vision of the eye; and with him: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Dajjal, and he said: I saw him, elephantine, white and fair-complexioned; and in the description of Isa: shapely in build; in the description of Musa: abundant in hair. And with him: And I saw Ibrahim, and I did not look at any limb of his limbs except that I looked as though he were your companion. And with him: He said: Jibril said to me. And the rest is like it. Al-Nasai narrated it - of it the statement of Abu Jahl - from Abu Dawud al-Harrani, from Arim, from Thabit. There is mentioned in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ibn Abbas the mention of the prophets and their descriptions, and the mention of the Dajjal; and in what we mentioned is other than what is mentioned in the two Sahihs."
"4577","Another, 316 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak and Abu Ahmad Abdillah informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Uhud and said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it would not please me that Uhud were gold for the family of Muhammad which I spend in the path of Allah, then I die the day I die while with me are two dinars - unless I set them aside for a debt. He said: So he died and left neither dinar nor dirham, nor slave nor slave-girl, and left his coat of mail pawned with a Jew for thirty sa' of barley."
"4578","317 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Uhud and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it would not please me that Uhud were transformed into gold for the family of Muhammad which I spend in the path of Allah, then I die the day I die leaving of it two dinars - except two dinars I set aside for a debt, if there is a debt upon me."
"4579","318 - And with the preceding chain, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, nor slave nor slave-girl, and left his coat of mail pawned with a Jew for thirty sa' of barley. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan and Abu Sa'id, from Thabit. And Ibn Majah narrated from it the pawning of the coat of mail, from Abdillah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi, from Thabit ibn Yazid."
"4580","Another, 319 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When there was revealed: When the help of Allah comes and the conquest - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Fatimah and said: My death has been announced to me - so she wept. Then he said to her: Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me - so she laughed. Then one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw her and said to her: We saw you weep then laugh. She said: He said to me: My death has been announced to me - so I wept; then he said: Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me - so I laughed."
"4581","320 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When there was revealed: When the help of Allah comes and the conquest - to the end of the surah - he said: His death was announced to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it was revealed. He said: So he exerted himself most intensely ever in the matter of the Hereafter. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thereafter: The conquest has come, and the help of Allah, and the people of Yemen have come. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and who are the people of Yemen? He said: A people whose hearts are tender, soft-hearted; faith is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni. The mention of the weeping of Fatimah and her laughter, and his statement, peace be upon him: You are the first of my family to join me - has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of A'ishah from Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"4582","Another, 321 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought an enemy and did not finish with them until he delayed Asr past its time. When he saw that, he said: O Allah, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, and fill their graves with fire - or something like that."
"4583","322 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu al-Qasim al-Qushayri and Abu Bakr al-Maghribi informed us, both saying: Abu al-Husayn al-Khaffaf informed us, Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us, Ali ibn Muslim narrated to me, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a campaign when the polytheists detained him from Zuhr and Asr until he combined them at dusk. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, fill their bellies and their graves with fire as they detained us from the middle prayer."
"4584","323 - And with the preceding chain, Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Thabit - he is Abu Zayd - narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought an enemy of his and did not finish until [...] Asr past its time. When he looked and saw that, he said: O Allah, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their houses and their graves with fire, and fill their hearts with fire - or something like that."
"4585","324 - And Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on a campaign and did not finish with them until he delayed Asr past the time he used to guard. When he finished with them, he looked, and Asr had indeed been delayed to dusk, so he prayed; and when he finished his prayer, he supplicated against his enemy, saying: O Allah, whoever busied us away from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, and fill their bellies with fire, and fill their graves with fire. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4586","Another, 325 - Abu Ja'far al-Asbahani informed us - there - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar ibn al-Khattab entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon a mat that had left marks on his side. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you took a bedding softer than this. He said: What have I to do with the world, and what has the world to do with me! By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of the world is only that of a rider who journeyed on a hot day and shaded himself under a tree for an hour of the day, then journeyed on and left it."
"4587","326 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad, Abu Sa'id, and Affan narrated to us, all saying: Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon a mat that had left marks on his side. He said: O Prophet of Allah, if only you took a bedding softer than this. He said: What have I to do with the world! My likeness and the likeness of the world is only that of a rider who journeyed on a hot day and shaded himself under a tree for an hour of the day, then departed and left it."
"4588","Another, 327 - And with the preceding chain, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad and Hasan narrated to us, both saying: Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, that Ikrimah was asked. Hasan said: I asked Ikrimah about the fasting one cupping, and he said: It was only disliked on account of weakness. And he narrated from Ibn Abbas. Hasan said: Then he narrated from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram, on account of a morsel he had eaten of a poisoned sheep which a woman of the people of Khaybar had poisoned. As for cupping, it has been narrated in the Sahih from the narration of Ibn Abbas; we intended only the eating from the poisoned sheep. And it has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Jewish woman brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a poisoned sheep, and he ate of it. Then she was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked her about that. She said: I intended to kill you. He said: Allah would not have given you power over that - or he said: over a Muslim. They said: Shall we not kill her? He said: No."
"4589","Another, 328 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of his campaigns when a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning the distracted ones? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent and did not answer him a word until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his campaign and circumambulated; then a boy fell from a litter, and he was digging in the earth. Then his caller called: Where is the one who asked about the distracted ones? So the man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade the killing of their children, and said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"4590","Another, 329 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them, Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse, he and his companions: O people, fear your Lord; indeed the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing - to the end of the verse. He said: Do you know which day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That is a day on which Allah, mighty and majestic, will say to Adam: O Adam, arise and send forth the dispatch of the Fire - or he said: a dispatch to the Fire. He said: So he will say: O Lord, from how many? He said: So He will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire, and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon the people, and gloom and grief fell upon them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I hope that you are a quarter of the people of Paradise. Then he said: Indeed I hope that you are a third of the people of Paradise. Then he said: Indeed I hope that you are half of the people of Paradise - or he said: one-half of the people of Paradise. So they rejoiced. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Work and receive glad tidings, for you are between two creations; they are not with anyone except that they are numerous: Ya'juj and Ma'juj. And you among people - or among nations - are but as a mole on the flank of a camel, or as a mark on the foreleg of a she-camel. And my nation is but one part of a thousand parts. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"4591","Another, 330 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami and Ubayd ibn Khalaf al-Qati'i narrated to us, both saying: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his uncle al-Abbas: O uncle, supplicate often for well-being. Al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Muthanna, from Musaddad, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, from Hilal, saying: This is a hadith sahih upon the condition of al-Bukhari. I say: Hilal ibn Khabbab was deemed trustworthy by Imam Ahmad, Yahya ibn Ma'in, and others. And Ibrahim ibn al-Junayd said: I asked Yahya ibn Ma'in about Hilal ibn Khabbab, saying: Yahya al-Qattan claims he changed before he died and became confused. Yahya said: No, he neither became confused nor changed. I said to Yahya: So is he trustworthy? He said: Trustworthy, reliable."
"4592","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Yamami from Ikrimah, 331 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed him, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Hisham, from Yahya ibn Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mukatab is freed in proportion to what he has paid, with the blood-money of a free man; and in proportion to what remains enslaved of him, with the blood-money of a slave."
"4593","332 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What has been freed of him is compensated by the reckoning of the free, and what remains enslaved of him by the reckoning of the slave."
"4594","333 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mukatab is compensated in proportion to what has been freed of him with the blood-money of the free, and in proportion to what remains enslaved of him with the blood-money of the slave. He said: And Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - and Marwan used to say that. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari and Isma'il ibn Ulayyah, from Hisham; and from Ya'la, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf - both from Yahya. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman, from Ya'la ibn Ubayd, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Ya'la, from Hajjaj; and from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah ibn Yazid, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, similarly. And he has therein other paths besides what we mentioned."
"4595","Another, 334 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdillah - known as Sammawayh - informed us, Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade animal for animal on credit."
"4596","335 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, both saying: Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of animal for animal on credit."
"4597","336 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Bundar - known as al-Sha''ar - informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of animal for animal on credit. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi', from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu Dawud al-Hafari, from Sufyan."
"4598","Another, 337 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them, Abu al-Ghana'im Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, saying: Abu Bakr Abdillah ibn Abi Dawud al-Sijistani informed us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch Umm Salamah while a garment was over her front - meaning: while she was menstruating."
"4599","Another, 338 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati, and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, all saying: Sa'id ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when he married Fatimah - said: O Ali, do not enter upon your wife until you present something to them. Ali said: I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give her your Hutamiyyah coat of mail."
"4600","Yazid ibn Hazim - brother of Jarir ibn Hazim - from Ikrimah, 339 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Da'laj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad informed us, Yazid ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Intimate friendship is for Ibrahim, and speech is for Musa, and the Vision is for Muhammad, peace be upon them. It has already come in the narration of Qatadah from Ikrimah."
"4601","Yazid ibn Abi Sa'id al-Nahwi Abu al-Hasan from Ikrimah, 340 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them, Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, saying: My father informed me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: O you who believe, fasting is prescribed for you as it was prescribed for those before you, that you may be God-conscious. People in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when they prayed Isha - food and drink became unlawful for them, and they fasted until the next night. Then a man wronged himself: he was intimate with his wife, though he had prayed Isha and had not broken his fast. So Allah willed to make that an ease for those who remained, and a mercy and benefit. So He said: Allah knew that you were wronging yourselves, so He turned to you - to - then complete the fast until the night. So this was of what Allah benefited people with. Abu Dawud narrated it similarly, from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Shabbuwayh, from Ali ibn al-Husayn."
"4602","341 - And with the preceding chain, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id al-Dashtaki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Ibrahim, from Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - Then when they purify themselves, come to them from where Allah commanded you - he said: Coming to them is from where the avoidance was; and the avoidance is from where the coming is; thus it only means their private parts: that is what he avoids and that is what he comes to when she is pure; nothing of their skins has been forbidden other than it, neither in menstruation nor in fasting."
"4603","Another, 342 - And with the preceding chain, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The man would eat of his wife's wealth which he had dowered her and of other than it, seeing no sin upon himself in that, until Allah revealed: And it is not lawful for you to take of what you gave them anything. Then it was no longer proper for them after this verse to take anything of their wealth. Then He said: Except that they both fear they will not uphold the bounds of Allah; so if you fear they will not uphold the bounds of Allah, there is no sin upon them both in what she ransoms herself with. And He said: But if they willingly give you of it anything, consume it wholesome, pleasant."
"4604","Another, 343 - And with the preceding chain, Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: And those of you who die leaving wives, a bequest for their wives of provision for a year without expulsion - he said: The term of the year was abrogated, its term being made four months and ten days. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi, from Ali ibn Husayn. And al-Nasai narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ali ibn Husayn, similarly; and from Qutaybah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak, from Ikrimah, his statement."
"4605","Another, 344 - And with the preceding chain, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten, We bring better than it or like it - he said: And when We substitute a verse in place of a verse. He said: The first of the Qur'an to be abrogated was the qiblah; that is that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to face the rock of Bayt al-Maqdis, which is the qiblah of the Jews; so Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced it for seventeen months, that they might believe in him and follow him, and that he might thereby call the illiterate of the Arabs. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, said: And to Allah belong the east and the west, so wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah - to the end of the verse; and He said: We see the turning of your face toward the sky, so We shall turn you to a qiblah that pleases you; so turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque."
"4606","Another, 345 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Muflih ibn Ahmad al-Dumi informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - Divorced women shall wait by themselves for three courses; and it is not lawful for them to conceal what Allah created in their wombs - the verse; and that is that the man, when he divorced his wife, was most entitled to take her back, even if he divorced her thrice; so that was abrogated, and He said: Divorce is twice - the verse. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it. And al-Nasai narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ali, similarly."
"4607","346 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - concerning His statement: Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten - and His statement: And when We substitute a verse in place of a verse - and His statement: And if they incline to peace, incline to it - he said: It was abrogated by the verse in Bara'ah: Fight those who do not believe in Allah nor in the Last Day - the verse."
"4608","Another, 347 - And with the preceding chain, he said: My father informed me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - Whoever disbelieves in Allah after his faith, except one who is compelled while his heart is content with faith - the verse; then that was abrogated, and He said: Then indeed your Lord, for those who emigrated after they were tried, then strove and were patient - indeed your Lord after that is Forgiving, Merciful. And he is Abdillah ibn Abi Sarh, who was over Egypt; he had been a scribe for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Satan caused him to slip, so he joined the disbelievers. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be killed on the day of the Conquest, but Uthman ibn Affan sought protection for him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him protection. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi, from Ali ibn Husayn, similarly. And al-Nasai narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ali, similarly."
"4609","Another, 348 - And with the preceding chain, from Ibn Abbas - So eat of that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned - and: And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, and indeed it is fisq. Then it was abrogated, and excepted from that: And the food of those given the Book is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them."
"4610","Another, 349 - And with the preceding chain, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, saying: I heard my father saying: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, saying: Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever disbelieves in stoning has disbelieved in the Qur'an without reckoning - His statement: O People of the Book, Our Messenger has come to you, making clear to you much of what you concealed of the Book. And stoning was of what they concealed."
"4611","Another, 350 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Daraqazzi informed us - there - that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive in the land spreading corruption is only that they be killed, or crucified, or their hands and feet cut off from opposite sides, or exiled from the land - to - Forgiving, Merciful. This verse was revealed concerning the polytheists; so whoever of them repents before he is overpowered, that does not prevent the hadd he incurred from being carried out upon him. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. And al-Nasai narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ali ibn al-Husayn - with an addition over the narration of Abu Dawud: before he is overpowered, there is no way against him; and this verse is not for the Muslim man who kills and spreads corruption in the land and wages war against Allah and His Messenger, then joins the disbelievers before he is overpowered."
"4612","351 - Abu al-Fath Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Kharaqi informed us of it - by license - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Duni authorized them in narration, Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sunni informed us, Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasai informed us - and with him: which he incurred."
"4613","Another, 352 - Umar ibn Muhammad informed us that Muflih ibn Ahmad al-Dumi informed them, Ahmad informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: If you do not go forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment - and: It was not for the people of Madinah - to His statement: they do - it was abrogated by the verse that follows it: And it was not for the believers to go forth all together. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"4614","Another, 353 - Umar informed us that Ibrahim al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Those who believe in Allah and the Last Day do not ask your leave - the verse; it was abrogated by the one in al-Nur: The believers are only those who believe in Allah and His Messenger - to His statement - Forgiving, Merciful. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"4615","Another, 354 - And with the preceding chain, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - If he leaves good, the bequest for parents and near relatives - so the bequest was thus until the verse of inheritance abrogated it."
"4616","Another, 355 - And with the preceding chain, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - And say to the believing women that they lower their gazes - the verse; then it was abrogated, and excepted from that: And elderly women who do not hope for marriage - the verse."
"4617","Another, 356 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad informed us that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Zawzani informed us, Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Awn informed us, Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of the two hands and the two feet is equal: ten camels for each finger. Thus Abu Hatim al-Busti transmitted it."
"4618","Another, 357 - And with the preceding chain, Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - Indeed those who believed and emigrated, and those who believed but did not emigrate - so the Bedouin would not inherit from the Emigrant, nor would the Emigrant inherit from him; then it was abrogated, and He said: And blood relatives are nearer to one another."
"4619","Another, 358 - And with the preceding chain, Ali ibn Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - But if they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them - then it was abrogated. He said: So judge between them by what Allah revealed."
"4620","Another, 359 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Fadl, known as Ibn al-Mu'arraj, informed us - at Shari' Dar al-Raqiq of Baghdad - that Ibrahim al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not consume your wealth among yourselves unjustly, except that it be trade by mutual consent among you - so the man would scruple to eat with anyone after this verse was revealed; then that was abrogated by the verse in al-Nur, saying: Nor upon yourselves that you eat of your houses - to His statement - separately. The rich man would invite a man of his family to food, saying: I am indeed reluctant to eat of it - and reluctance is scruple - saying: The poor one is more entitled to it than I. So He permitted therein that they eat of that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned, and permitted the food of the People of the Book."
"4621","Another, 360 - And with the preceding chain, Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated - and: They ask you about wine and gambling; say: In them is great sin and benefits for people - they were abrogated in al-Ma'idah: Wine and gambling and idols - the verse."
"4622","Another, 361 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us - at Dar al-Qazz of Baghdad - that Ibrahim al-Karkhi informed them, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: And those of your women who commit indecency - take four witnesses from you against them; then if they testify, confine them in houses until death takes them or Allah makes for them a way - and he mentioned the man after the woman, then joined them, saying: And the two of you who commit it - harm them; then if they repent and reform, turn away from them - then that was abrogated by the verse of flogging, saying: The adulteress and the adulterer - flog each one of them a hundred lashes."
"4623","Another, 362 - Umar al-Mu'addib informed us that Muflih ibn Ahmad informed them, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: And the poets - the erring follow them - then of that was abrogated and excepted, and He said: Except those who believed and did righteous deeds and remembered Allah much."
"4624","Another, 363 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Isa ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam al-Naysaburi narrated to us. [Transmission break.] 364 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abdillah ibn Isma'il ibn Abdillah al-Muktib narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aqil al-Khuza'i narrated to us, both saying: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Abu Sufyan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, I adjure you by Allah and kinship - for we have eaten al-ilhiz - meaning camel hair mixed with blood. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And We seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves to their Lord, nor did they supplicate. The wording is that of al-Khuza'i; and in the narration of al-Naysaburi: Abu Sufyan ibn Harb came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, I adjure you by Allah and kinship - we have eaten al-ilhiz - meaning camel hair mixed with blood."
"4625","Another, 365 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Dharr al-Salihani informed them, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, I heard my father narrating, from Abu Hamzah, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fingers and teeth are equal."
"4626","366 - And Abu Ahmad Abdillah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn al-Hasan - meaning Ibn Shaqiq - narrated to us, Abu Hamzah informed us, Yazid al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Teeth are equal, and fingers are equal. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, from al-Fadl ibn Musa, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from Yazid, saying: A hasan sahih gharib hadith. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Nasih, from Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq. We intended of it only: Teeth are equal."
"4627","Another, 367 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment which took spoils; and among them was a man who said to them: I am not of them; I fell in love with a woman and followed her - so let me look at her, then do what you will. Then a tall, dark woman appeared. He said to her: Accept Islam, Hubaysh, before life runs out - traveling by night; and in one narration: I found you in the gardens; and in one narration: was it true? She said: Yes, may I be sacrificed for you. He said: So they brought him forward and struck his neck. Then the woman came and fell upon him, and gasped once or twice, then died. When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they informed him of the report. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Was there not among you a merciful man! Thus al-Nasai narrated it similarly."
"4628","Another, 368 - And with the preceding chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A thousand of Banu Sulaym were present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah - or Hunayn. The mention of Makkah was not in the copy of Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr."
"4629","Another, 369 - Abu Ghalib [...] Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarzi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Hiri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Hafs al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when he returned from a journey - would kiss his daughter Fatimah."
"4630","Yazid ibn Abi Habib - and the name of Abu Habib is Suwayd al-Misri - from Ikrimah, 370 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Hani' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, saying: I said to Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Those whom the sons of Ubayriq accused of the two coats of mail - a Jewish man called al-Nu'man ibn Mahs. So Asim said: He is rather Labid ibn Sahl - concerning His statement: And whoever earns a fault or a sin then casts it upon an innocent one has borne slander and manifest sin."
"4631","Ya'qub ibn Utbah ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas ibn Shariq al-Thaqafi from Ikrimah, 371 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ya'qub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) affirmed as true two verses of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"4632","372 - And Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it from Abdillah ibn Muhammad - Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ya'qub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) affirmed as true something of the poetry of Umayyah. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"4633","Abu Yazid al-Madini from Ikrimah, 373 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us - there - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Abu Azzah al-Dabbagh narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that a man of the Ansar had two stallions which became excited, so he put them into a garden and shut the door upon them. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting him to supplicate for him - while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with a group of the Ansar. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I have come for a need: two stallions of mine became excited, and I put them into a garden and shut the door upon them; so I wish you would supplicate for me that Allah make them submissive to me. So he said to his companions: Stand with us. Then he went until he came to the door and said: Open. The man feared for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Open - and he opened the door. One of the two stallions was near the door; when it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it prostrated to him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me something with which I tie its head and give you power over it. So he brought a bridle, and he tied its head and gave him power over it. Then he walked to the far end of the garden to the other stallion; when it saw him, it fell prostrating to him. So he said to the man: Bring me something with which I tie its head - and he tied its head and gave him power over it. Then he said: Go, for they will not disobey you. When the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, they said: O Messenger of Allah, these are two stallions that do not reason, yet they prostrated to you; then we are more entitled to prostrate to you. He said: I do not command anyone to prostrate to anyone; and had I commanded anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband. Abu Azzah's name is: al-Hakam ibn Tahman al-Basri; and Abu Awn al-Ziyadi is: Muhammad ibn Awn al-Basri, freedman of the family of Ziyad ibn Abi Sufyan. As for Abu Azzah, Yahya ibn Ma'in and Abu Zur'ah al-Razi deemed him trustworthy; and Abu Awn was also deemed trustworthy by Abu Zur'ah. And this is not Muhammad ibn Awn al-Khurasani."
"4634","Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas from his father, 374 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The auspiciousness of horses is in their sorrel color."
"4635","375 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the auspiciousness of horses is in their sorrel color."
"4636","376 - And Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dimashqi informed us - there - that his grandfather al-Husayn informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman informed us, Khaythamah informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shayban informed us, Isa ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The auspiciousness of horses is in sorrel. Abu Dawud narrated it from Yahya ibn Ma'in, from Husayn ibn Muhammad. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abdillah ibn al-Sabbah al-Hashimi al-Basri, from Yazid ibn Harun, saying: A gharib hadith; we know it by this chain only from the hadith of Shayban."
"4637","Another, 377 - The Imam Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli informed us, or another, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yusuf ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Abbadani narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm al-Ansari, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn al-Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest while upon the Ka'bah there were three hundred and sixty idols, whose feet Iblis had fastened with lead. So he came with a staff, and began pointing it at each idol of them, and it fell upon its face, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has vanished; indeed falsehood is ever vanishing - until he passed over all of them. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Ali ibn Abdillah except Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr; Ibn Ishaq is alone in it."
"4638","378 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the Conquest while upon the Ka'bah there were three hundred and sixty idols, whose feet Iblis had fastened for them with lead. So he came with his staff, and began pointing it at each idol of them, and it fell upon its face, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has vanished; indeed falsehood is ever vanishing - until he passed it over all of them."
"4639","379 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad al-Khabbaz informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja' informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, saying: Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indeed came to Makkah while around the House there were sixty and three hundred idols whose feet Iblis had fastened for them with lead; and with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a small staff of wood in his hand. He said: So he began pointing to one of them [...] and saying: Truth has come, and falsehood neither begins nor repeats - until he toppled them from the last of them. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Ma'mar Abdillah ibn Sakhbarah, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud."
"4640","Another, 380 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydillah al-Makhzumi, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was displayed to me what will be opened for my nation after me, and it pleased me. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And the Hereafter is better for you than the first - to His statement - and you shall be pleased. Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces of pearl, whose soil is musk; in each palace is what befits him."
"4641","381 - Abu Ja'far - also - (at Isfahan) and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Bakr b. Sahl narrated; Amr b. Hashim al-Bayruti narrated, he said: I heard al-Awza'i narrating from Isma'il b. Ubayd Allah al-Makhzumi, from Ali b. Abd Allah b. Abbas, from his father Abd Allah b. Abbas, he said: There was shown to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what would be opened for his ummah after him, town by town, and he rejoiced at that, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And your Lord will surely give you, and you will be pleased}. So Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces, in every palace what befits him of youths and servants."
"4642","Another, 382 - The Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq b. Abd al-Qadir b. Abi Salih al-Jili - at Baghdad - informed us that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad b. Umar b. Yusuf al-Urmawi informed them; Abu al-Husayn Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Naqqur al-Bazzaz informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali b. Umar b. Muhammad al-Sayrafi al-Harbi informed us; Yahya - he is Ibn Ma'in - narrated; Hisham b. Yusuf narrated, from Abd Allah b. Sulayman al-Nawfali, from Muhammad b. Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas. (Ha)."
"4643","383 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated; Yahya b. Ma'in told me; Hisham b. Yusuf narrated; Abd Allah b. Sulayman al-Nawfali informed us, from Muhammad b. Ali b. Abd Allah b. al-Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love Allah for what He nourishes you with of His blessings, and love me out of love for Allah, and love the people of my household out of love for me. In the narration of Abd Allah b. Ahmad: He nourishes you of His blessings."
"4644","Ammar b. Abi Ammar al-Makki Abu Amr, freedman of Banu al-Harith b. Nawfal al-Hashimi, from Ibn Abbas. 384 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far b. Ahmad b. Faris informed us; Yunus b. Habib narrated; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Hammad narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - that he recited this verse: {This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My blessing and approved for you Islam as religion}, and with him was a Jewish man, who said: Had this been revealed to us we would have taken its day as a festival. Ibn Abbas said: It was indeed revealed on a Friday, the Day of Arafah, or the evening of Arafah."
"4645","385 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Yusuf al-Qadi narrated; Sulayman b. Harb narrated; Hammad b. Salamah narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, that Ibn Abbas recited this verse {This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My blessing} to the end of the verse, and with him was a Jew, who said: Had this verse been revealed to us we would have taken its day as a festival. Ibn Abbas said: It was revealed on a day of two festivals together: Friday and the Day of Arafah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd b. Humayd, from Yazid b. Harun, from Hammad b. Salamah, and said: A hasan gharib hadith from the hadith of Ibn Abbas. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Tariq b. Shihab, from Umar b. al-Khattab. Muslim reported from Ishaq b. Rahawayh, from Rawh, from Hammad b. Salamah, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, a single hadith."
"4646","Another, 386 - Al-Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz b. Mahmud b. al-Mubarak b. al-Akhdar informed us - with my recitation to him at Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Isma'il b. Ahmad b. Umar al-Samarqandi and Abu Muhammad Yahya b. Ali b. Muhammad b. al-Tarrah informed you. (Ha). And Abu Hamid Abd Allah b. Muslim b. Thabit b. Jawa'iq informed us - recited to him while I heard at Baghdad - it was said to him: Abu al-Fath Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Muhammad b. al-Baydawi informed you. (Ha). 387 - And Abu al-Fadl Sulayman b. Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Mawsili informed us - with my recitation to him at Baghdad - I said to him: Yahya b. Ali b. al-Tarrah informed you. They said: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Naqqur al-Bazzaz informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah b. Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Hababah al-Bazzaz informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us; Hudbah narrated; Hammad narrated: from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to preach leaning against a palm trunk, and when the minbar was made he moved to it, so the trunk moaned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and embraced it, and it subsided. He said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection."
"4647","388 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated; Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated; Hammad b. Salamah narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach toward a trunk before the minbar was made; when the minbar was made and he moved to it, the trunk moaned, so he embraced it and it subsided, and he said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Affan, and Abu Kamil, and Yunus, and others, from Hammad b. Salamah. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr b. Khallad, from Bahz b. Asad, from Hammad b. Salamah, and from Thabit from Anas. The hadith of the trunk has been narrated by more than one of the Companions; al-Bukhari narrated the hadith of Ibn Umar and Jabir b. Abd Allah."
"4648","Another, 389 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us that al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present -; Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far narrated; Yunus b. Habib narrated; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Hammad b. Salamah narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father began speaking to him while he turned his face away from him, facing toward a man. When we went out, my father said to me: O my son, did you see your cousin! I was speaking to him and he would not answer me. I said: O father, did you not see the man who was with him speaking to him. He said: No. He said: Was there anyone with him?! I said: Yes. He said: So he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, was there anyone with you. He said: (And did you see him?) He said: Abd Allah told me of that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to me. He said: (Did you see him?) I said: Yes. He said: (That was Jibril, peace be upon him)."
"4649","390 - Abu Ja'far - also - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Yusuf al-Qadi narrated; Sulayman b. Harb narrated. (Ha). 391 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us, they said: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated; Hammad b. Salamah narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with my father with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a man conversing with him privately, and he was as if turned away from my father. We went out from him, and he said to me: Did you not see your cousin, as if turned away from me. I said to him: O father, with him was a man conversing with him privately. He said: Was there anyone with him?! I said: Yes. So we returned, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I said to Abd Allah such-and-such, and he said to me such-and-such, and was there anyone with you?! He said: Yes, did you see him, O Abd Allah? I said: Yes. He said: (That was Jibril; he is the one who kept me from you). Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Kamil and Affan, from Hammad. And his son Abd Allah narrated it from Hudbah b. Khalid, likewise."
"4650","Another, 392 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Abu Kamil and Hasan b. Musa narrated, they said: Hammad narrated; Ammar b. Abi Ammar informed us. Hasan said: from Ammar. Hammad said: And I think it is from Ibn Abbas, and Hasan had no doubt in it, he said: from Ibn Abbas."
"4651","393 - My father said: And Affan told it to us; Hammad narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, mursal, in it there is no Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadijah... then he mentioned the hadith. Abu Kamil and Hasan said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadijah: I see a light and hear a voice, and I fear that there is madness in me. She said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, would not do that to you, O son of Abd Allah. Then she came to Waraqah b. Nawfal and mentioned that to him, and he said: If he is truthful, then this is a namus like the namus of Musa, peace be upon him. If he is sent and I am alive, I shall strengthen him, aid him and believe in him."
"4652","394 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated; Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated; Hammad b. Salamah narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - as Hammad reckons - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadijah: I hear a voice and see a light, and I fear that there is derangement in me. Khadijah said: Allah would not do that to you, O son of Abd Allah. Then she came to Waraqah b. Nawfal and mentioned that to him. He said: If he is truthful, then this is a namus like the namus of Musa, and if he is sent and I am alive, I shall strengthen him, aid him and assist him. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Urwah, from A'ishah, likewise."
"4653","Another, 395 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Yusuf al-Qadi narrated; Sulayman b. Harb narrated; Hammad b. Salamah narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - as Abu Salamah reckons, meaning Hammad - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and her father wished to marry her to him, so she prepared food and drink and invited her father and some people of Quraysh, and they ate and drank. Khadijah said to her father: Muhammad b. Abd Allah is proposing to me; stand and marry him to me. So he married her to him, and she perfumed him and dressed him in a hulla, and thus they used to do with fathers when they married off their daughters. When the intoxication lifted from him he looked, and there he was perfumed with a hulla upon him. He said: What is my affair? She said: You married me to Muhammad. He said: Did I marry you to the orphan of Abu Talib! No, by my life. Khadijah said: Are you not ashamed; do you wish to disgrace yourself, telling Quraysh and the people that you were drunk. She kept at him until he was pleased."
"4654","396 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Abu Kamil narrated; Hammad narrated, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - as Hammad reckons - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah, and her father wished to marry her to him, so she prepared food and drink and invited her father and groups of Quraysh, and they ate and drank until they became intoxicated. Khadijah said to her father: Muhammad b. Abd Allah is proposing to me, so marry me to him. So he married her to him, and she perfumed him and dressed him in a hulla, and thus they used to do with fathers. When his intoxication lifted he looked, and there he was perfumed with a hulla upon him. He said: What is my affair, what is this? She said: You married me to Muhammad b. Abd Allah. He said: Would I marry the orphan of Abu Talib! No, by my life. Khadijah - may Allah be pleased with her - said: Are you not ashamed; you wish to disgrace yourself before Quraysh, telling the people that you were drunk. She kept at him until he was pleased."
"4655","397 - With it my father told me; Affan narrated; Hammad narrated; Ammar b. Abi Ammar narrated, from Ibn Abbas - as he reckons - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah bint Khuwaylid... then he mentioned its meaning. End of the juz, and praise belongs to Allah alone, and may Allah send blessings upon Muhammad and his family with abundant salutations."
"4656","Imran b. Taym - and it is said: b. Milhan - al-Utaridi, Abu Raja' al-Basri, from Ibn Abbas. 1 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Hamzah b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Safar al-Qurashi - at Damascus - informed us that Abu al-Hasan Ali b. al-Husayn al-Sulami al-Mawazini informed them; it was said to him: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Abd al-Salam b. Abd al-Rahman b. Ubayd b. Sa'dan - the witness at Damascus - informed you, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Yusuf b. Ya'qub al-Rab'i informed us - recited to him - he said: Abu al-Abbas Hajib b. Arkin al-Farghani informed us - from what I read to him -; Muhammad b. Jabir - he is Ibn Bujayr b. Uqbah b. Sa'id b. Amir al-Muharibi Abu Bujayr - narrated; Yahya - he is Ibn Ya'la - narrated, from his father, from Bakr b. Wa'il, from Isma'il, from Abu Raja' al-Utaridi, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: A man called a man, saying: O Abu al-Qasim! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was startled by it. A man said: O Messenger of Allah! I did not mean you; I meant another. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya as a kunya. Isma'il b. Muslim are a group; one of them, the Basri who settled in Makkah, was spoken about. And I think it is this one, and Allah knows best. Except that this hadith has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Muhammad b. Sirin from Abu Hurayrah."
"4657","2 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated; Muhammad b. Jabir al-Muharibi narrated; Yahya b. Ya'la b. al-Harith narrated, from his father, from Bakr b. Wa'il, from Isma'il b. Muslim, from Abu Raja', from Ibn Abbas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya as a kunya."
"4658","Another, 3 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad b. Hamzah b. Ali al-Sulami informed us that al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - by ijazah - and Yahya b. Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed you - recited to him at Baghdad -; Hamad b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they said: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah al-Asbahani informed us; the Qadi Abu Ahmad - he is Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Ibrahim - narrated; Muhammad b. Ayyub narrated; Abd Allah b. al-Jarrah al-Quhistani narrated; Hammad b. Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Raja' al-Utaridi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Render a sa' of food - meaning in the fitr charity. It was said: Gharib from the hadith of Ayyub. And Hammad has no known narrator except Abd Allah b. al-Jarrah."
"4659","Another, 4 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Aslam b. Sahl al-Wasiti and Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated, he said: Muhammad b. Aban al-Wasiti narrated; Jarir b. Hazim narrated, he said: I heard Abu Raja' al-Utaridi say: I heard Ibn Abbas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The affair of this ummah will not cease to be close or aligned until they speak about the wildan and qadar."
"4660","5 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz al-Harawi - there - informed us that Tamim al-Jurjani informed them; Ali b. Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Zawzani informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad b. Hibban al-Busti informed us; al-Hasan b. Sufyan narrated; Yazid b. Salih al-Yashkuri and Muhammad b. Aban al-Wasiti narrated, he said: Jarir b. Hazim narrated, he said: I heard Abu Raja' al-Utaridi say: I heard Ibn Abbas saying upon the minbar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The affair of this ummah will not cease to be aligned or close so long as they do not speak about the wildan and qadar. Abu Hatim said: By wildan he meant the children of the polytheists."
"4661","Imran b. al-Harith al-Sulami Abu al-Hakam, from Ibn Abbas. 6 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Amr b. Muhammad Abu Sa'id al-Anqazi narrated; Sufyan informed us, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Imran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives for a month, and when twenty-nine days had passed Jibril came to him and said: Your oath has been fulfilled and the month is complete."
"4662","7 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far informed us; Yunus b. Habib narrated; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Shu'bah narrated, he said: Salamah b. Kuhayl informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami narrating from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore off from his wives for a month, then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: O Muhammad! The month is complete: twenty-nine."
"4663","8 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated, they said: Amr b. Marzuq narrated; Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami narrating, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril said to me: The month is complete: twenty-nine."
"4664","9 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim b. Mansur informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated; Wahb narrated, from Shu'bah, from Salamah, from Abu al-Hakam, from Ibn Abbas, raised: He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said: The month is complete: twenty-nine. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad b. Ja'far, from Shu'bah likewise, and in it: I heard Abu al-Hakam. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr b. Yazid b. Bahz, from Shu'bah; and from Ibn Bashshar from Ghundar, from Shu'bah likewise, and he did not mention Jibril."
"4665","Another, 10 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Waki' narrated, from Sufyan, from Salamah, from Imran Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Supplicate your Lord for us that al-Safa become gold for us; if it becomes gold we shall follow you, and we shall know that what you said is as you said. So he asked his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: If you wish, this Safa will become gold for them, then whoever disbelieves among them after that, I shall punish him with a punishment with which I punish no one of the worlds; and if you wish, We open for them the doors of repentance. He said: No, O Lord, no; rather open for them the doors of repentance."
"4666","11 - With it my father told me; Abd al-Rahman narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Imran b. al-Hakam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Supplicate your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold for us and we shall believe in you. He said: And will you do? They said: Yes. He said: So he supplicated, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Your Lord conveys salutations to you, and says to you: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold for them, then whoever disbelieves after that among them, I shall punish him with a punishment with which I punish no one of the worlds; and if you wish, I opened for them the door of repentance and mercy. He said: Rather the door of repentance and mercy."
"4667","12 - Abu Ja'far and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated; Abu Nu'aym narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Imran al-Sulami, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Supplicate your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold for us; if it becomes gold for us we shall follow you. So he supplicated his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Your Lord conveys greetings to you, and says to you: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold for them, then whoever disbelieves among them, I shall punish him with a punishment with which I punish no one of the worlds; and if you wish, I opened for them the door of repentance and mercy. He said: Rather the door of repentance and mercy."
"4668","Amr b. Dinar al-Athram al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas. 13 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Makki b. Abi al-Raja' al-Hanbali - at Isfahan - informed us that Mas'ud b. al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ziyad narrated; Muhammad b. Ghallab b. Harb narrated; Abd al-Samad b. al-Nu'man narrated; Warqa' narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The slain will come dragging the killer, holding his forelock, his jugular veins gushing blood, until he brings him near the Throne. He said: Repentance was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, so he recited this verse: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally} - it has not been abrogated since it was revealed. So how can he have repentance. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Hasan b. Muhammad al-Za'farani, from Shabbabah, from Warqa' b. Umar likewise. And he said: A hasan hadith, and some narrated this hadith from Amr, from Ibn Abbas, and did not raise it. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad b. Rafi', from Shabbabah likewise. I say: There has been narrated in the Sahih something like this, not raised; we only established it in our book because it is raised, and it has already come raised in the narration of Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from Ibn Abbas."
"4669","Another, 14 - Abu Abd Allah b. Hamzah b. Muhammad al-Qurashi - at Damascus - informed us that Abu al-Hasan Ali b. al-Muslim b. Muhammad b. al-Fath al-Sulami informed them; al-Husayn b. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Tallab al-Qurashi informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Jumi' al-Ghassani informed us; Hashim b. Ahmad b. Masrur al-Nasibi Abu al-Walid narrated; Sulayman b. Sayf al-Harrani narrated; Abu Attab Sahl b. Hammad narrated; Azrah b. Thabit narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas told me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron."
"4670","15 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad b. Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated; Sulayman b. Sayf Abu Dawud al-Harrani narrated; Sahl b. Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated; Azrah b. Thabit narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umrah, for they remove sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it in his book, and in it: poverty and sins."
"4671","Another, 16 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi - at Isfahan - informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him -; Abu al-Fath Mansur b. al-Husayn b. Ali b. al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad b. Ali b. Mahrabazd informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. Ali b. al-Muqri' informed us; Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Qutaybah al-Asqalani informed us; Harmalah narrated; Ibn Wahb narrated; Zam'ah b. Salih told me, from Amr b. Dinar, he said: Abd Allah b. Abbas prayed while he was at Basra upon a mat, then told his companions that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a mat. Ibn Majah narrated it from Harmalah. There has been narrated in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Ishaq b. Abd Allah b. Abi Talhah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat, prostrating upon it. And Muslim narrated from the narration of Jabir b. Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a mat, prostrating upon it."
"4672","Another, 17 - Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated; Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated; Muhammad b. Muslim narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel. They said: To whom? He said: To the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and to the leaders of the Muslims. Muhammad b. Muslim is al-Ta'ifi; the narration differed about him from Yahya b. Ma'in: he declared him trustworthy in one narration and weak in another. And Muslim narrated from him. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Tamim al-Dari. And Imam Ahmad narrated this hadith from Zayd b. al-Hubab, from Abd al-Rahman b. Thawban, he said: I heard Amr b. Dinar say: one who heard Ibn Abbas informed him, in this narration Amr did not hear it from Ibn Abbas, and Allah knows best."
"4673","Another, 18 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. Ali b. Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated; my father narrated; Abu al-Nadr Hashim b. al-Qasim narrated; Warqa' b. Umar narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I poured wudu water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Allah, give him understanding in the religion, and teach him interpretation. We intended from it: and teach him interpretation, only."
"4674","Another, 19 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad b. al-Hasan b. Bundar al-Razi al-Muqri' informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad b. Ibrahim b. Ahmad b. Ali b. Firas informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Dubayli narrated; Abu Ubayd Allah Sa'id b. Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated; Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {It was made obscure to you, shall we compel you to it} he said: From the midst of ourselves."
"4675","Another, 20 - With it, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {And behind them was a king who seized every ship} [sound] {by force} he said: Before them."
"4676","Another, 21 - With it, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {There is no blame upon them to lay aside their garments} he said: They are the jilbabs."
"4677","Another, 22 - With it, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {I shall surely punish him with a severe punishment} he said: His punishment: plucking his feathers."
"4678","Another, 23 - And from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {We drive the water to the barren land} he said: It is the land of Yemen. Sufyan narrated it from Amr b. Dinar, from Ata', from Ibn Abbas. And it has already come in the biography of Ata'."
"4679","Another, 24 - With it, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {Among them is one who wrongs himself} he said: The one who wrongs himself: the disbeliever."
"4680","Another, 25 - And from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {Then drinking the drink of thirsty camels} he said: The thirsty wandering of the land."
"4681","Another, 26 - Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us; Muhammad b. Raja' informed me; Ahmad informed us; Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Ibrahim narrated; Abu al-Qasim Nasr b. Ali narrated; my father narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas: ((I have vowed to the Most Merciful silence) I have vowed to the Most Merciful silence). Abu Yunus's name is Hatim b. Abi Saghir; and it is said: Abu Saghir is his mother's husband, and it is said: his mother's father. And he is Hatim b. Muslim."
"4682","Another, 27 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq b. Abd al-Khaliq b. Ahmad informed us - by ijazah -. (Ha). And my maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed from him that his uncle Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad b. Abd al-Qadir informed them; Muhammad b. Abd al-Malik b. Bishran informed us; Abu al-Husayn Ali b. Umar b. Ahmad b. Mahdi al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us; al-Husayn b. Isma'il and Ibrahim b. Dubays b. Ahmad and others narrated, they said: Abu al-Walid b. Burd al-Antaki narrated; al-Haytham b. Jamil narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no suckling except what was in the two years. Thus al-Daraqutni narrated it. And he said: None raised it from Ibn Uyaynah except al-Haytham b. Jamil, and he is trustworthy, a hafiz."
"4683","Amr b. Sufyan, from Ibn Abbas. 28 - With it Ahmad b. Musa informed us; Ahmad b. Ahmad b. al-Hasan al-Razzaz narrated; my maternal grandfather Muhammad b. al-Khattab narrated; Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl b. Dukayn narrated; al-Hasan b. Salih narrated, from al-Aswad b. Qays, from Amr b. Sufyan, from Ibn Abbas: {You take from it intoxicant and good provision} he said: The intoxicant: what was forbidden of its fruit, and the good provision: what was lawful of its fruit."
"4684","29 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them; Abd al-Rahman al-Razi informed us; Ahmad b. Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Dubayli informed us; Sa'id b. Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated; Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated, from al-Aswad b. Qays, from Amr b. Sufyan, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His Exalted saying: {You take from it intoxicant and good provision} he said: The intoxicant: what Allah forbade of its price - and the correct is: of its fruit - and the good provision: what was lawful of its fruit. In our audition copy it was Amr b. Sa'id, and it is a corruption."
"4685","Amr b. Kaysan, from Ibn Abbas. 30 - Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad b. Raja' b. Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Da'laj narrated; Muhammad b. Ali b. Zayd informed us; Sa'id b. Mansur narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Amr b. Kaysan. He said: I heard Ibn Abbas reciting: {darasta} - you disputed, and you recited."
"4686","31 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad b. Ibrahim b. Ahmad b. Ali b. Firas informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Dubayli narrated; Sa'id b. Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated; Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Amr b. Kaysan, from Ibn Abbas: regarding His saying: {darasta} he said: You recited, you disputed, you argued."
"4687","Amr b. Maymun al-Awdi Abu Abd Allah al-Kufi, from Ibn Abbas. 32 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Yahya b. Hammad narrated; Abu Awanah narrated; Abu Balj narrated; Amr b. Maymun narrated, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas when seven men came to him. They said: O Abu Abbas! Either you stand with us, or you leave these alone for us. Ibn Abbas said: Rather I shall stand with you. He said: And that day he was healthy, before he became blind. He said: They began and spoke, and we do not know what they said. He said: He came shaking his garment, saying: Uff and tuff, they spoke ill of a man who has ten virtues, they spoke ill of a man to whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely send a man whom Allah will never disgrace, whom Allah and His Messenger love. He said: Whoever aspired, aspired for it. He said: Where is Ali? They said: He is in the baggage grinding. He said: And none of you would grind. He said: He came while bleary-eyed, hardly seeing. He said: He spat in his eye. Then he shook the banner three times and gave it to him, and he came with Safiyyah bint Huyayy. He said: Then he sent so-and-so with Surat al-Tawbah. Then he sent Ali after him, he said: None shall take it except a man from me, and I am from him. He said: And he said to his cousins: Which of you will ally with me in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And Ali was sitting, and they refused. Ali said: I shall ally with you in this world and the Hereafter. He said: He left him, then turned to a man among them. He said: Which of you will ally with me in this world and the Hereafter, and they refused. He said: Ali said: I shall ally with you in this world and the Hereafter. He said: You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And he was the first of the people to accept Islam after Khadijah. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his garment and placed it upon Ali and Fatimah and Hasan and Husayn. He said: {Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}. He said: And Ali sold himself. He wore the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then slept in his place. He said: And the polytheists used to pelt the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came while Ali was sleeping, and Abu Bakr thought he was the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He said: O Prophet of Allah! He said: Ali said to him: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has set out toward the well of Maymun, so catch up with him. He said: Abu Bakr set out and entered the cave with him. He said: And Ali kept being pelted with stones just as the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pelted, writhing, having wrapped his head in the garment, not bringing it out until morning. Then he uncovered his head. They said: You are indeed contemptible. Your companion we pelted and he did not writhe, while you writhe, and we found that strange. He said: And he set out with the people in the expedition of Tabuk. He said: Ali said: Shall I come out with you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No. Ali wept. He said to him: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that you are not a prophet; it is not fitting that I go except with you as my successor. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You are my ally over every believer after me. He said: And he closed the doors of the mosque except the door of Ali. He said: So he enters the mosque in janabah, and it is his path; he has no path but it. He said: And he said: Whomsoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. He said: And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, informed us that He was pleased with them - with the companions of the Tree - and He knew what was in their hearts. Did He tell us that He was angry with them after. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar when he said: Permit me to strike his neck - meaning Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, when he sent a letter to Quraysh, so Umar sought the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permission to strike his neck - he said: And would you do! And what do you know; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish."
"4688","33 - With it Abd Allah told us; Abu Malik Kathir b. Yahya narrated; Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Balj, from Amr b. Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, likewise."
"4689","34 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim b. Hashim al-Baghawi narrated; Kathir b. Yahya narrated; Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Balj, from Amr b. Maymun, he said: We were with Ibn Abbas when seven men came to him while that day he was healthy, before he became blind. They said: O Ibn Abbas! Stand with us. Or he said: Leave, O these. He said: Rather I shall stand with you. So he stood with them. We do not know what they said. He returned shaking his garment, saying: Uff, uff, they spoke ill of a man about whom was said what I now tell you; they spoke ill of Ali b. Abi Talib. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said: I shall surely send a man whom Allah will not disgrace, so he sent for Ali while he was at the mill grinding - and none of you would grind? They brought him bleary-eyed. He said: O Prophet of Allah! I can hardly see. He spat in his eye and shook the banner three times, then handed it to him. It was conquered for him. He came with Safiyyah bint Huyayy. Then he said to his cousins: Which of you will ally with me in this world and the Hereafter, three times, until he passed over the last of them. Ali said: O Prophet of Allah! I am your ally in this world and the Hereafter. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And he sent Abu Bakr with Surat al-Tawbah, and sent Ali after him. Abu Bakr said: O Ali, perhaps Allah and His Prophet are displeased with me. Ali said: No, but the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting that any convey from me except a man from me, and I am from him. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his garment upon Ali and Fatimah and al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and said: {Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}. And he was the first to accept Islam after Khadijah among the people. He said: And Ali sold himself; he wore the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then slept in his place. He said: And the polytheists used to pelt the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Abu Bakr came and said: To me, O Messenger of Allah! - Abu Bakr thinking him the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has set out toward the well of Maymun, so catch up with him. Abu Bakr set out and entered the cave with him, and Ali kept being pelted with stones just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pelted, writhing, having wrapped his head in the garment, not bringing it out until morning. Then he uncovered his head when morning came. They said: You are indeed contemptible. Your companion we pelted with stones and he did not writhe, while you writhe, and we found that strange. He said: Then he set out with the people in the campaign of Tabuk. Ali said to him: Shall I come out with you? The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No. Ali wept. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that you are not a prophet; it is not fitting that I go except with you as my successor. He said: And he said to him: You are the ally of every believer after me. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closed the doors of the mosque except the door of Ali. So he enters the mosque in janabah, and it is his path; he has no path but it. He said: And he said: Whomsoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. Ibn Abbas said: Allah informed us in the Qur'an that He was pleased with them - with the companions of the Tree - knowing what was in their hearts. So did He tell us that He was angry with them after. And he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar when he said: Will you permit me to strike his neck - meaning Hatib - he said: And would you do! And what do you know; perhaps Allah - meaning - looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish."
"4690","35 - With it Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah b. al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated; Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated; Miskin b. Bukayr narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from Abu Balj, from Amr b. Maymun, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered all the doors to be closed except the door of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4691","36 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far informed us; Yunus b. Habib informed us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Balj, from Amr b. Maymun, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are the ally of every believer after me."
"4692","37 - With it, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The first to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Khadijah was Ali, may Allah's pleasure be upon him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the doors to be closed except the door of Ali, from Muhammad b. Humayd al-Razi, from Ibrahim b. al-Mukhtar, from Shu'bah, from Abu Balj. And he said: A gharib hadith; we do not know it from Shu'bah except from this route. I say: The narration of Miskin b. Bukayr al-Harrani from Shu'bah did not reach al-Tirmidhi, and Allah knows best. And it was related from al-Hakim Abu Abd Allah that Miskin was alone in it. As if he did not know that al-Tirmidhi narrated it from the narration of one other than Miskin. And Allah knows best. And al-Tirmidhi narrated with this isnad: The first to pray was Ali. And said like his saying. And al-Nasa'i narrated: I shall surely send a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, whom Allah will never disgrace: from Ibn al-Muthanna, from Yahya b. Hammad. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it at length from Abu Khaythamah from Yahya b. Hammad, and in it seven men as in the narration of Kathir b. Ali. Abu Balj: his name is Yahya b. Sulaym, and it is said: b. Abi Sulaym al-Fazari al-Kufi. Al-Bukhari said: There is consideration in him. Ibn Hibban said: He used to err, and Yahya b. Ma'in declared him trustworthy. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: There is no harm in him. And the narration of Shu'bah from him suffices."
"4693","Antarah al-Shaybani Abu Waki' al-Basri, from Ibn Abbas. 38 - Abu Muslim Muhammad b. Muhammad b. al-Junayd al-Sufi informed us - in writing - that Mahmud b. Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah b. Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad b. Amr b. Abi Asim informed us; al-Hasan b. al-Sabbah al-Bazzaz narrated; Ishaq b. Yusuf narrated, from Sufyan, from Harun b. Antarah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The polytheists envied the Muslims. They said: What is it that what Allah kills you do not eat, while what you kill yourselves you eat, though you seek Allah's command? So Allah revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}."
"4694","39 - Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad b. Raja' b. Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Bazzaz narrated; Muhammad b. Yahya narrated; Yahya b. Dawud al-Wasiti narrated; Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Harun b. Antarah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The polytheists disputed with the Muslims. They said: What is it that what Allah kills you do not eat, while what you kill yourselves you eat, though you follow Allah's command? So Allah revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr b. Ali, from Yahya al-Qattan, from Sufyan."
"4695","Another, 40 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated; Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated; Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated, from Harun b. Antarah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us no yellow in white except what is in his two covers. I stood to the hilt of his sword and found in the scabbard of his sword a sheet written in it: Whoever innovates an innovation, or shelters an innovator, or ascribes to other than his father, or allies with other than his masters: upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Ali b. Abi Talib likewise."
"4696","Awsajah al-Makki, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas. 41 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas: A man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving no heir except a slave whom he had freed, so he gave him his inheritance."
"4697","42 - With it my father told me; Rawh narrated; Ibn Jurayj narrated; Amr b. Dinar informed me that Awsajah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, informed him, from Ibn Abbas, that a man died leaving no one to inherit him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed his inheritance to a freedman of his whom the deceased had freed; he is the one to whom his wala' belongs and who freed."
"4698","43 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad Abd al-Rahim b. Ahmad b. al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar b. Abd al-Wahid b. al-Fakhir - at Isfahan - informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Ishaq b. Ahmad b. Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us; Muhammad b. Yahya b. Abi Umar al-Adani informed us; Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving no heir except a slave whom he had freed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his inheritance."
"4699","44 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far informed us; Yunus b. Habib narrated; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Hammad narrated, from Amr, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man freed a slave of his, then died with no heir but him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made him inherit; he made the lower inherit from the upper. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa b. Isma'il from Hammad b. Salamah, from Amr. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad b. Yahya b. Abi Umar al-Adani, and said: A hasan hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, from Sufyan; and from Abu Dawud al-Harrani, from Abu Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Amr. Al-Nasa'i said: Awsajah is not well known, and we know no one narrating from him but Amr."
"4700","Another, 45 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr - at Cairo - informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abdan b. Ahmad narrated; Muhammad b. Amr b. al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated; Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah! What prevents the Habash of Banu al-Mughirah from coming to you except that they fear you will turn them away. He said: There is no good in the Habash. When they hunger they steal, and when they are sated they commit adultery, yet in them are two good traits: feeding food, and valor in battle."
"4701","Awf b. Hayyan al-Azdi, from Ibn Abbas. 46 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad b. Abd al-Rahim and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' informed them; Ahmad b. Muhammad b. al-Nu'man informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Ishaq b. Ahmad al-Khuza'i narrated; Muhammad b. Yahya b. Abi Umar al-Adani narrated; Abu Usamah narrated, he said: Awf b. Hayyan al-Azdi told me, from Ibn Abbas: The seventy whom Musa, peace be upon him, chose from his people, the tremor seized them only because they did not forbid the calf nor were pleased with it. Awf: Abu Hatim did not mention him in his book."
"4702","Fatimah bint al-Husayn b. Ali b. Abi Talib, from Ibn Abbas. 47 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Waki' narrated; Abd Allah b. Sa'id b. Abi Hind narrated, from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Amr b. Uthman, from his mother Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Ibn Abbas. (Ha)."
"4703","And Safwan, he said: Abd Allah b. Sa'id b. Abi Hind informed us, from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Amr, from his mother Fatimah bint Husayn, that she heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not keep looking at lepers."
"4704","48 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - recited to him as I see - that Mahmud b. Isma'il b. Muhammad al-Sayrafini informed them - recited to him while he was present -; Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah b. Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Amr b. Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated; Waki' narrated, from Abd Allah b. Sa'id, from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Amr b. Uthman, from his mother Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not keep looking at lepers. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Ishaq b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Zinad from Muhammad of the family of Amr b. Uthman. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd al-Rahman b. Ibrahim, from Abd Allah b. Nafi', from Ibn Abi al-Zinad; and from Ali b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Khasib, from Waki', from Abd Allah b. Sa'id b. Abi Hind, all from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Amr b. Uthman b. Affan, known as al-Dibaj, from his mother Fatimah. And Abd Allah b. Amir al-Aslami narrated it from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Amr, from his mother Fatimah, from her father al-Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in it is an addition. Al-Aslami was criticized by more than one of the imams, and the narration of Abd Allah b. Sa'id is more worthy, and Allah knows best."
"4705","Al-Qasim b. Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, from Ibn Abbas. 49 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn b. Muhammad b. Ali al-Mu'addib - at Isfahan - informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Baghiban informed them - while he was present -; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Zayd narrated - as I see -; Ahmad b. Amr b. al-Dahhak narrated; Ahmad b. Khuzaymah narrated; Habib b. Abi Marzuq narrated; the nephew of al-Zuhri narrated, from his uncle, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The first to be given his book in his right hand is Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Asad, he said: And he is the one who says: {Here, read my book}. He said: And Ibn Abbas used to recite it: Eat and drink, O Abu Salamah, with pleasure for what you sent forth in the days past. As for the one given his book in his left, the first to be given it is his brother Sufyan b. Abd al-Asad."
"4706","Another, 50 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad b. Abd al-Rahim b. al-Ikhwah informed us that Abu Sahl Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. Sa'dawayh informed them; Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad al-Razi informed us; Ali b. Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Yusuf informed us; Ibrahim b. Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi informed us; Abu Mus'ab narrated; Malik narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, he said: I heard a man asking Abd Allah b. Abbas about the anfal, and Ibn Abbas said: The horse is of the nafl, and the spoil is of the nafl. Then he repeated the question, and Ibn Abbas said that also. The man said: The anfal which Allah mentioned in His Book, what are they? Al-Qasim said: He kept asking him until he almost vexed him, then Ibn Abbas said: Do you know what the likeness of this is? The likeness of Sabigh whom Umar b. al-Khattab beat."
"4707","Another, 51 - Abu al-Hasan Ali b. Hamzah b. Ali b. Talhah al-Baghdadi - at Cairo - informed us that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah b. Muhammad b. Abd al-Wahid b. al-Husayn informed them; Abu Talib Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. Ghaylan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us; Ishaq b. al-Husayn al-Harbi narrated; Abu Hudhayfah narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas when a Bedouin came to him and said: O Ibn Abbas! In my care are orphans, and I have camels and they have camels, and I lend from my camels and I impoverish. What is lawful for me of their milk? He said: If you seek its stray, treat its mange, repair its trough, and water upon it, then drink, without harming offspring nor straining in milking."
"4708","Qays b. Habtar al-Nahshali al-Tamimi, and it is said: al-Asadi, from Ibn Abbas. 52 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Zakariyya b. Adi narrated; Ubayd Allah - he is Ibn Amr - informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas: from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the price of wine, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog. He said: When he comes to you seeking the price of the dog, fill his two palms with dust."
"4709","53 - With it my father told me; Waki' narrated, from Isra'il, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar, from Ibn Abbas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dowry of the prostitute, the price of the dog, and the price of wine."
"4710","54 - With it my father told me; Ahmad b. Abd al-Malik narrated; Ubayd Allah narrated, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar, from Ibn Abbas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of wine, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog. And he said: When its owner comes seeking its price, fill his two palms with dust."
"4711","55 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated; al-Fadl b. Dukayn narrated; Isra'il narrated, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, he raised the hadith, he said: The price of the dog, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of wine are unlawful."
"4712","56 - With it Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythamah narrated; Abd al-Jabbar al-Khattabi narrated; Ubayd Allah b. Amr narrated, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar, from Ibn Abbas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of the dog is foul. And he said: When he comes to you seeking the price of the dog, fill his two palms with dust. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abu Nu'aym as the narration of Zuhayr; and from Abd al-Jabbar b. Muhammad al-Khattabi. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Tawbah Rabi' b. Nafi' from Ubayd Allah b. Amr al-Raqqi likewise."
"4713","Another, 57 - Abu Ahmad and Abu Tahir informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Zakariyya narrated; Ubayd Allah narrated, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden for you wine, gambling and the kubah. And he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"4714","58 - With it my father told me; Abu Ahmad narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Ali b. Badhimah; Qays b. Habtar told me, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the white jar, the green jar and the red jar, and he said: The first to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the delegation of Abd al-Qays, who said: We partake of the dregs, so in which vessels? He said: Do not drink in dubba', muzaffat, naqir and hantam, and drink in skins. Then he said: Allah has forbidden to me - or: has forbidden - wine, gambling and the kubah, and every intoxicant is unlawful. Sufyan said: I said to Ali b. Badhimah: What is the kubah? He said: The drum."
"4715","59 - With it my father told me; Ahmad b. Abd al-Malik and Abd al-Jabbar b. Muhammad narrated, they said: Ubayd Allah - meaning Ibn Amr - narrated, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Habtar, from Ibn Abbas: from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Exalted, has forbidden for you wine, gambling and the kubah, and he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"4716","60 - Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated; Muhammad b. Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Ali b. Badhimah, from Qays b. Habtar: He said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the white jar, the green jar and the red, and he said: The first to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the delegation of Abd al-Qays, who said: Do not drink in dubba', muzaffat, naqir and hantam, and do not drink in jars, and drink in skins. He said: If it ferments in the skins, pour water upon it. They said to him the third or fourth time, he said: Pour it out. Then he said: Allah has forbidden to me - or: has forbidden - wine, gambling and the kubah, and every intoxicant is unlawful. Sufyan said: I said to Ali b. Badhimah: What is the kubah? He said: The drum. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili likewise. We only intended mention of gambling and the kubah."
"4717","Kurayb b. Abi Muslim Abu Rishdin, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from him. 61 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim b. Mansur informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated; Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from al-Dahhak b. Uthman, from Makhramah b. Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at a man who approaches a man or a woman in her behind."
"4718","62 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Hamzah b. Muhammad b. Abi Jamil al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi and Abu al-Fadl Isma'il b. Ali b. Ibrahim b. al-Janzawi, both - at Damascus - informed us that Abu al-Hasan Ali b. Ahmad b. Mansur al-Ghassani al-Maliki informed them - recited to him -; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad b. Abd al-Wahid b. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Uthman b. Abi al-Hadid al-Sulami informed us - recited to him - it was said to him: Your grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi al-Hadid al-Sulami informed you, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ja'far b. Muhammad b. Sahl al-Samiri, known as al-Khara'iti - from what was read to him while I heard - informed us; Ibrahim b. Abd Allah b. al-Junayd narrated; Yusuf b. Abi Umayyah al-Thaqafi narrated; Abd Allah b. Sa'id al-Kindi narrated; Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from al-Dahhak b. Uthman, from Makhramah b. Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at a man who approaches a man or a woman in her behind. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Sa'id Abd Allah al-Kindi, and said: A hasan gharib hadith. And al-Nasa'i also narrated it from Abu Sa'id al-Kindi; and from Hannad, from Waki', from al-Dahhak with its isnad from the saying of Ibn Abbas. And Abu Hatim b. Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan b. Sufyan, from Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah."
"4719","Another, 63 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; al-Hakam b. Musa narrated; Isa b. Yunus narrated, from Rishdin, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel twice."
"4720","64 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Bara' narrated; al-Mu'afa b. Sulayman narrated; Isa b. Yunus narrated, from Rishdin b. Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he drank would breathe twice. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ali b. Khashram, from Isa b. Yunus, and said: A gharib hadith; we know it only from the hadith of Rishdin. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham b. Ammar and Muhammad b. al-Sabbah, from Marwan b. Mu'awiyah, from Rishdin. I say: This Rishdin was spoken about, except that there was narrated in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Thumamah b. Abd Allah b. Anas, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times."
"4721","Another, 65 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Ya'qub narrated; my father narrated, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Muhammad b. al-Walid b. Nuwayfi', from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Banu Sa'd b. Bakr sent Dimam b. Tha'labah as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to him and made his camel kneel at the mosque door, then tied it. Then he entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his companions, and Dimam was a sturdy hairy man with two braids. He came forward until he stood over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his companions, and said: Which of you is the son of Abd al-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib. He said: Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: O son of Abd al-Muttalib, I am asking you and shall be stern in questioning, so do not find it in yourself. He said: I shall not find it in myself; ask whatever occurs to you. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah send you to us as a messenger? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah command you to command us to worship Him alone, associating nothing with Him, and to cast off these rivals which our fathers worshipped with Him? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah command you to pray these five prayers? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: Then he began mentioning the obligations of Islam, obligation by obligation: zakah, fasting, Hajj and all the laws of Islam, adjuring him as before. Until when he finished he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and I shall perform these obligations and avoid what you forbade me, then I shall neither add nor lessen. He said: Then he turned back to his camel. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he turned: If the one with two braids is truthful, he shall enter Paradise. He said: He came to his camel and released its hobble, then went out until he came to his people, and they gathered to him. The first thing he spoke was to say: Evil are al-Lat and al-Uzza. They said: Hush, O Dimam! Fear leprosy and leukoderma; fear madness. He said: Woe to you; by Allah they neither harm nor benefit. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sent a messenger and revealed to him a Book by which He rescued you from what you were in. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. I have come to you from him with what He commanded you and forbade you. He said: By Allah! That evening none remained in his camp, man or woman, except a Muslim. He said: Ibn Abbas says: We never heard of a delegate of a people better than Dimam b. Tha'labah."
"4722","66 - Abu Muhammad Hibat Allah Yahya b. Ali b. Haydarah al-Misri - there - informed us that Abd Allah b. Rifa'ah b. Ghadir b. Ali al-Sa'di informed them; Ali b. al-Hasan b. Muhammad al-Khila'i informed us; Abd al-Rahman b. Umar b. Muhammad b. Sa'id al-Tujibi informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far al-Ward al-Baghdadi informed us; Abd al-Rahim b. Abd Allah b. Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi informed us; Abd al-Malik b. Hisham informed us; Ziyad b. Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated; Ibn Ishaq said: Muhammad b. al-Walid b. Nuwayfi' told me, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Banu Sa'd b. Bakr sent Dimam b. Tha'labah as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he came to him and made his camel kneel at the mosque door, then tied it... then he mentioned the hadith at length like the hadith before it. Abu Dawud narrated it likewise from Muhammad b. Amr Zunayj al-Razi from Salamah b. al-Fadl, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Salamah b. Kuhayl and Muhammad b. al-Walid b. Nuwayfi', from Kurayb."
"4723","Another, 67 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim b. Mansur informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Bishr b. al-Walid narrated; Sharik narrated, from Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! My sister vowed to perform Hajj walking. He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no need of your sister's hardship. Let her perform Hajj riding and expiate her oath."
"4724","68 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Yahya b. Adam narrated; Sharik narrated, from Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas - raising it to him -: that he said: Let her ride and expiate her oath."
"4725","69 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz b. Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us that Tamim b. Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them; Ali b. Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Zawzani informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad b. Hibban al-Busti informed us; al-Hasan b. Sufyan informed us; Zakariyya b. Yahya Zahmawayh narrated; Sharik narrated, from Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister imposed upon herself to perform Hajj walking. He said: Order her to ride and to expiate."
"4726","Another, 70 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Ridhah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated; Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated; Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Thabit narrated; Isma'il b. Ibrahim b. Uqbah told me, from his uncle Musa b. Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a gap between his two front teeth; when he spoke, light was seen as if between his front teeth."
"4727","71 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad b. Abd Allah b. Abd al-Samad al-Sulami - at Damascus - informed us that Abd al-Awwal b. Isa b. Shu'ayb al-Sufi informed them; Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. al-Muzaffar al-Dawudi informed us; Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us; Isa b. Umar al-Samarqandi informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah b. Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi informed us; Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir informed us; Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Thabit al-Zuhri narrated; Isma'il b. Ibrahim, nephew of Musa, told me, from his uncle Musa b. Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a gap between his two front teeth; when he spoke, light was seen coming out from between his teeth. Al-Tirmidhi reported it in the Book of Shama'il, from al-Darimi."
"4728","Another, 72 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim b. Mansur informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad b. Ali b. al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Ishaq b. Hatim narrated; Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata' narrated, from Thawr b. Yazid, from Makhul, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the evening of Monday, come to me, you and your son. He seated al-Abbas and his son and cast over them a cloak of his, then said: O Allah, forgive al-Abbas and his son with a forgiveness outward and inward, leaving no sin. O Allah, succeed him in his son. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari, from Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata' likewise, and said: This is a hasan gharib hadith; we know it only from this route. I say: And Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata': al-Bukhari, al-Razi and al-Nasa'i said: He is not strong. And Muslim reported from him."
"4729","Another, 73 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi informed us, they said: Abd Allah b. Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated; Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad narrated, from Ibrahim b. Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sisters are believers: Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, and Salma, wife of Hamzah, and Asma' bint Umays; she is their sister through their mother. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr b. Mansur al-Nasa'i, from Abd Allah b. Abd al-Wahhab."
"4730","Another, 74 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah b. Ali b. Su'ud b. Thabit al-Busiri - at Egypt - informed us that Abu Sadiq Murshid b. Yahya b. al-Qasim al-Madini informed them; Muhammad b. al-Husayn b. Muhammad al-Naysaburi informed us; Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Zakariyya b. Hayyawayh narrated; Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad b. Shu'ayb b. Ali b. Sinan b. Bahr al-Nasa'i informed us; Muhammad b. Ayyub b. Ibrahim informed us; Abd Allah b. Idris narrated, from al-A'mash, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed and was brought a towel but did not touch it, and kept gesturing with the water thus. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it. There has been narrated in the Two Sahihs in the description of the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bath something like this from the hadith of al-A'mash from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from his aunt Maymunah. And there has been narrated in the Sahih something like this. Perhaps the Companion narrated it from another Companion, and perhaps he sufficed and did not narrate it from the other Companion."
"4731","Another, 75 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Ya'qub narrated; my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, from Salamah b. Kuhayl and Muhammad b. al-Walid b. Nuwayfi', freedman of al-Zubayr, both told me from Kurayb, freedman of Abd Allah b. Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at night in a Hadrami cloak wrapped in it, with nothing else upon him. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Abu Khaythamah, from Ya'qub b. Ibrahim with its isnad."
"4732","Another, 76 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz b. Muhammad al-Harawi - there - informed us that Tamim b. Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them; Ali b. Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Harun al-Zawzani informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad b. Hibban al-Busti informed us; Ibn Khuzaymah informed us; Sa'd b. Abd Allah b. Abd al-Hakam narrated; my father narrated; al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated, from Khalid b. Yazid, from Sa'id b. Abi Hilal, from Makhramah b. Sulayman, that Kurayb informed him, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, saying: The night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in one of his chambers, and whoever was outside would hear. Thus Abu Hatim reported it in his book."
"4733","Another, 77 - Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman - he is Ibn Iqal al-Harrani - narrated; Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated; Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated, from Ibrahim b. Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas. (Ha)."
"4734","78 - Abu Ja'far b. Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Ridhah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ja'far b. Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated; Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated; Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad narrated, from Ibrahim b. Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mistresses of the women of Paradise after Maryam bint Imran: Fatimah, and Khadijah, and Asiyah, wife of Pharaoh. The wording of Ja'far al-Firyabi. And in the narration of Ahmad al-Harrani: The mistresses of Paradise. And with him: Then Asiyah. Something like it has come in the narration of Ilba' b. Ahmad, from Ikrimah."
"4735","Another, 79 - With it Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Yahya b. Mansur Abu Sa'd al-Harawi narrated; Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated; Ibn Wahb narrated; Amr b. al-Harith informed me that Bukayr b. Abd Allah told him, from Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas and Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar and al-Miswar b. Makhramah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after the Asr prayer."
"4736","Another, 80 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Abd Allah b. Bakr narrated; Hatim - meaning Ibn Abi Saghir - Abu Yunus narrated, from Amr b. Dinar, that Kurayb informed him, that Ibn Abbas said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of the night and prayed behind him, so he took my hand and drew me until he made me level with him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to his prayer, I withdrew. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and when he finished he said to me: What is my affair that I make you level with me and you withdraw? I said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it fitting for anyone to pray level with you while you are the Messenger of Allah whom Allah has given? He said: I pleased him. He supplicated Allah for me to increase me in knowledge and understanding. He said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep until I heard him snore, then Bilal came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah! The prayer. He stood and prayed. He did not repeat wudu. There has been narrated in the Two Sahihs mention of Ibn Abbas praying with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from another route, but in what we narrated of mention of withdrawing, and the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to him, and his answer to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it was not mentioned in the Sahih."
"4737","Another, 81 - The Imam Muzaffar b. Abi al-Qasim b. Abi al-Hasan b. Qayba - at the Harim of Baghdad - informed us that Abu Muhammad Sulayman b. Mas'ud al-Qassab informed them - recited to him -; Abu al-Qasim Ali b. al-Husayn b. Abd Allah al-Rab'i informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Makhlad al-Bazzaz informed us; Uthman - he is Ibn al-Sammak - narrated; Ja'far b. Muhammad b. al-Hasan al-Za'farani narrated; Ahmad b. al-Sabbah al-Nahshali narrated; Shabbabah narrated, from Warqa', from Mansur, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the rabbi of Tayma': Peace upon you, and then."
"4738","82 - My maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Maqdisi, informed us of it, that Abu Bakr Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Naqur informed them - at Baghdad -; Abu al-Qasim Ali b. al-Husayn al-Rab'i informed us with its isnad likewise."
"4739","83 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad b. Mahmud b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Abu Bishr al-Dulabi - he is Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Hammad al-Razi - narrated; Ahmad b. Abi Shurayh al-Razi narrated; Shabbabah narrated; Warqa' narrated, from Mansur, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the rabbi of Tayma' and greeted him."
"4740","Another, 84 - Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Abi al-Qasim informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad b. Raja' b. Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Ibrahim narrated; Muhammad b. Ayyub narrated; Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Abi Ja'far informed us; my father narrated, from his father, from Musa b. Uqbah, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard him say: Allah knows best, the people before there came down about fasting what came down, would eat and drink, and the affair of women was lawful for them; when one of them slept, he would not eat nor drink nor approach his wife until he broke fast the next time. It reached us that Umar b. al-Khattab, after he slept and fasting became obligatory upon him, fell upon his wife. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I complain to Allah and to you of what I did. He said: And what did you do? He said: My soul enticed me, so I fell upon my wife after I slept while I intended fasting. They claimed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were not fit to do so. Then the Book came down: {Permitted to you on the night of fasting is intimacy with your wives}."
"4741","Kulayb b. Shihab al-Jarmi al-Kufi, father of Asim, from Ibn Abbas. 85 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad b. Abi Mansur b. Muhammad b. Yanal al-Sufi and Abu al-Fath Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi - in writing from Isfahan - informed us that Abd al-Rahman b. Hamad b. al-Hasan al-Duni informed them - recited to him -; Ahmad b. al-Husayn b. al-Kassar informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ishaq b. al-Sunni informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman b. Shu'ayb b. Ali al-Nasa'i narrated; Ali b. Maymun narrated, from Sufyan, from Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man, when he ordered the two mutual cursers to curse, to place his hand at the fifth upon his mouth, and said: It is binding."
"4742","86 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad b. Abd al-Rahim b. al-Ikhwah and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad b. Muhammad b. al-Nu'man informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Ishaq b. Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us; Muhammad b. Yahya b. Abi Umar al-Adani narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made li'an between the man and the woman, he ordered a man to place his hand upon the mouth of the curser, and said: It is binding."
"4743","87 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated; Yunus b. Muhammad narrated, from Salih b. Umar; Asim b. Kulayb narrated, from his father, he said: Ibn Abbas told me, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accused his wife with a man, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that. He kept pressing him until there came down upon him: {And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves}. He recited to him until he finished the two verses, then he sent to them and called them, and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has revealed concerning you. He called the man and recited to him. He bore four testimonies by Allah that he is of the truthful. He said: Then he ordered him, so he was held by his mouth and he admonished him, saying: Everything is easier upon you than the curse of Allah. Then he released him, and he said: The curse of Allah upon him if he is of the liars. Then he called her and recited to her. She bore four testimonies by Allah that he is of the liars. He ordered her, so she was held by her mouth and he admonished her, saying: Woe to you! Everything is easier upon you than the anger of Allah. Then he released her, and she said: The anger of Allah upon her if he is of the truthful. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, Allah, Majestic His remembrance, shall surely judge between you a decisive judgment. She gave birth, and I never saw a newborn in Madinah with more visitors than him. He said: If she brings him of such-and-such, then he is of such, and if she brings him of such-and-such, then he is of such. She brought him resembling the one she was accused with. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Makhlad b. Khalid al-Sha'iri, from Sufyan. There has been narrated in the Sahih mention of li'an from Ibn Abbas. Except that placing the hand at the fifth upon the mouth, and the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to them: Everything is easier than the curse of Allah, and than the anger of Allah; and the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, shall surely judge between you a decisive judgment, were not mentioned. And Asim b. Kulayb: Ali b. al-Madini said: What he alone narrates is not adduced as proof, and Muslim narrated from him. Imam Ahmad said: There is no harm in his hadith, and Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Righteous."
"4744","Muhammad b. Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas. 88 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Sufyan narrated, from Amr, from Muhammad b. Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I am amazed at one who anticipates the month, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast until you see it. Or he said: Fast upon seeing it. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Yazid, from Sufyan."
"4745","89 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz al-Harawi - there - informed us that Zahir b. Tahir al-Shahhami informed them; Muhammad b. Abi Bakr - he is al-Kanjarudhi - informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Hiri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr b. Harb narrated; Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated - meaning from Amr - from Muhammad b. Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I marveled at one who anticipates the month, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break fast; if it is obscured to you, complete the number as thirty."
"4746","Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn Abbas. 90 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Hushaym narrated; Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that a funeral passed by al-Hasan and Ibn Abbas, so al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas did not stand. Al-Hasan said to Ibn Abbas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not stand for it? He said: He stood and sat."
"4747","91 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated; Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated; Hammad b. Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, he said: A funeral passed by Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan b. Ali - may Allah be pleased with them - so al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas remained seated. Al-Hasan said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not stand for the funeral of a Jew or Jewess that passed by him? Ibn Abbas said: Yes indeed, and he sat."
"4748","92 - With it al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, that Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan b. Ali were passed by a funeral, so one of them stood and the other sat. The one who stood said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood? The other said: Yes indeed, and he sat. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, from Hammad; and from Ya'qub b. Ibrahim, from Hushaym, from Mansur, from Ibn Sirin likewise."
"4749","Another, 93 - With it Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated; al-Husayn b. Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated; al-Nadr b. Shumayl narrated; Ibn Awn informed us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended his hand to Hudhayfah, and Hudhayfah as if held back until he went and bathed and came. He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I was junub. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim does not become impure. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Abu Wa'il Shaqiq b. Salamah, from Hudhayfah. And it was narrated from Shu'bah and others that Muhammad b. Sirin did not hear from Ibn Abbas. I say: Al-Bukhari narrated in the Sahih in Foods: from Abd Allah b. Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi, from Hammad b. Zayd, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked meat from a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform wudu."
"4750","Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas. 94 - My maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Abu Zur'ah Tahir b. Muhammad b. Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them - at Baghdad -; Muhammad b. al-Husayn b. Ahmad b. al-Haytham informed us; al-Qasim b. Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us; Ali b. Ibrahim b. Salamah b. Bahr al-Qattan informed us; Abu Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Yazid b. Majah al-Qazwini narrated; Ali b. Muhammad narrated; Abd Allah b. Musa narrated, from Uthman b. al-Aswad, from Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: Where did you come from? He said: From Zamzam. He said: Did you drink from it as befits? He said: And how? He said: When you drink from it, face the Ka'bah, mention the name of Allah, breathe three times, drink your fill from it, and when you finish, praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill from Zamzam."
"4751","Muhammad b. Ali b. Abd Allah b. Abbas Abu Abd Allah, from his grandfather. 95 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim b. Abd Allah b. Umar b. Ahmad b. al-Saffar - at Naysabur - informed us that Abu Bakr Wajih b. Tahir b. Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them - recited to him -; Abu Hamid Ahmad b. al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us; Abu Sa'id Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Hamdun al-Tajir informed us; Abu Hamid Ahmad b. Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. al-Sharqi narrated; Muhammad b. Yahya b. Abd Allah b. Khalid b. Faris b. Dhu'ayb al-Dhuhli narrated; Yazid b. Abd Rabbihi narrated; Baqiyyah b. al-Walid narrated, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Abbas, he said: Ibn Abbas used to narrate that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent to His Prophet an angel of the angels with Jibril. The angel said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah gives you the choice between being a servant-prophet and being a king-prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Jibril as consulting him, and Jibril gestured to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his hand to be humble. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather I shall be a servant-prophet. He said: He never ate after that word reclining until he met his Lord. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr b. Uthman, from Baqiyyah. And thus in it Muhammad b. Abd Allah, so he was ascribed to his grandfather."
"4752","Muhammad b. Amr b. Ata' b. Alqamah al-Amiri, from Ibn Abbas. 96 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Nasr al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad b. Ali al-Abbar narrated; al-Walid b. Abd al-Malik al-Harrani narrated; Musa b. A'yan narrated, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Muhammad b. Amr b. Ata', from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for me al-Wasilah, for no servant asks it for me in this world except I shall be for him a witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Musa b. A'yan."
"4753","97 - It was read to Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Hamzah b. Muhammad al-Qurashi - while we heard at Damascus -: Abu al-Hasan Ali b. al-Muslim b. Muhammad al-Sulami informed you - recited to him -; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad b. Abd al-Wahid b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Hadid informed us; my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi al-Hadid informed us; al-Hasan b. Ali the Imam informed us; Sa'id b. Abdus b. Abi Zaydun al-Qaysarani narrated; Muhammad b. Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated; Sufyan narrated, from Musa, from Muhammad b. Amr b. Ata', from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for me al-Wasilah, I shall be for him an intercessor or a witness, or a witness or an intercessor. Musa in this narration I see is Ibn Ubaydah, and we did not rely upon his narration; we only mentioned him as a witness for another."
"4754","Another, 98 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad b. Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated; Dawud b. Rashid narrated; Abd Allah b. Ja'far narrated, from Muhammad b. Amr b. Halhalah, from Muhammad b. Amr b. Ata', from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of these greens of yours anything, let him not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what the sons of Adam are harmed by. Abd Allah b. Ja'far - I am not certain whether he is al-Madini or al-Barmaki or al-Raqqi, for al-Madini is Abu Ali, spoken about, while al-Barmaki and al-Raqqi are trustworthy. Except that this hadith has a witness in the Sahih from another route about eating garlic, onion and leek."
"4755","Muhammad b. al-Munkadir b. Abd Allah b. al-Hudayr al-Tamimi al-Qurashi, from Ibn Abbas. 99 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad b. Mahmud b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Abd al-Samad b. Sa'id al-Himsi narrated; Uthman b. Khurrazadh narrated; Ahmad b. Isa b. Hassan al-Tustari narrated; Ibn Wahb narrated; Shabib b. Sa'id narrated; Aban b. Taghlib told me, from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wakes pleasing his parents or one of them, two doors to Paradise are opened for him; and whoever wakes displeasing his parents or one of them, two doors to Hell are opened for him. Imam Ahmad narrated - in his Musnad in the Musnad of Ibn Abbas - from Aswad b. Amir, from al-Hasan b. Salih, from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir, he said: It was told from Ibn Abbas that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The drunkard, if he dies, shall meet Allah like a worshipper of idols. I do not know whether Muhammad b. al-Munkadir heard from Ibn Abbas or not."
"4756","Mahmud b. Labid al-Ansari, from Ibn Abbas. 100 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated; Muhammad b. Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated; Ibrahim b. al-Mukhtar narrated, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Harith b. Fudayl, from Mahmud b. Labid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are upon Bariq, a river at the gate of Paradise; their provision comes out to them from Paradise morning and evening."
"4757","101 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad b. Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythamah narrated; Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated; my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: al-Harith b. Fudayl al-Ansari told me, from Mahmud b. Labid al-Ansari, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are upon Bariq, a river at the gate of Paradise, a green dome; their provision comes out to them morning and evening."
"4758","102 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Ya'qub narrated; my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: al-Harith b. Fudayl al-Ansari told me, from Mahmud b. Labid al-Ansari, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are upon Bariq, a river at the gate of Paradise, in a green dome; their provision comes out to them from Paradise morning and evening. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili. And with him: in a dome, as in the narration of Imam Ahmad."
"4759","Mujahid b. Jabr al-Makki Abu al-Hajjaj, freedman of Banu Makhzum, from Ibn Abbas. 103 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us that al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah b. Ja'far informed us; Yunus b. Habib narrated; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ha."
"4760","104 - Abu al-Mufakhir Khalaf b. Ahmad b. Hamad b. Muhammad b. Ja'far al-Farra' and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid b. al-Qasim b. al-Fadl b. Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani - at Isfahan - informed us that Abu al-Fath Isma'il b. al-Fadl b. Ahmad b. al-Ikhshid al-Sarraj informed them - recited to him -; Abu Tahir Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Ja'far b. Hayyan informed us; Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Asad b. Yazid al-Madani informed us; Abu Dawud narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ha."
"4761","105 - Abu Ja'far - also - and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated; Amr b. Marzuq narrated; Shu'bah informed us. Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad b. Asad b. Yazid al-Asbahani told us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ha."
"4762","106 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he was at the Stone with a crooked staff, striking the Stone with it and kissing it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims} - if a drop of Zaqqum dripped upon the earth, it would embitter the livelihood of the people of this world; so how about one whose food it is, with no food for him but it. The wording of Muhammad b. Ja'far. And the narration of Yunus b. Habib, from Abu Dawud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims} - if a drop of Zaqqum dripped into the seas of this world, it would corrupt the livelihoods of the people of this world. How about one whose food it is. And the narration of Muhammad b. Asad, from Abu Dawud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {Fear Allah as He should be feared}, the verse, like the one before it. Except that he said: Would be corrupted. And with him: So how about one whose food and drink it is. And the narration of Amr b. Marzuq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {Fear Allah as He should be feared}, the verse, and said: If a drop of Zaqqum dripped into the seas of this world, it would corrupt their livelihoods. How about one whose food it is? Imam Ahmad also narrated it likewise from Rawh, from Shu'bah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad b. Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud. And he said: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Bishr b. Khalid al-Askari from Ghundar likewise. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad b. Bashshar, from Ibn Abi Adi from Shu'bah likewise. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it likewise from al-Husayn b. Muhammad b. Abi Ma'shar, from Muhammad b. Bashshar, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Shu'bah. And Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated it from Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri, from Fudayl b. Iyad, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid. Perhaps al-A'mash heard it from Mujahid and from Abu Yahya from him, or perhaps he used to conceal it, and Allah knows best."
"4763","Another, 107 - Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Harbi and al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Husayn narrated; Jarir b. Hazim narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted among his sacrificial camels a camel that belonged to Abu Jahl, in its nose a ring of silver."
"4764","108 - With it my father told me; Ya'qub narrated; my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq; Abd Allah b. Abi Najih told me, from Mujahid b. Jabr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gifted the camel of Abu Jahl which was seized on the day of Badr, in its head a ring of silver, in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah among his sacrificial animals. And he said in another place: To enrage thereby the polytheists."
"4765","109 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythamah narrated; Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated; my father narrated with its isnad likewise. And its end: his sacrificial animal."
"4766","110 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated; Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ayyub - author of the Maghazi - narrated; Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah b. Abi Najih said: Mujahid told me, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah among his gifts a camel of Abu Jahl, in its head a ring of silver; to enrage thereby the polytheists."
"4767","111 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated; Ahmad b. Abd al-Malik b. Waqid al-Harrani narrated; Muhammad b. Salamah narrated, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted in the Umrat al-Hudaybiyyah the camel of Abu Jahl b. Hisham, upon it a nose-rein of gold - and it is the halter - and he did that only to enrage Quraysh. The well-known is of silver, not of gold. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Nufayli, from Muhammad b. Salamah; and from Muhammad b. al-Minhal, from Yazid b. Zuray', both from Muhammad b. Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah b. Abi Najih said."
"4768","Another, 112 - Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad b. Raja' b. Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad b. Ali b. Duhaym narrated; Ahmad b. Hazim narrated; Uthman b. Muhammad narrated; Yahya b. Ya'la narrated; my father narrated, from Ghaylan b. Jami', from Ja'far b. Iyas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When there came down: {And those who hoard gold and silver} it weighed heavily upon the Muslims, and they said: None of us can leave for his child what remains after him. Umar said: I shall relieve you. He said: They set out - or: Umar and Thawban set out - and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah! This verse has weighed heavily upon your companions. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah imposed zakah only to purify what remains of your wealth, and He imposed inheritances only in wealth remaining after you. Umar exclaimed Allahu Akbar, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of what a man hoards: The righteous woman - when he looks at her she pleases him, when he commands her she obeys him, and when he is absent from her she guards him. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman b. Abi Shaybah. Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Sulayman al-Shadhakuni and others narrated it from Yahya b. Ya'la b. al-Harith, from his father, from Ghaylan b. Jami', from Uthman b. Umayr Abu al-Yaqzan, from Ja'far b. Iyas, adding in its isnad Uthman b. Umayr, and he is spoken about; if Ghaylan heard it from Ja'far b. Iyas, otherwise he concealed it, and Allah knows best."
"4769","Another, 113 - Abu Ali Diya' b. Abi al-Qasim b. Abi Ali b. al-Khurayf - at Baghdad - informed us that Abu al-Husayn Muhammad, son of the Qadi Abu Ya'la Muhammad b. al-Farra', informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Ali b. Thabit al-Khatib informed us; al-Qasim b. Ja'far al-Hashimi informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us; Abu Dawud Sulayman b. al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated; Dawud b. Rashid narrated; Yahya b. Zakariyya narrated; Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated, from Aban b. Salih and from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: A man asked Ibn Abbas one day while I was with him, saying: O Abu Abbas! I divorced my wife thrice. Ibn Abbas said: You disobeyed your Lord, and your wife is forbidden to you, and you did not fear Allah that He make for you a way out. One of you divorces, then says: O Abu Abbas! Allah said: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them facing their waiting period) - and thus Ibn Abbas used to recite this letter."
"4770","114 - With it Ibn Mardawayh informed us; Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated; Abd Allah b. Najiyah narrated; al-Husayn b. Junayd narrated; Sa'id b. Maslamah narrated; Isma'il b. Umayyah narrated, from Abd Allah b. Kathir, from Mujahid, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas one day when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas! I divorced my wife thrice - then he mentioned like the hadith of Ayyub - and said: Allah said: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them facing their waiting period). Isma'il b. Umayyah said, from Ubayd Allah b. Abi Yazid: that he was in the مجلس with Ibn Abbas and heard from him what Mujahid narrated of this hadith."
"4771","115 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad b. Ma'mar al-Qurashi informed us that Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid b. Ahmad b. Muhammad informed us; Abd Allah b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq b. Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad b. Mani' informed us; Ibn Ulayyah narrated; Ayyub narrated, from Abd Allah b. Kathir, from Mujahid, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said that he divorced his wife thrice. He was silent until I thought he would return her to him, then he said: One of you goes and rides folly, then says: O Ibn Abbas... O Ibn Abbas, while Allah the Exalted said: {And whoever fears Allah, He shall make for him a way out}. You disobeyed your Lord, and your wife is separated from you. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them facing their waiting period)."
"4772","116 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated; my father told me; Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated; Shu'bah narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih and Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid, that a man asked Ibn Abbas, saying: He divorced his wife a hundred times. He said: You disobeyed your Lord and your wife is separated from you; you did not fear Allah that He make for you a way out and provide for you whence you do not expect, and he recited: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them in their waiting period). Abu Dawud narrated from Humayd b. Mas'adah, from Isma'il b. Ulayyah, from Ayyub, from Abd Allah b. Kathir likewise. And al-Nasa'i narrated from Muhammad b. Bashshar, from Muhammad, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them in their waiting period) - Ibn Abbas said: Facing their waiting period. Al-Nasa'i did not add beyond this."
"4773","Another, 117 - Abu Ja'far Umar b. Muhammad b. Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Mansur al-Karkhi informed them; Ahmad b. Ali Thabit al-Khatib informed us; al-Qasim b. Ja'far informed us; Muhammad b. Ahmad informed us; Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated; Ibn al-Sarh narrated; Ibn Wahb narrated, from Usamah, from Aban b. Salih, from Mujahid b. Jabr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The connector and the one connected, the plucker and the one plucked, the tattooer and the one tattooed, without ailment, are cursed. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs likewise from the hadith of Alqamah from Abd Allah b. Mas'ud."
"4774","Another, 118 - Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad b. Raja' b. Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Ahmad b. al-Hasan narrated; Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Bara' narrated; Mu'afa b. Sulayman narrated; Muhammad b. Salamah narrated, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Aban b. Salih, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar - and may Allah forgive him - erred; rather this clan of the Ansar, being idolaters, with this clan of Jews, would approach women only from the side, and that is the most modest a woman can be. The Ansar had taken that from their practice, while this clan of Quraysh would spread women open in a repugnant spreading and enjoy them front, back and lying. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, a man of the Muhajirin married a woman of the Ansar and went to do with her as they used to do, and she disapproved of that from him, saying: We were only approached from the side; if you wish, do that, otherwise avoid me. Her affair spread until it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Allah revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish} - that is: front, back and lying. Meaning thereby the place of offspring."
"4775","119 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated; Asad b. Musa narrated; Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Aban b. Salih, from Mujahid, he said: I recited to Ibn Abbas from its opening to its seal, stopping him at every verse of it and asking him about it, until I reached this verse: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish}. Ibn Abbas said: This clan of Quraysh in Makkah used to spread women open and enjoy them front and back. When they came to Madinah and married among the Ansar, they went to do with them, and they disapproved of that, saying: This is something we were not approached upon. The talk spread until it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish}. If you wish, front, and if you wish, kneeling; He means thereby only the place of offspring for tilth. He says: The tilth is from whencesoever you wish. Ibn Abbas said: Ibn Umar said: In her behind, so Ibn Umar erred, and may Allah forgive him; the hadith was only upon this. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd al-Aziz b. Yahya, from Muhammad b. Salamah likewise."
"4776","Another, 120 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn b. Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim b. Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated; Yahya b. Adam narrated; Sharik narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas: raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he forbade eating every fanged beast of prey, and killing children, and selling spoils. He said: And I think he said: And pregnant women, that they be approached."
"4777","121 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman b. Ahmad informed us; Muhammad b. Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated; Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr narrated; Yazid b. Harun narrated; Sharik informed us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the flesh of domestic donkeys, and pregnant women, that they be approached until they deliver what is in their wombs, and eating every fanged beast of prey, and selling spoils until divided, and killing children."
"4778","122 - With it Sulayman b. Ahmad informed us; al-Hasan b. Ali al-Ma'mari narrated; Mus'ab b. Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated; al-Mughirah b. Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith b. Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'ah al-Makhzumi narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah b. Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with them both - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar pregnant women, saying: You water the crop of another. And selling spoils before they are divided, and eating the flesh of domestic donkeys, and every fanged beast of prey."
"4779","123 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan b. Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present -; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad b. Abd Allah informed us; Ahmad b. Bundar, known as al-Sha''ar, informed us; Ahmad b. Amr b. Abi Asim narrated; Abu Bakr narrated; Yahya b. Adam narrated, from Sharik, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas: raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade selling spoils until divided."
"4780","124 - With it Ahmad b. Amr narrated; Ibn Numayr narrated; Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated; Shayban narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like."
"4781","125 - Abu al-Fath Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi al-Asbahani informed us - in writing - that Abd al-Rahman b. Hamad b. al-Hasan al-Duni informed them - recited to him -; Ahmad b. al-Husayn b. al-Kassar informed us; Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ishaq b. al-Sunni informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad b. Shu'ayb b. Ali al-Nasa'i narrated; Ahmad b. Hafs b. Abd Allah narrated; my father told me; Ibrahim told me, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Amr b. Shu'ayb, from Abd Allah b. Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling spoils until divided, and pregnant women, that they be approached until they deliver what is in their wombs, and every fanged beast of prey. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it. As for the forbidding of every fanged beast of prey: Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from the narration of Maymun b. Mihran from Ibn Abbas."
"4782","Another, 126 - Abu al-Majd Zahir b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi - at Isfahan - informed us that Abd al-Mun'im b. Ahmad b. Ya'qub b. Ahmad and Sa'id b. Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad b. Mahmud b. Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Muqri' informed us; Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Salim narrated - at Bayt al-Maqdis -; Hisham b. Ammar narrated; al-Walid b. Muslim narrated; Ibn Jurayj and Rawh b. Janah Abu Sa'd narrated, from Mujahid, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A single faqih is harder upon Satan than a thousand worshippers. Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham b. Ammar, and did not mention Ibn Jurayj. We only reported it for the mention of Ibn Jurayj, for Rawh is spoken about."
"4783","Another, 127 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated; Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated; Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated; Sufyan b. Husayn narrated, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Two verses of Surat al-Ma'idah were abrogated: the verse of the sacrificial animals and necklaces, and the other verse: {So judge between them or turn away from them}. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was therein given a choice: if he wished he judged between them, and if he wished he turned them back to the judgment of another, until there came down: {So judge between them by what Allah revealed}."
"4784","128 - Abu Bakr b. Muhammad al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad b. Raja' b. Ibrahim informed them; Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad b. Musa b. Mardawayh informed us; Ahmad b. Uthman b. Yahya narrated; al-Abbas b. Muhammad al-Duri narrated; Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated; Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated, from Sufyan b. Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Two verses were abrogated of this surah - meaning al-Ma'idah - the verse of the necklaces and His saying: {So judge between them or turn away from them}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a choice: if he wished he judged between them, and if he wished he turned away from them and turned them back to their judgments. Then there came down: {And judge between them by what Allah revealed, and do not follow their desires}. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was commanded to judge between them by what is in our Book."
"4785","129 - With it Ahmad b. Mardawayh informed us; Abu Amr Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ibrahim narrated; Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated; Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. al-Rabi' narrated; Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated, from Sufyan b. Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Two verses of this surah were abrogated: the verse of the necklaces and His saying: {And if they come to you, judge between them}. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Hilal b. al-Ala' b. Hilal, from his father, from Abbad."
"4786","130 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: Muhammad - meaning Ibn Ishaq - narrated: Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: Men shaved on the day of al-Hudaybiyah and others shortened, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: And those who shorten. They said: Why did you single out those who shave for mercy, O Messenger of Allah? He said: They did not doubt. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed."
"4787","131 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated. Al-Tabarani said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated: Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: from Ibn Abi Najih: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten. On the third time he said: And those who shorten."
"4788","132 - Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi and others informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: from Ibn Abi Najih: from Mujahid. 133 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Hudaybiyah: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And those who shorten. They said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you single out those who shave for mercy? He said: They did not doubt. The wording is that of Zuhayr ibn Harb, and the wording of Ibn Mani is similar. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah."
"4789","Another: 134 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak and Abu Ahmad Abdullah informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from al-Amash: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while in Makkah toward Bayt al-Maqdis with the Kabah before him, and after he emigrated to Madinah for sixteen months. Then he was turned toward the Kabah."
"4790","135 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from al-Amash: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while in Makkah toward Bayt al-Maqdis with the Kabah before him, and after he emigrated for sixteen months. Then he was turned toward the Kabah."
"4791","136 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, in Isbahan: Zahir ibn Zahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Nasr ibn Abi al-Husayn al-Haramayni and others informed us, they said: Abu al-Husayn al-Khaffaf informed us: Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us: Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from al-Amash: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Makkah toward Bayt al-Maqdis with the Kabah before him, and after he emigrated to Madinah for sixteen months, then he was turned toward the Kabah. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ibn Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib."
"4792","Another: 137 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Musa ibn Harun and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated, they said: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated: from Ibrahim ibn Abi Jamrah: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam: in it is food for nourishment and cure for sickness. And the worst water on the face of the earth is water in the valley of Barahut in Hadramawt, like the legs of locusts of vermin; in the morning it gushes forth and in the evening it has no moisture. Muhammad ibn Muhajir, I think he is al-Ansari."
"4793","Another: 138 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated: from Rabah ibn Abi Maruf al-Makki: from Qays ibn Sad: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will enter Paradise, and no household or chamber in Paradise will remain but they will say: Welcome, welcome to us. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, what hardship has this man borne on that day? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, and you are he, O Abu Bakr. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Walid ibn Bayan from Ahmad."
"4794","Another: 139 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated: from Ibn Abi Najih: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fight a people until he called them."
"4795","Another: 140 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated, they said: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated: from Ibn Abi Najih: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever flees from two has fled, and whoever flees from three has not fled. It was narrated in Sahih al-Bukhari from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, who said: There was revealed: If there are twenty steadfast among you they will overcome two hundred. That was hard upon the Muslims when it was made obligatory that one not flee from ten, then came the alleviation, and He said: Now Allah has lightened for you, up to His saying: they will overcome two hundred. He said: When Allah lightened their number He reduced patience by what He lightened from them. And what we mentioned is not the wording of what he mentioned."
"4796","Another: 141 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Mamari - he is al-Hasan ibn Ali - narrated: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated: my father narrated: Abu Said ibn Awdh al-Makki narrated: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sleeping before Isha and talking after it. Abu Said ibn Awdh was narrated from by Abu Nuaym al-Fadl and Marwan ibn Muawiyah and Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil, and he was not named. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Barzah al-Aslami."
"4797","Another: 142 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated: Said ibn Sulayman narrated: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated: from Sufyan ibn Husayn: from al-Hakam: from Miqsam and Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a day before al-Tarwiyah: Our lodging tomorrow, God willing, will be at Khayf al-Ayman where the idolaters swore."
"4798","Another: 143 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Muadhdhin informed us, in Isbahan: Umm al-Baha Fatimah bint al-Imam Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Baghdadi informed them, recited to her, it was said to her: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed you: Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn Yaqub ibn Fannaki informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated: Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated: Yahya ibn Adam narrated: from Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Ayyash - from al-Amash: from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: that he was asked: From what were things created? He said: From fire, light, darkness, water and wind. Then he was asked: From what were these things created? He said: Then he recited: And He subjected for you whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth, all from Him."
"4799","Another: 144 - Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi informed us, in Cairo: Hibah Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaylan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafii informed us: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun al-Harbi narrated: Abu Hudhayfah narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Mansur: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: Allusion is to say: I want to marry. Three times."
"4800","145 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Junayd al-Sufi informed us, in his book: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr informed us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated: from Mansur: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas about: There is no blame upon you for what you allude of engagement to women. He said: He alludes, saying: I want to marry."
